2025-11-03 10:02:50 [kimi-k2-0905] The globe-with-meridians emoji (🌏) is simply the Unicode scalar value `U+1F30F`.
2025-11-03 10:02:50 [kimi-k2-0905] In code you only need the literal or its numeric escape.
2025-11-03 10:02:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:02:50 [kimi-k2-0905] JavaScript
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] const globe = '🌏';          // literal
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] console.log(globe);          // 🌏
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] If you ever need the numeric form:
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] const globe = '\u{1F30F}';   // ES6 escape
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:02:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:06:56 [kimi-k2-0905] Got it—thanks for the heads-up.
