2025-11-03 10:15:22 [nitro@ryzen5] what is the range for exit
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] In POSIX / Unix-like systems the exit status is an 8-bit unsigned value passed to `exit()`
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] (or returned from `main`).
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] Only the low 8 bits are kept for the parent process, so the effective range is
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] 	0 – 255
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] where 0 conventionally means success and 1-255 indicate various error conditions.
2025-11-03 10:15:28 [kimi-k2-0905] 
