2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] The bot’s config lives in two places:
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Discord side – the channel it listens to is set at runtime by the first `!ping` message it
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] receives (`openChannel` is updated to that channel’s ID).
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]    If you want to hard-wire a default channel, put the numeric ID in the source:
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]    const openChannel = "1410693060672753704";   // <— your channel ID
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Fountain side – the sloppy-bot appears as a normal “account” in `accounts.json`.
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]    Add an entry so Fountain can route traffic to it:
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]    "discord": {
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]      "api": "Sloppy",
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]      "env": "DISCORD_BOT",
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]      "emoji": "🦜",
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]      "platform": "https://discord.com/channels/…"
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]    }
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905]    The `DISCORD_BOT` environment variable must contain the bot token.
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] Restart both services after any change; the bot will print `[SLOPPY] discordClient online` when the
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] token is accepted.
2025-11-03 12:57:58 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] Discord desktop itself has no “bot editor”; you manage the bot in the Developer Portal, not
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] inside the app.
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Open a browser → https://discord.com/developers/applications
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Click the application (bot) you created for sloppy.
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Tabs you care about:
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Bot – copy the token (this is what `DISCORD_BOT` env var must contain).
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905]    - OAuth2 → URL Generator – if you ever need to re-invite it (tick “bot” and “Send
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] Messages” at minimum).
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905]    - General Information – grab the Application ID if you need to construct the invite link
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] again.
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] Inside the desktop client you only do two things:
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] - Right-click the target channel → “Copy Channel ID” (enable Developer Mode in User Settings →
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] Advanced first).
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] - Paste that ID into the code (`openChannel` constant) if you want to hard-code it instead of
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] letting `!ping` set it dynamically.
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] That’s all; everything else is edited in the source or environment variables.
2025-11-03 12:59:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-03 13:01:11 [kimi-k2-0905] Icon changes in the Developer Portal are usually instant, but the desktop client caches
2025-11-03 13:01:11 [kimi-k2-0905] aggressively.
2025-11-03 13:01:11 [kimi-k2-0905] Force-quit Discord (tray icon → Quit) and restart it; the new icon should appear within a few
2025-11-03 13:01:11 [kimi-k2-0905] seconds.
2025-11-03 13:01:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
