2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] The crash shows `js8="0x%5B%5D=androxgh0st"` being passed in. The problem is that this isn't valid
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] JSON at all - it looks like URL-encoded form data that somehow got routed to your JSON-RPC parser.
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] 
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] The assertion failure is:
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] 
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] std::__cxx11::basic_string<wchar_t>::operator[]: Assertion '__pos <= size()' failed
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] 
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] 
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] This means `pos` exceeded the string length, but your bounds check `if(pos>=js.length())` should
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] have caught this. The issue might be that you're checking `js.length()` but the conversion from
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] UTF-8 to wide string (`convert32.from_bytes(js8)`) could be failing or producing a different length
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] than expected.
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] 
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] • The actual fix needed:*
2025-11-04 07:32:58 [claude-sonnet-4] 1. Validate that `js8` contains valid JSON before attempting UTF-32 conversion
