2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] ✅ 7. Add a Fail2ban Rule
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] • Problem:*
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] You’re handling bad behavior in-app, but log-based bans are easier to audit.
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] • Fix:*
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] Log a single line per bad path:
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] INTRUDER a00:b73c:: +CSCOL+
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] Then add a fail2ban filter:
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] [fit3-intruder]
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] failregex = ^INTRUDER <HOST> .*$
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] And jail:
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] [fit3]
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] enabled = true
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] filter = fit3-intruder
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] logpath = /var/log/fit3.log
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] maxretry = 3
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] bantime = 1h
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 10:11:21 [kimi-k2-0905] 
