2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] Yes! .NET's `UrlDecode` has a few other important differences your C++ version should
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] match:
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 🔍 .NET UrlDecode Behavior
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 1. Character Set Handling:
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]    .NET uses UTF-8 by default for `%XX` sequences, not raw bytes
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 2. Error Handling:
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]    Invalid `%` sequences (like `%G1`, `%`, `%1`) are passed through literally
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 3. Case Insensitivity:
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]    `%2E` and `%2e` both decode to `.` (hex is case-insensitive)
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 🛠️ C++ Updates to Match .NET
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] std::string url_decode(std::string_view encoded) {
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]     std::ostringstream decoded;
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]     for(size_t i = 0; i < encoded.length(); ++i) {
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]         if(encoded[i] == '%' && i + 2 < encoded.length()) {
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             // Case-insensitive hex parsing (like .NET)
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             std::string hex_str = std::string(encoded.substr(i + 1, 2));
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             std::transform(hex_str.begin(), hex_str.end(), hex_str.begin(), ::tolower);
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             // Validate hex digits (like .NET's error handling)
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             if(std::all_of(hex_str.begin(), hex_str.end(), ::isxdigit)) {
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]                 std::istringstream hex_stream(hex_str);
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]                 int hex_value;
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]                 if(hex_stream >> std::hex >> hex_value) {
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]                     decoded << static_cast<char>(hex_value);
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]                     i += 2;
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]                     continue;
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]                 }
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             }
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             // If invalid % sequence, pass through literally (like .NET)
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]         }
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]         // .NET-compatible: + becomes space
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]         if(encoded[i] == '+') {
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             decoded << ' ';
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]             continue;
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]         }
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]         decoded << encoded[i];
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]     }
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat]     return decoded.str();
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] }
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] 🎯 What This Fixes
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] - `%2Eetc%2Fpasswd` → `../etc/passwd` (case-insensitive hex)
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] - `%G1bad` → `%G1bad` (invalid % sequences preserved)
2025-11-04 10:50:25 [deepseek-chat] - `hello%20world` → `hello world` (proper space handling)
