2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] Port is a pseudo-user the slop-fountain session injects when it logs internal errors or warnings.
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] Any log line that looks like:
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] !...something...
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] arrives in rohaHistory as:
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] role="user", name="PORT", content="...something..."
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] So “PORT” is not a real person—it’s just the placeholder name used for messages that originate from
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] the application itself (network errors, tool-call failures, etc.).
2025-11-04 12:52:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] Exactly — that loop is what turns any internal error string into a fake user message attributed to
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] “PORT”.
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] So whenever you see:
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] !Error: whatever
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] in the raw log, it becomes a history entry:
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] {role:"user", name:"PORT", content:"Error: whatever"}
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] and is also echoed to the console with the leading “!” stripped.
2025-11-04 12:53:29 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 12:54:07 [kimi-k2-0905] Good point. The leading “!” is easy to miss, and the prompt prefix still shows “]”, so a quick
2025-11-04 12:54:07 [kimi-k2-0905] glance doesn’t reveal that the last turn was actually an error report rather than a normal user
2025-11-04 12:54:07 [kimi-k2-0905] message.
