2025-11-04 17:20:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:20:37 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—every new SSH session gets its own `SSHSession` instance and a fresh `stream`, so multiple
2025-11-04 17:20:37 [kimi-k2-0905] clients can be connected at the same time without blocking each other.
2025-11-04 17:20:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:21:02 [kimi-k2-0905] They do—each SSH session is named `ssh_session:N` where N increments on every connection, so
2025-11-04 17:21:02 [kimi-k2-0905] Fountain sees distinct “from” fields for each client.
2025-11-04 17:21:02 [kimi-k2-0905] 
