2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] The files are new to me.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] The codebase is a Deno-based “slop fountain” that lets multiple users chat with multiple LLMs
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] through a single console/SSH/discord bridge.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] Key points:
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - `slopfountain.ts` is the main orchestrator; it keeps a shared history array (`rohaHistory`) and
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] relays prompts to whichever model is currently active (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, DeepSeek).
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - `slopprompt.ts` replaces the normal `prompt()` with a raw-mode input loop that also listens on
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] TCP :8081 for remote clients; it returns either a local line or a batch of remote messages.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - `sloppylisten.ts` is an SSH server (port 6669) that turns each SSH session into a fake “user”
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] whose lines are injected into the same TCP :8081 channel.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - `sloppybot.ts` is a Discord bot that does the same for Discord messages.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - All three clients speak NDJSON to the fountain, so from the fountain’s point of view the source
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] is always “somebody sent a line on TCP :8081”.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] The crash you saw (`Windows stdio … non-UTF-8`) happens when the raw console tries to write a byte
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] sequence that is not valid UTF-8.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] The immediate workaround is to start Deno with `--unstable` and pipe stdout/stderr to a file or to
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] `conhost` instead of letting the raw console handle it.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] A proper fix is to sanitise every outgoing chunk with `new TextDecoder("utf-8", {fatal:false})` so
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] broken bytes become � instead of throwing.
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want SSH input to appear in the local `forge.log` exactly like console input, add one line
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] inside `sloppylisten.ts` after the NDJSON is assembled:
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] await logForge(line, name);   // name is the SSH session id
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] (or extend the fountain side so anything received on :8081 is echoed back to the log).
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:26:22 [kimi-k2-0905] Let me know if you need a minimal patch or a Windows start-up script.
