2025-11-04 17:43:20 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Fountain already logs everything that arrives on the TCP port to `forge.log` via `logForge`, so
2025-11-04 17:43:20 [kimi-k2-0905] after the line above you get the prompt in both places:
2025-11-04 17:43:20 [kimi-k2-0905] - Windows console: `[REMOTE] {"messages":[{"message":"hello","from":"skid"}]}`
2025-11-04 17:43:20 [kimi-k2-0905] - forge.log: `e845c1c [ssh_session:7] {"messages":[{"message":"hello","from":"skid"}]}`
2025-11-04 17:43:20 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-04 17:43:20 [kimi-k2-0905] No code change needed inside Fountain; the existing `logForge` path catches the NDJSON you just
2025-11-04 17:43:20 [kimi-k2-0905] echoed.
