2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] Summary after reading the shared tree:
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. No auth gate on Discord → anyone in the channel can drive the bot and therefore the Fountain
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] shell.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905]    If that channel is public, random users can run any `/command`, including `/share`, `/push`,
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] `/reset`, or indirectly trigger file-system writes via tool calls.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Path leakage still exists:
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905]    - `slopfountain.ts` prints absolute Windows paths (`C:\nitrologic\…`) in `/history`, `/share`,
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] and error echoes.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Those lines go straight into `forge.log` and are echoed back to Discord without scrubbing.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Command injection surface:
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Discord input is forwarded as-is to `callCommand`; no whitelist for Discord-side users.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Tool-call results from the model are re-parsed and can contain back-tick fenced code blocks
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] that Discord will render—no sanitisation before broadcast.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. File-system limits are only size-based (`MaxFileSize`); no per-user quota or chroot.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. No audit trail that ties Discord message → executed command → side effects; only a shared
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] `forge.log` timestamped in 1/16 s hex.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] Quick hardening you can add right now:
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] - In `sloppybot.ts` drop any line that starts with `/` unless the author ID is in a hard-coded
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] allow-list.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] - In `slopfountain.ts` run every outgoing echo through a cheap redactor:
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905]   const safe = line.replace(/[A-Z]:[\/\\][^\s]+/gi, "<local-path>");
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] - Disable dangerous commands from remote users (`/share`, `/push`, `/reset`, `/cd`, `/dir`) unless
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] a `--unsafe` flag is supplied at start-up.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] Beyond that the code is solid; those three changes close the obvious public-channel holes.
2025-11-05 08:26:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
