2025-11-06 07:53:29 [scudmarks@discord] how does zero width joiners affect discord fixed with rendering?
2025-11-06 07:53:30 [qwen3-coder-plus] Zero Width Joiners don't affect fixed-width rendering - they're invisible. Discord processes them
2025-11-06 07:53:30 [qwen3-coder-plus] for emoji sequences but they don't impact monospace alignment. Use them only for combining emoji
2025-11-06 07:53:30 [qwen3-coder-plus] sequences, not for spacing.
2025-11-06 07:53:30 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-11-06 07:53:42 [scudmarks@discord] are you sure?
2025-11-06 07:53:44 [qwen3-coder-plus] You're right to question - ZWJ can affect rendering. In monospace:
2025-11-06 07:53:44 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-11-06 07:53:44 [qwen3-coder-plus] - ZWJ (U+200D) joins emoji sequences but may shift alignment
2025-11-06 07:53:44 [qwen3-coder-plus] - Some emoji sequences consume different cell widths
2025-11-06 07:53:44 [qwen3-coder-plus] - Combining marks can break fixed-width assumptions
2025-11-06 07:53:44 [qwen3-coder-plus] 
2025-11-06 07:53:44 [qwen3-coder-plus] Test this:
