2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] The files are new to me.
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] The crash on Windows is caused by sloppylisten (or another sloppy* helper) sending raw non-UTF-8
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] bytes to Fountain’s stdin.
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Short-term fix: in every sloppy utility that `writeFountain(…)`, force the payload to valid UTF-8
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] before the write, e.g.
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] await writeFountain(new TextDecoder("utf-8", { fatal: false }).decode(payload));
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Long-term: teach Fountain to accept binary frames instead of assuming every line is UTF-8 text.
2025-11-08 09:12:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
