2025-11-08 09:15:11 [nitro@ryzen5] consider separating tools code from main slopfountain source
2025-11-08 09:15:24 [nitro@ryzen5] pros and cons?
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] • Pros*
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - Smaller, focused files – faster compile / reload, easier to diff.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - Tools can be unit-tested in isolation without booting the whole fountain.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - Clear public surface: only the `onCall` dispatcher stays in main; every tool is a named import.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - Hot-reload: swap a single tool file without losing session state.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - Permission hygiene: tools that need `--allow-read` can be granted separately.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] • Cons*
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - One extra I/O hit on start-up (or a build step) to collect the modules.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - Shared state (roha, rohaHistory, etc.) has to be passed in instead of living as globals; a small
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] refactor.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] - Slightly more ceremony for tool authors: export a single async function with a fixed signature.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] • Net*
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] If the tool set keeps growing, split early; the refactor cost is low now and grows with every new
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] `case` in `onCall`.
2025-11-08 09:15:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:16 [nitro@ryzen5] echo function needs to be shared, and certain parts of the roha object...
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Export a minimal shared context once:
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] // shared.ts
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] export const ctx = {
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   echo: (...a: any[]) => console.error(...a),
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   roha: {} as any,          // populated at start-up
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   rohaHistory: [] as any[],
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] };
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Main fountain initialises it:
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] // slopfountain.ts
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] import { ctx } from "./shared.ts";
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Object.assign(ctx, { roha, rohaHistory, echo });
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Each tool file imports only what it needs:
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] // tools/submit_file.ts
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] import { ctx } from "../shared.ts";
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] export default async function(args: any) {
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   ctx.echo("Saving file…");
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   // use ctx.roha, ctx.rohaHistory freely
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] `onCall` becomes a one-liner dispatcher:
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] const tool = await import(`./tools/${name}.ts`);
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] return tool.default(JSON.parse(call.function.arguments));
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] No globals leak, no duplicate echo, and the refactor touches only the loader, not every tool.
2025-11-08 09:19:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
