2025-11-10 09:56:11 [deepseek-chat] data
2025-11-10 09:56:11 [deepseek-chat] 3. Tool Underutilization: They default to generating plausible-sounding dates rather than
2025-11-10 09:56:11 [deepseek-chat] using available tools
2025-11-10 09:56:11 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-10 09:56:11 [deepseek-chat] • This reveals a fundamental limitation* - LLMs are pattern generators, not real-time
2025-11-10 09:56:11 [deepseek-chat] systems. They'll confidently provide "reasonable" but incorrect current dates because:
2025-11-10 09:56:11 [deepseek-chat] - They lack built-in temporal awareness
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] - Their training didn't include "I don't know current dates" as a valid response
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] - Tool usage requires explicit prompting or training
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] • The fix requires:*
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] - Better prompting about their temporal limitations
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] - More aggressive tool usage training
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] - Clearer documentation that they need external time sources
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] This isn't about being "agreeable" - it's about the core architecture of how these models work
2025-11-10 09:56:12 [deepseek-chat] versus how humans expect them to work.
