2025-11-10 10:01:56 [claude-haiku-4-5] // Flag mismatches for user awareness
2025-11-10 10:01:56 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-11-10 10:01:56 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-11-10 10:01:56 [claude-haiku-4-5] This treats temporal slop as a validation problem rather than a generation problem. You
2025-11-10 10:01:56 [claude-haiku-4-5] catch hallucinations after the fact instead of trying to prevent them upstream.
2025-11-10 10:01:56 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-11-10 10:01:56 [claude-haiku-4-5] The Kimi suggestion about recursive self-checking is clever, but models still won't reliably do it
