2025-11-10 10:07:33 [kimi-k2-0905] mistakes; the linter catches the rest.
2025-11-10 10:07:33 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-10 10:07:33 [kimi-k2-0905] So: yes, add the static line, but treat it as a fast-cache that expires quickly, not as
2025-11-10 10:07:33 [kimi-k2-0905] authoritative data.
2025-11-10 10:07:33 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-10 10:08:19 [scudmarks@discord] doesn't slopfountain generate systemprompt for each prompt in realtime?
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes - slopfountain rebuilds the system block on every turn, so you can time-stamp it for free:
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] // in the payload builder
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] const now = new Date();
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] const liveStamp = `Live stamp: ${now.toISOString()}`;
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] const systemBlock = [
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   ...rohaGuide,
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   liveStamp,          // ← injected fresh each call
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905]   "Use read_time if exact data is required."
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] ];
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Because the system array is re-created inside `prepareGeminiPrompt` / `anthropicSystem` etc., the
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] string is always < 1 s old when the request leaves the relay.
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] No restart, no stale cache, no extra linter pass—just a constantly refreshed hint that costs one
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] line of tokens.
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] (If you want sub-second accuracy you still call the tool, but this removes the “obviously wrong
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] date” class of slop without touching the post-generation pipeline.)
2025-11-10 10:08:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
