2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] function and pushes the result to history, then `relay()` recursively calls itself (`await
2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] relay(depth+1)`) without muting the tool flag or removing the original user prompt. The next
2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] recursive request still contains the same user message plus the latest tool result, so the model
2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] (still in tool-call mode) can ask for `readtime` again, triggering another recursion.
2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] 
2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] 3. There’s no guard to stop calling tools on each nested relay depth, so if the model doesn’t emit
2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] a final text reply after each result (or keeps re-requesting the tool), you get a chain of repeated
2025-11-14 09:51:32 [gpt-5.1-codex-mini] `read_time` calls—75 in your log.
