2025-11-15 20:17:14 [nitro@ryzen5] minio is running on my pi, how do i setup accounts?
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] Use the MinIO client (`mc`) on any machine that can reach the Pi.
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Install mc (one-time):
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] wget https://dl.min.io/client/mc/release/linux-arm/mc   # or linux-amd64 if not on the Pi
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] chmod +x mc
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo mv mc /usr/local/bin
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Point mc at the Pi (alias can be anything; change user/key to taste):
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] mc alias set pi http://<pi-ip>:9000 minioadmin minioadmin   # default root creds
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Create a new user and a policy that gives that user its own bucket:
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] # policy file (put-users-own-bucket.json)
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] cat >put-users-own-bucket.json <<'EOF'
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 	"Version": "2012-10-17",
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 	"Statement": [
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 		{
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 			"Effect": "Allow",
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 			"Action": ["s3:GetBucketLocation", "s3:ListBucket"],
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 			"Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::${aws:username}"]
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 		},
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 		{
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 			"Effect": "Allow",
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 			"Action": ["s3:PutObject", "s3:GetObject", "s3:DeleteObject"],
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 			"Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::${aws:username}/*"]
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 		}
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 	]
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] EOF
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] mc admin policy create pi put-users-own-bucket put-users-own-bucket.json
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] mc admin user add pi alice mySecretKey
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] mc admin policy attach pi put-users-own-bucket --user alice
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Make the user’s bucket (optional; the policy above expects a bucket named `alice`):
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] mc mb pi/alice
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] That’s it—alice can now connect with any S3 client using:
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] - endpoint: `http://<pi-ip>:9000`
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] - access key: `alice`
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] - secret key: `mySecretKey`
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] Repeat steps 3-4 for additional accounts.
2025-11-15 20:19:54 [kimi-k2-0905] 
