2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Drop caches to free RAM:
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905]    echo 3 | sudo tee /proc/sys/vm/drop_caches
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Lightweight file-count from now on:
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905]    # one-time snapshot (no tree walk)
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905]    sudo df -i /grid5 | awk 'NR==2{print $3}'
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905]    (gives used inodes ≈ file count on ext4)
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. If you still need live updates, enable `inotifywait` counters instead of ever running `find`
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] again.
2025-11-15 21:07:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:40:53 [nitro@ryzen5] config v8 for pi5 build
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] For a Pi 5 build you can use the same “config-v8.txt” that ships with current 64-bit Raspberry Pi
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] OS – it already contains the dt-blob and overlays needed for BCM2712 / Pi 5.
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] Nothing extra is required unless you are enabling additional hardware; in that case just append the
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] usual dtoverlay= lines at the bottom.
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] Example minimal /boot/firmware/config.txt (v8, Pi 5):
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] # enable 64-bit kernel
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] arm_64bit=1
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] kernel=kernel_2712.img
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] # Pi 5 firmware defaults
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] dtoverlay=dwc2,dr_mode=host
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] otg_mode=1
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] pciex1_gen=3
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] camera_auto_detect=1
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] display_auto_detect=1
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] # over-clocking head-room (optional)
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] arm_freq=3000
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] over_voltage=5
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] gpu_freq=1000
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] # your extras go here
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] # dtoverlay=your_addon
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] Place the file in /boot/firmware (or /boot on older images), reboot, done.
2025-11-16 15:41:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:29:48 [nitro@ryzen5] is this ok for .bashrc?
2025-11-17 09:29:48 [nitro@ryzen5] https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git
2025-11-17 09:29:52 [nitro@ryzen5] oops
2025-11-17 09:29:59 [nitro@ryzen5] PATH="$HOME/depot_tools:$PATH"
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] It’s fine, just drop the “.git” from the URL when you clone:
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] git clone https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools "$HOME/depot_tools"
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] and keep the PATH line exactly as you have it.
2025-11-17 09:30:06 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:27 [nitro@ryzen5] test call?
2025-11-17 09:30:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:31 [kimi-k2-0905] which gn
2025-11-17 09:30:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:31 [kimi-k2-0905] If depot_tools is on PATH you’ll get something like
2025-11-17 09:30:31 [kimi-k2-0905] `/home/you/depot_tools/gn`
2025-11-17 09:30:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:30:46 [nitro@ryzen5] pass
2025-11-17 09:31:13 [nitro@ryzen5] am fetching v8
2025-11-17 09:31:16 [kimi-k2-0905] Good—carry on. If `fetch v8` stalls or throws a network error, just interrupt and re-run; the tool
2025-11-17 09:31:16 [kimi-k2-0905] resumes cleanly.
2025-11-17 09:31:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:32:04 [nitro@ryzen5] [ec2-user@ip-172-31-8-229 v8]$ fetch v8Running: gclient rootWARNING: Your metrics.cfg file was invalid or nonexistent. A new one will be created.Running: gclient config --spec 'solutions = [  {    "name": "v8",    "url": "https://chromium.googlesource.com/v8/v8.git",    "deps_file": "DEPS",    "managed": False,    "custom_deps": {},  },]'
2025-11-17 09:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] That’s normal first-run chatter—gclient is creating its config and will start syncing the full
2025-11-17 09:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] tree. Let it finish; the “WARNING” about metrics.cfg is harmless.
2025-11-17 09:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:32:47 [nitro@ryzen5] i should add some swap
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—EC2 micro instances run out of RAM fast. Add 2-4 GB:
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo fallocate -l 4G /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo chmod 600 /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo mkswap /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo swapon /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] Make it persistent:
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] echo '/swapfile none swap sw 0 0' | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] Then re-run `fetch v8`.
2025-11-17 09:33:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:44 [nitro@ryzen5] 8G to be safe?
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 4 GB is usually enough for the fetch itself; 8 GB won’t hurt if you have the disk space and want
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] head-room for the later build. Either way, the commands stay the same—just change the `fallocate`
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] size:
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo fallocate -l 8G /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] Then continue with `chmod`, `mkswap`, `swapon`, and the fstab line as before.
2025-11-17 09:33:52 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:34:02 [nitro@ryzen5] this is for building it dummy
2025-11-17 09:34:11 [kimi-k2-0905] Got it—8 G swap is fine. Commands stay identical, just swap the size:
2025-11-17 09:34:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:34:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:34:11 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo fallocate -l 8G /swapfile && sudo chmod 600 /swapfile && sudo mkswap /swapfile && sudo swapon /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:34:11 [kimi-k2-0905] echo '/swapfile none swap sw 0 0' | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab
2025-11-17 09:34:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:34:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:35:07 [nitro@ryzen5] what is needed for building chromium on m5 large
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] m5.large (2 vCPU, 8 GB) is tight but doable; give it 8–16 GB swap and expect 6–8 h builds.
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Essentials
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo dnf install -y git python3 perl gcc-c++ glibc-devel bison flex pkgconf-pkg-config \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      alsa-lib-devel atk-devel bzip2-devel cairo-devel cups-devel dbus-devel \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      expat-devel fontconfig-devel freetype-devel gdk-pixbuf2-devel glib2-devel \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      gtk3-devel harfbuzz-devel java-17-openjdk-devel libatomic libcap-devel \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      libdrm-devel libffi-devel libgcrypt-devel libjpeg-turbo-devel libpng-devel \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      libsecret-devel libvpx-devel libxkbcommon-x11-devel libxshmfence-devel \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      mesa-libEGL-devel mesa-libgbm-devel nss-devel pango-devel pciutils-devel \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      pulseaudio-libs-devel systemd-devel util-linux-devel valgrind-devel \
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905]      wget which xz zlib-devel
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Optional but recommended
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo dnf install -y ccache lld-devel llvm-devel ninja-build
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Bootstrap depot_tools (once)
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] git clone https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/tools/depot_tools.git $HOME/depot_tools
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] echo 'export PATH="$HOME/depot_tools:$PATH"' >> ~/.bashrc
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] source ~/.bashrc
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Create 16 GB swap (disk is cheap)
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo fallocate -l 16G /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo chmod 600 /swapfile && sudo mkswap /swapfile && sudo swapon /swapfile
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] echo '/swapfile none swap sw 0 0' | sudo tee -a /etc/fstab
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Fetch & build
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] mkdir ~/chromium && cd $_
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] fetch --nohooks chromium   # 20–30 GB download
2025-11-17 09:36:23 [kimi-k2-0905] cd src
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] ./build/install-build-deps.sh   # accepts all prompts
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] gclient runhooks
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] gn gen out/Release --args='is_debug=false is_component_build=true dcheck_always_on=false'
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] autoninja -C out/Release chrome
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] Tips
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] - Use `iscomponentbuild=true` to cut link RAM.
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] - Add `uselld=true usegold=false` if lld is installed.
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] - Keep ccache dir on instance storage: `ccache --max-size=20G`.
2025-11-17 09:36:24 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:38:21 [nitro@ryzen5] i want to build c++ programs that link with v8 for scripting duties
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] For “I just want V8 as a scripting engine” you don’t need the full Chromium tree—build only the
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] standalone static/dynamic libraries that the V8 project already publishes.
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Install the same depot_tools and swap you already have.
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Fetch the minimal V8 tree (no Chromium):
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] mkdir ~/v8 && cd ~/v8
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] fetch v8              # ~2 GB instead of 30 GB
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] cd v8
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Install the helper packages that V8’s build needs:
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] ./build/install-build-deps.sh   # accepts all prompts
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Pick a release configuration and generate Ninja files:
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] gn gen out.gn/x64.release --args='
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     is_component_build = false   # static libs
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     is_debug = false
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8_use_external_startup_data = false
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8_enable_i18n_support = false
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     treat_warnings_as_errors = false'
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] (Flip `iscomponentbuild = true` if you prefer shared libraries.)
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. Build the libraries you actually link against:
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] autoninja -C out.gn/x64.release v8_monolith
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] # produces:
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] #   out.gn/x64.release/obj/libv8_monolith.a   (static everything)
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] #   out.gn/x64/release/icudtl.dat             (if you kept i18n)
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 6. Write a minimal host program (hello.cpp):
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <v8.h>
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <libplatform/libplatform.h>
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <iostream>
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] int main() {
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::V8::InitializeICUDefaultLocation("");
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::V8::InitializeExternalStartupData("");
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     std::unique_ptr<v8::Platform> platform = v8::platform::NewDefaultPlatform();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::V8::InitializePlatform(platform.get());
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::V8::Initialize();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::Isolate::CreateParams params;
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     params.array_buffer_allocator =
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::ArrayBuffer::Allocator::NewDefaultAllocator();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::Isolate* isolate = v8::Isolate::New(params);
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     {
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::Isolate::Scope isolate_scope(isolate);
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::HandleScope handle_scope(isolate);
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::Local<v8::Context> context = v8::Context::New(isolate);
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::Context::Scope context_scope(context);
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::Local<v8::String> src =
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]             v8::String::NewFromUtf8(isolate, "'Hello '+ 'V8!'").ToLocalChecked();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::Local<v8::Script> script =
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]             v8::Script::Compile(context, src).ToLocalChecked();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::Local<v8::Value> result = script->Run(context).ToLocalChecked();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         v8::String::Utf8Value utf8(isolate, result);
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]         std::cout << *utf8 << '\n';
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     }
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     isolate->Dispose();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::V8::Dispose();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     v8::V8::ShutdownPlatform();
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     delete params.array_buffer_allocator;
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     return 0;
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 7. Compile against the monolith:
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905] g++ -std=c++17 hello.cpp \
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     -I$HOME/v8/v8/include \
2025-11-17 09:41:47 [kimi-k2-0905]     -I$HOME/v8/v8 \
