2025-11-17 10:06:55 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo journalctl _COMM=bash
2025-11-17 10:06:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 10:06:55 [kimi-k2-0905] # 4. audit subsystem (only if auditd was running)
2025-11-17 10:06:55 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo aureport --tty
2025-11-17 10:06:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 10:06:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 10:06:55 [kimi-k2-0905] If none of those exist, the commands are simply gone—bash never writes them anywhere else.
