2025-11-17 13:43:12 [nitro@ryzen5] canit see a config string?
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] There’s no single “config string” API, but you can dump the exact GN build flags that produced the
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] library.
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] Cheapest way at run-time: embed the file yourself.
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. While building, ask GN to write the args file into the object directory:
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] gn args out.gn/arm64.release --list >out.gn/arm64.release/gn_args.txt
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. In your program:
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <fstream>
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <sstream>
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] std::string readBuildArgs()
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905]     std::ifstream f("gn_args.txt");   // or full path to out.gn/.../gn_args.txt
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905]     std::ostringstream buf;
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905]     buf << f.rdbuf();
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905]     return buf.str();
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] /* inside main after V8 version print */
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] std::cout << "Build args:\n" << readBuildArgs() << '\n';
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] That gives you the verbatim `--args` list (or any subset you choose to embed) so you can log the
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] exact configuration the binary was produced with.
2025-11-17 13:43:25 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:00 [nitro@ryzen5] can you list the basic api for v8::V*
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] Core “V8::V*” (global, not per-isolate) routines you’ll actually call:
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] // Lifecycle
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::Initialize()
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::Dispose()
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::InitializePlatform(Platform*)
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::ShutdownPlatform()
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::GetVersion()                      // const char*
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] // Build-time feature queries
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::IsPointerCompressionEnabled()
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::IsSandboxedPointers()
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::Is32BitSMIEnabled()
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] // Process-wide options (set before Initialize)
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::SetFlagsFromString(const char*, size_t)
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::SetFlagsFromCommandLine(int* argc, char** argv, bool remove_flags)
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] // ICU / snapshot (no-ops when disabled at build time)
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::InitializeICUDefaultLocation(const char* exec_path)
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::InitializeExternalStartupData(const char* exec_path)
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] // Sampling profiler, etc.
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] V8::InitializeProfiler()
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] Everything else (context, script compile/run, values, etc.) lives on isolates, contexts, or local
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] handles—those are the only true global entry points.
2025-11-17 13:44:16 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:44:42 [nitro@ryzen5] so the context api?
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] The context API is small—everything you need to create, enter, exit, and optionally set security or
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] embedder data:
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] // Creation / lifetime
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] static Local<Context> Context::New(
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905]         Isolate* isolate,
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905]         ExtensionConfiguration* extensions = nullptr,
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905]         MaybeLocal<ObjectTemplate> global_template = MaybeLocal<ObjectTemplate>(),
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905]         MaybeLocal<Value> global_object = MaybeLocal<Value>(),
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905]         size_t context_snapshot_index = 0,
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905]         DeserializeInternalFieldsCallback embedder_fields_deserializer = DeserializeInternalFieldsCallback(),
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905]         MicrotaskQueue* microtask_queue = nullptr);
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] void Context::Enter();
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] void Context::Exit();
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] void Context::DetachGlobal();
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] Local<Object> Context::Global();
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] // Embedder slot (one pointer per context)
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] void* Context::GetAlignedPointerFromEmbedderData(int index);
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] void  Context::SetAlignedPointerInEmbedderData(int index, void* data);
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] // Security tokens
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] void Context::SetSecurityToken(Local<Value> token);
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] Local<Value> Context::GetSecurityToken();
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] // microtask policy helpers
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] MicrotaskQueue* Context::GetMicrotaskQueue();
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] // convenience isolate back-pointer
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] Isolate* Context::GetIsolate();
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] That’s the whole public surface; everything else (running scripts, adding globals, etc.) you do
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] through the returned `Local<Context>` and the usual `Local<Object>`, `Local<String>`,
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] `Script::Compile`, etc.
2025-11-17 13:45:01 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:20 [nitro@ryzen5] and the isloate api
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Key public Isolate-level methods (no templates, just names):
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Lifetime / core
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `static Isolate* New(const CreateParams&)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void Dispose()`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void Enter()`, `void Exit()`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void GetData(uint32t slot)`, `void SetData(uint32t slot, void)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Heap / GC
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void RequestGarbageCollectionForTesting(GCType)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void LowMemoryNotification()`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `size_t GetNumberOfDataSlots()`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Exceptions
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void ThrowException(Local<Value>)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `Local<Value> GetException()` (inside catch block)
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Locks / tasks
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `bool IsLocked()`, `Locker` ctor needs it
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void RunMicrotasks()`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `MicrotasksPolicy GetMicrotasksPolicy()`, `SetMicrotasksPolicy(...)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Codegen / JIT flags
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void SetJitCodeEventHandler(JitCodeEventOptions, JitCodeEventHandler)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void SetAllowCodeGenerationFromStringsCallback(AllowCodeGenerationFromStringsCallback)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Sampling / profiling
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void SetEventLogger(EventLogger)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] - `void AddGCPrologueCallback(GCCallback)`, `AddGCEpilogueCallback(...)`
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] And the three nested scope classes:
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] `Isolate::Scope`, `HandleScope`, `EscapableHandleScope`.
2025-11-17 13:45:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:47:27 [nitro@ryzen5] how would basic token test work
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <v8.h>
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <libplatform/libplatform.h>
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <iostream>
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] int main()
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 	v8::V8::InitializePlatform(v8::platform::NewDefaultPlatform().get());
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 	v8::V8::Initialize();
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 	v8::Isolate::CreateParams params;
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 	params.array_buffer_allocator = v8::ArrayBuffer::Allocator::NewDefaultAllocator();
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 	v8::Isolate* iso = v8::Isolate::New(params);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 	{
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		v8::Isolate::Scope isos(iso);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		v8::HandleScope hs(iso);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		/*---- create two contexts ----*/
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		v8::Local<v8::Context> ctxA = v8::Context::New(iso);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		v8::Local<v8::Context> ctxB = v8::Context::New(iso);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		/*---- give them different security tokens ----*/
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		ctxA->SetSecurityToken(v8::String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "tokenA"));
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		ctxB->SetSecurityToken(v8::String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "tokenB"));
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		/*---- enter A and try to access B’s global ----*/
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		ctxA->Enter();
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		{
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 			v8::Context::Scope cs(ctxA);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 			v8::TryCatch tc(iso);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 			v8::Local<v8::Value> result;
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 			bool ok = v8::Script::Compile(ctxA,
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 				v8::String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso,
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 					"try { b_global } catch(e) { e.toString() }"))
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 				.ToLocalChecked()
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 				->Run(ctxA)
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 				.ToLocal(&result);
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 			if (ok)
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 				std::cout << "cross-context read: "
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 				<< *v8::String::Utf8Value(iso, result) << '\n';
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		}
2025-11-17 13:48:00 [kimi-k2-0905] 		ctxA->Exit();
