2025-11-17 14:03:36 [nitro@ryzen5] basic standardio buffer firsts
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] Here’s a zero-dependency, blocking-only “stdio buffer” module that gives Node-compatible
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] `process.stdin|stdout|stderr` streams so you can test piping and small scripts before tackling
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] sockets.
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] C++ side (one file, no threads, no libuv)
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <v8.h>
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <libplatform/libplatform.h>
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <iostream>
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] #include <vector>
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] using namespace v8;
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] static std::vector<char> g_inBuf;          // reusable read buffer
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] void StdinRead(const FunctionCallbackInfo<Value>& args)
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Isolate* iso = args.GetIsolate();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	HandleScope hs(iso);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	g_inBuf.resize(65536);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::cin.read(g_inBuf.data(), g_inBuf.size());
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::streamsize n = std::cin.gcount();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Local<ArrayBuffer> ab = ArrayBuffer::New(iso, n);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	memcpy(ab->Data(), g_inBuf.data(), n);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	args.GetReturnValue().Set(Uint8Array::New(ab, 0, n));
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] void StdoutWrite(const FunctionCallbackInfo<Value>& args)
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	if (!args[0]->IsUint8Array()) return;
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Isolate* iso = args.GetIsolate();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Local<Uint8Array> ui = args[0].As<Uint8Array>();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	ArrayBuffer::Contents cont = ui->Buffer()->GetBackingStore();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::cout.write(static_cast<char*>(cont.Data()) + ui->ByteOffset(),
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	                ui->ByteLength());
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::cout.flush();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] void StderrWrite(const FunctionCallbackInfo<Value>& args)
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	if (!args[0]->IsUint8Array()) return;
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Isolate* iso = args.GetIsolate();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Local<Uint8Array> ui = args[0].As<Uint8Array>();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	ArrayBuffer::Contents cont = ui->Buffer()->GetBackingStore();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::cerr.write(static_cast<char*>(cont.Data()) + ui->ByteOffset(),
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	                ui->ByteLength());
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	std::cerr.flush();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] void CreateProcessObject(Local<Context> ctx)
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] {
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Isolate* iso = ctx->GetIsolate();
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Local<Object> process = Object::New(iso);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Local<Object> stdin  = Object::New(iso);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Local<Object> stdout = Object::New(iso);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	Local<Object> stderr = Object::New(iso);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	stdin ->Set(ctx, String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "read"),
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	            Function::New(ctx, StdinRead).ToLocalChecked());
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	stdout->Set(ctx, String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "write"),
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	            Function::New(ctx, StdoutWrite).ToLocalChecked());
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	stderr->Set(ctx, String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "write"),
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	            Function::New(ctx, StderrWrite).ToLocalChecked());
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	process->Set(ctx, String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "stdin"),  stdin);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	process->Set(ctx, String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "stdout"), stdout);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	process->Set(ctx, String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "stderr"), stderr);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 	ctx->Global()->Set(ctx, String::NewFromUtf8Literal(iso, "process"), process);
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] Usage from JS (same as Node)
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] const chunk = process.stdin.read();   // Uint8Array
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] process.stdout.write(chunk);          // echo
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] process.stderr.write(Buffer.from("oops\n"));
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] Compile & link exactly like the earlier hello-world sample; now you have synchronous
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] stdin/stdout/stderr “streams” without any extra event loop.
2025-11-17 14:04:14 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:48 [nitro@ryzen5] wo dont even need console.???
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] Correct—`console` is just a thin JS wrapper around `process.stdout.write`, `process.stderr.write`,
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] and `util.format`.
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] If you expose those three streams yourself you can recreate `console.log/warn/error` in
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] half-a-dozen lines of JS:
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] globalThis.console = {
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905]   log: (...a) => process.stdout.write(Buffer.from(a.join(' ') + '\n')),
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905]   warn: (...a) => process.stderr.write(Buffer.from(a.join(' ') + '\n')),
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905]   error: (...a) => process.stderr.write(Buffer.from(a.join(' ') + '\n'))
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] };
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] No extra native code required; `console` is optional sugar.
2025-11-17 14:04:56 [kimi-k2-0905] 
