2025-11-17 14:37:31 [nitro@ryzen5] in v8
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] V8 is Google’s high-performance JavaScript and WebAssembly engine, written in C++.
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] It compiles JS to native machine code, handles garbage collection, and provides the runtime for
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Chrome, Node.js, Deno, Edge, etc.
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Key points:
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] - Ignition: interpreter that produces bytecode quickly
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] - TurboFan: optimizing compiler that re-compiles hot functions to native code
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] - Sparkplug: fast baseline compiler (Ignition → Sparkplug → TurboFan pipeline)
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] - Orinoco: parallel, concurrent, incremental GC (young & old generations)
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] - Pointer compression & sandboxing (recent security work)
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] - ECMAScript feature development happens here first; Node ships whatever V8 ships
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] If you have a specific V8 question (embedding, tracing, JIT internals, API usage, etc.) let me know
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] and I’ll dive straight into the details.
2025-11-17 14:37:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
