2025-11-18 07:55:05 [nitro@ryzen5] it seems to be functioning well, can discord bots do direct messages?
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] Yes, Discord bots can send direct messages (DMs) to users, but with some caveats:
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] - Requirements: The bot must share a mutual server (guild) with the user, and the user must
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] have DMs enabled or have interacted with the bot recently.
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] - How to Implement: Use `user.send(message)` or create a DM channel with `await
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] user.createDM()`. For example, in your messageCreate handler:
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1]   const dmChannel = await message.author.createDM();
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1]   await dmChannel.send('Hello!');
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] - Limitations: Bots can't DM users who block them or haven't consented. Avoid spamming, as
2025-11-18 07:55:09 [grok-code-fast-1] it can lead to bans.
