2025-11-18 08:56:07 [nitro@ryzen5] what is raspberry pi pico toolchain, bare 32 or 64 bit arm?
2025-11-18 08:56:13 [kimi-k2-0905] The official Raspberry Pi Pico toolchain targets the RP2040 which contains dual Arm
2025-11-18 08:56:13 [kimi-k2-0905] Cortex-M0+ cores – these are 32-bit only, so the toolchain is bare-metal 32-bit ARM
2025-11-18 08:56:13 [kimi-k2-0905] (ARMv6-M).
2025-11-18 08:56:13 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 08:56:40 [nitro@ryzen5] can i build v8 with depot tools for such a target?
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] No.
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] V8’s build system (gn + ninja) only supports:
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] - 32-bit Arm with VFP (ARMv7-A and newer)
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] - 64-bit Arm (AArch64)
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] Cortex-M0+ is ARMv6-M, no VFP, no MMU, 264 kB on-chip RAM.
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] Even if you hack the toolchain, V8’s baseline interpreter alone is >600 kB and needs an OS for
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] memory mapping and signals. It will not link, let alone run.
2025-11-18 08:56:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 08:57:35 [nitro@ryzen5] i am interested in hosting it given these constraints
2025-11-18 08:57:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Host it elsewhere.
2025-11-18 08:57:44 [kimi-k2-0905] Run a minimal 64-bit Arm (or x86-64) board as the V8 engine and let the Pico talk to it over
2025-11-18 08:57:44 [kimi-k2-0905] UART/SPI/I²C.
2025-11-18 08:57:44 [kimi-k2-0905] The Pico stays a 32-bit bare-metal device; V8 never lives on it.
2025-11-18 08:57:44 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 08:58:20 [nitro@ryzen5] is there more suitable js engine for embedded?
2025-11-18 08:58:36 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—use an engine written for MCUs, not phones.
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] Engine               Flash   RAM   32-bit bare-metal   Notes
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] QuickJS              ~200 k  64 k  yes                  Full ES2020, no JIT, MIT
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] Duktape              ~150 k  56 k  yes                  ES5.1, refcount, MIT
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] MuJS                 ~100 k  32 k  yes                  ES5.1, C89, ISC
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] JerryScript          ~100 k  32 k  yes                  ES5.1, CMake, Apache-2
2025-11-18 08:58:37 [kimi-k2-0905] Espruino             ~120 k  8 k   yes                  ES5.1, MIT, Pico SDK built-in
