2025-11-18 09:02:45 [nitro@ryzen5] which ones are ARM64 and x86_64
2025-11-18 09:02:52 [kimi-k2-0905] None in that table—every engine listed is C/C++ and interpreter-only, so they build
2025-11-18 09:02:52 [kimi-k2-0905] and run on any 32- or 64-bit target (ARM64, x86-64, RISC-V, …) with nothing more than a
2025-11-18 09:02:52 [kimi-k2-0905] compiler switch.
