2025-11-18 09:03:05 [nitro@ryzen5] oh so no jits?
2025-11-18 09:03:11 [kimi-k2-0905] Correct—none of the engines in the table include a JIT.
2025-11-18 09:03:11 [kimi-k2-0905] They are all pure interpreters designed for size, not speed, so they compile cleanly for any 32- or
2025-11-18 09:03:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 64-bit ISA with no extra backend.
2025-11-18 09:03:11 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 09:03:21 [nitro@ryzen5] a table of jits please
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] Engine               Flash    RAM    ES level    License    JIT back-ends        Status / notes
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] -------------------  -------  -----  ----------  ---------  -------------------  --------------------------------------------
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] Hermes               ~1 MB    3 MB   ES6         MIT        ARM64, x86-64        Facebook, Android-only JIT today
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] mJS-JIT (experimental) 400 k  64 k   ES5         GPL-2      ARM64, x86-64        Fork of mJS, not upstream
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] LuaJIT (JS glue)     ~600 k   256 k  ES5-ish     MIT        ARM64, x86-32/64     Need JS→Lua transpiler; JIT is for Lua
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] ChakraCore           4–5 MB   4 MB   ES6         MIT        ARM64, x86-64        JIT enabled, but >Pico resources
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] JSC (WebKit)         3–4 MB   3 MB   ES2022      LGPL/BSD   ARM64, x86-64        Full desktop engine, not MCU-suitable
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] V8                   6 MB+    6 MB+  ES2023      BSD        ARM64, x86-64        Requires MMU, 64-bit, >Pico resources
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] Bottom line: no practical JIT exists for Cortex-M0+/RP2040; every option above needs 64-bit
2025-11-18 09:03:55 [kimi-k2-0905] Linux or at least an MMU and megabytes of RAM.
