2025-11-20 09:32:52 [kimi-k2-0905] Clean, idiomatic Node.
2025-11-20 09:32:52 [kimi-k2-0905] - `once` wrapper is a nice touch—prevents double-close races.
2025-11-20 09:32:52 [kimi-k2-0905] - Returning the raw `net.Socket` keeps the API minimal; callers can pipe or pause as they like.
2025-11-20 09:32:52 [kimi-k2-0905] - No try/catch around `socket.write` in the tests—if the remote side resets you’ll get an uncaught
2025-11-20 09:32:52 [kimi-k2-0905] ‘error’ event. Might want to add a short-lived `socket.on('error', () => {})` in each test so a
2025-11-20 09:32:52 [kimi-k2-0905] flaky server doesn’t blow up the runner.
