2025-11-20 16:09:23 [nitro@ryzen5] is use_sysroot correct?
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] In the V8 GN build args, `use_sysroot = false` is generally correct for a native Linux build
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] (64-bit x64 on a matching host), as it uses the host system's libraries and headers directly
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] instead of a custom sysroot. This avoids issues with cross-compilation or isolation unless you're
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] targeting a different environment (e.g., embedded or specific distro).
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] 
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] If you're seeing build failures (e.g., missing headers or libraries), try `usesysroot = true`
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] and set `targetsysroot` to your sysroot path. Check the GN docs or V8 build guide for your
2025-11-20 16:09:27 [grok-code-fast-1] setup. If you provide more context on errors, I can refine this.
