2025-11-25 08:45:54 [scudmarks@discord] humanoids and quadrupeds, any other terms I can use?
2025-11-25 08:46:03 [kimi-k2-0905] Common synonyms you can drop in without sounding forced:
2025-11-25 08:46:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 08:46:03 [kimi-k2-0905] - Humanoids → bipeds, androids, legged robots, anthropomorphic bots
2025-11-25 08:46:03 [kimi-k2-0905] - Quadrupeds → four-leg robots, dog-bots, legged rovers, mammal-type bots
2025-11-25 08:46:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 08:46:03 [kimi-k2-0905] If you need to group both, “legged robots” or “limbed systems” covers the set.
2025-11-25 08:46:03 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 08:46:49 [scudmarks@discord] in nature what are 4 legged mammals known as?
2025-11-25 08:46:50 [kimi-k2-0905] Quadrupeds — literally “four feet.”
2025-11-25 08:46:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 08:47:15 [scudmarks@discord] in art?
2025-11-25 08:47:19 [kimi-k2-0905] Art shorthand: “quadrupeds” still works, but you’ll also see “four-legged beasts” or simply
2025-11-25 08:47:19 [kimi-k2-0905] “animals” when the pose is obvious.
2025-11-25 08:47:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 08:47:40 [scudmarks@discord] humanoid and animoid?
2025-11-25 08:47:48 [kimi-k2-0905] “Animoid” isn’t standard English; if you need a concise counterpart to “humanoid” for animal-shaped
2025-11-25 08:47:48 [kimi-k2-0905] machines, “zoomorph” or “quadruped robot” keeps things clear.
2025-11-25 08:47:48 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 08:47:57 [scudmarks@discord] zoomorph?
2025-11-25 08:48:02 [kimi-k2-0905] “Zoomorph” = something shaped like an animal (Greek zōon “animal” + morphē “form”).
2025-11-25 08:48:02 [kimi-k2-0905] In robotics it’s the straight antonym of “humanoid”: humanoid = human-shaped, zoomorph =
2025-11-25 08:48:02 [kimi-k2-0905] animal-shaped.
2025-11-25 08:48:02 [kimi-k2-0905] 
