2025-11-25 11:58:59 [kimi-k2-0905] The client is sending a key that starts with `wiki.` (and the server will create it if it
2025-11-25 11:58:59 [kimi-k2-0905] doesn’t exist), but the server-side code you posted never reads any key that begins with
2025-11-25 11:58:59 [kimi-k2-0905] `wiki.`.
2025-11-25 11:58:59 [kimi-k2-0905] So the banner key is simply stored in Redis; nothing in this C++ codebase ever touches it again.
2025-11-25 11:58:59 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:19 [nitro@ryzen5] how does redis.run work pls
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] `redis.run` is just another RPC method the server exposes.
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] The call chain is:
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. HTTP POST `/api` with JSON-RPC body
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905]    `{ "method":"redis.run", "params":"SET wiki.banner …" }`
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. `http.h → onRequest()` extracts the body and passes it to
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905]    `parseRPC(header, body)`
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. `headless.h → InvokeRPC()` sees method == `"redis.run"` and does:
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905]    `stereo->redisrun(command, result, true)`
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. `redis.h → Redis::redisrun()` wraps the literal command string and calls:
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905]    `RedisContext::run(command, result, quoted=true)`
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. `RedisContext::run()` forwards the text to hiredis:
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905]    `redisCommand(context, command.c_str())`
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905]    (or `redisCommandArgv` if the line contains quotes)
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 6. The reply is formatted back to JSON and returned in the HTTP response.
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] No inspection or rewriting of the command is done; whatever the client puts after `"redis.run"` is
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] sent straight to Redis.
2025-11-25 11:59:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
