2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] The `(no command)` message typically appears when Deno executes a task defined in
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] `deno.json` that contains a trailing semicolon, an empty instruction, or a trailing operator (like
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] `&&` with nothing after it).
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] It means Deno finished the main part (`sloppyredis`) but found an empty statement at the end of the
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] `test` task definition.
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] How to fix it
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] Check your `deno.json` file.
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] • Likely current state (note the trailing semicolon):*
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] {
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]   "tasks": {
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]     "sloppyredis": "deno run --allow-net sloppyredis.ts",
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]     "test": "deno task sloppyredis;"
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]   }
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] • The Fix (remove the semicolon):*
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] {
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]   "tasks": {
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]     "sloppyredis": "deno run --allow-net sloppyredis.ts",
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]     "test": "deno task sloppyredis"
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro]   }
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] Can you add a return?
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, if you want to be explicit or force a clean exit to "shut it up" without changing the
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] structure too much, you can add `exit 0` (which acts like a return 0):
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] "test": "deno task sloppyredis && exit 0"
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-25 12:12:24 [gemini-3-pro] 
