2025-11-25 13:31:54 [nitro@ryzen5] div section needs a tint background
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] Add a semi-transparent background to the div and drop it behind the content:
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] .section-tint {
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	position: relative;          /* containing block for the pseudo-element */
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .45);   /* black 45 % tint */
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	color: #fff;                 /* light text so it stays readable */
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] If you only want the tint to cover an image or video that sits inside the section, use a
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] pseudo-element instead:
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] .section-tint::before {
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	content: "";
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	position: absolute;
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	inset: 0;                    /* top:0 right:0 bottom:0 left:0 */
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	background: rgba(0, 0, 0, .45);
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	z-index: 1;                  /* keep tint below section text */
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	pointer-events: none;        /* let clicks pass through */
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] .section-tint > * {
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	position: relative;
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 	z-index: 2;                  /* raise content above tint */
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] Adjust the RGBA alpha value (last number) to make the tint darker or lighter.
2025-11-25 13:32:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
