2025-11-27 06:33:41 [nitro@ryzen5] options for deno nginx stack to authenticate user once across zones
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Deno itself has no built-in single-sign-on (SSO) primitives; you have to bolt it on.
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] With NGINX in front you can do the “authenticate once” part at the edge and let every Deno zone
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] trust the same header that NGINX injects.
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Pick one auth method
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905]    - OpenID-Connect (Keycloak, Authelia, Auth0, Ory Hydra …)
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905]    - SAML (simpleSAMLphp, Shibboleth)
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Basic auth + htpasswd (quick demo only)
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Put an auth daemon in front of NGINX
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905]    lua-resty-openidc (Lua) or nginx-auth-jwt (Go) are the lightest; they validate the cookie / JWT
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] and set `X-User: alice`.
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. NGINX snippet (works in `http` or `server` block):
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] # ——— shared resolver for OIDC ———
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] resolver 8.8.8.8 8.8.4.4 valid=10s;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] # ——— external auth endpoint ———
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] location = /oauth2/auth {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	internal;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	proxy_pass              http://auth_daemon:4180;   # oauth2-proxy, Authelia, …
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	proxy_pass_request_body off;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	proxy_set_header        Content-Length "";
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	proxy_set_header        X-Original-URI $request_uri;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	proxy_set_header        X-Original-Method $request_method;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] # ——— protected zone A ———
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] server {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	listen 80;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	server_name a.demo.local;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	location / {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		auth_request        /oauth2/auth;          # 1. check cookie
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		auth_request_set    $auth_user $upstream_http_x_user;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		proxy_set_header    X-User  $auth_user;    # 2. inject header
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		proxy_pass          http://deno_zone_a:8080;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] # ——— protected zone B ———
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] server {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	listen 80;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	server_name b.demo.local;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	location / {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		auth_request        /oauth2/auth;          # same endpoint
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		auth_request_set    $auth_user $upstream_http_x_user;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		proxy_set_header    X-User  $auth_user;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		proxy_pass          http://deno_zone_b:8081;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	}
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. Deno side – reusable helper (`auth.ts`):
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] import { serve } from "https://deno.land/std@0.208.0/http/server.ts";
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] export function mustAuth(req: Request): string {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	const user = req.headers.get("x-user");
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	if (!user) throw new Error("Unauthorized");
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	return user;
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] export function handler(user: string): Response {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	return new Response(`hello ${user} from Deno\n`);
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] if (import.meta.main) {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	serve((req) => {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		try {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 			const user = mustAuth(req);
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 			return handler(user);
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		} catch {
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 			return new Response("Unauthorized", { status: 401 });
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 		}
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 	});
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. Cookie domain
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Set the cookie domain to `.demo.local` so it is sent to `a.demo.local`, `b.demo.local`, etc.
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Most OIDC proxies do this with `--cookie-domain=.demo.local`.
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 6. HTTPS
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Terminate TLS at NGINX (certbot/Let’s Encrypt) so the cookie is `Secure`.
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] Result: user logs in once on any zone; NGINX re-uses the same session for every Deno backend.
2025-11-27 06:34:30 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:44:46 [nitro@ryzen5] am using redis for local stores
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] If Redis is already part of the stack you can let the auth daemon (oauth2-proxy, Authelia,
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] lua-resty-openidc, etc.) store its session there instead of using the default SQLite / in-memory
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] store.
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] That gives you:
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] - single sign-on across every NGINX zone
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] - shared logout / revocation
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] - zero changes to the Deno apps—they still just read the `X-User` header
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:45:42 [kimi-k2-0905] Minimal nginx + oauth2-proxy + Redis snippet:
