2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 4. systemd units
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] `/etc/systemd/system/authelia.service`
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] [Unit]
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] Description=Authelia OpenID provider
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] After=network.target redis.service
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] [Service]
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] Type=simple
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] User=authelia
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] Group=authelia
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] WorkingDirectory=/opt/authelia
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] ExecStart=/opt/authelia/authelia --config /etc/authelia/configuration.yml
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] Restart=on-failure
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] AmbientCapabilities=CAP_NET_BIND_SERVICE
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] [Install]
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] WantedBy=multi-user.target
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] Create user, enable/start:
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo useradd -r -M -s /bin/false authelia
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo mkdir -p /var/lib/authelia
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo chown authelia:authelia /var/lib/authelia
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo systemctl daemon-reload
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo systemctl enable --now authelia
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 5. NGINX (same snippet as before, just change `proxy_pass`)
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905] location = /oauth2/auth {
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905]     internal;
2025-11-27 06:49:50 [kimi-k2-0905]     proxy_pass              http://127.0.0.1:9091/api/verify;
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905]     proxy_pass_request_body off;
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905]     proxy_set_header        Content-Length "";
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905]     proxy_set_header        X-Original-URI $request_uri;
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905]     proxy_set_header        X-Original-Method $request_method;
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 6. Done – single sign-on across all zones, sessions in Redis, no containers.
2025-11-27 06:49:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:51:26 [nitro@ryzen5] does authelia just need to be on one instance or all of the,?
2025-11-27 06:51:32 [kimi-k2-0905] One Authelia instance is enough.
2025-11-27 06:51:32 [kimi-k2-0905] Point every NGINX `auth_request` to that single address (`127.0.0.1:9091` or
2025-11-27 06:51:32 [kimi-k2-0905] `authelia.internal:9091`) and every zone shares the same session store (Redis) and the same login
2025-11-27 06:51:32 [kimi-k2-0905] screen.
2025-11-27 06:51:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:51:49 [nitro@ryzen5] simpler way to install on pi5
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] Pi5 (arm64) – use the distro repo and a one-liner build.
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] # 1. deps
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y redis-server build-essential git golang-go nodejs npm
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] # 2. grab pre-built arm64 binary (official)
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo mkdir -p /opt/authelia && cd /opt/authelia
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] wget https://github.com/authelia/authelia/releases/download/v4.38.8/authelia-linux-arm64.tar.gz
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] tar xf authelia-linux-arm64.tar.gz
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] chmod +x authelia
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] # 3. user + folders
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo useradd -r -M -s /bin/false authelia
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo mkdir -p /etc/authelia /var/lib/authelia
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo chown authelia:authelia /var/lib/authelia
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] # 4. drop the same two files (configuration.yml & users.yml) into /etc/authelia
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] # 5. systemd unit exactly as above
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] # 6. enable services
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] sudo systemctl enable --now redis authelia
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] No Docker, no Go build on the Pi – just download, unpack, start.
2025-11-27 06:52:09 [kimi-k2-0905] 
