2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding your question: `bomb` is better.
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] It is the standard 4-letter code for the genus Bombus (Bumblebees). `boml` would typically
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] imply a specific species (like Bombus lucorum), but since you already have `bter` and
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] `bimp` for specific bees, `bomb` serves as the best catch-all for the genus.
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the next 3 distinct groups:
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Trichoptera (Caddisflies) - Vital for aquatic ecosystems.
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Megaloptera (Dobsonflies & Alderflies) - Famous for "Hellgrammites".
2025-11-27 11:13:45 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Zygentoma (Silverfish) - The primitive household insects (formerly Thysanura).
