2025-11-27 11:17:44 [nitro@ryzen5] no more suggestions please, just review and brief comments
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding `bomb` vs `boml`:
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] `bomb` is the better choice here. It clearly represents the genus Bombus (Bumblebees).
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] `boml` is restrictive as it implies a specific species (e.g., Bombus lapidarius or
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] Bombus lucorum), whereas `bomb` covers the whole group.
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] • Review of `version 1.3.2`*:
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Completeness: The addition of Strepsiptera, Mecoptera,
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] Raphidioptera, and Archaeognatha successfully rounds out the remaining minor insect
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] orders.
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Taxonomy: Keeping Isoptera (Termites) separate from Blattodea is practical for
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] this type of listing, even if phylogenetically they are often combined.
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Codes: The update to `dapl` (Monarch butterfly) brings it in line with standard
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 4-letter coding conventions.
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Syntax: Valid JSON with correct tab indentation.
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] The catalogue now appears to have full ordinal coverage for Insecta.
2025-11-27 11:18:08 [gemini-3-pro] 
