2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] Here is a review of the specific code values in version 1.3.2, focusing on 4-letter consistency and
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] potential typos:
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Blattodea: `bloat` (5 letters).
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Likely Blatta orientalis.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Issue: 5 letters and reads like an English word.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Suggestion: `blor` is the standard 4-letter code.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Lepidoptera: `actlu` (5 letters).
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Likely Actias luna (Luna moth).
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Issue: 5 letters.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Suggestion: `alun` fits the pattern better.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Isoptera: `rypt`.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Likely Cryptotermes.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Issue: appears to be a typo missing the leading 'c'.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Suggestion: `cryp`.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Archaeognatha: `dilta` (5 letters).
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Genus Dilta.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Issue: 5 letters.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Suggestion: `dilt`.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  Diptera: `trich` (5 letters).
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Issue: Ambiguous (could imply Order Trichoptera) and is 5 letters.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro]        Suggestion: If Trichoplusia*, use `trni`. If generic, `tric`.
2025-11-27 11:19:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
