2025-11-28 12:19:20 [nitro@ryzen5] LUMA2 - capture 2bit monochrome video such as C64 luma pin Pico 4 input pins CSYNC G0 G1 G2Fed by 2 x LM319 featuring 4 fast voltage comparatorsCSYNC based on fixed threshold, 2 gray and 1 white detector adjustable with trimmers.Simon to add Pico PIO code in which 4 GPIO digital inputs format output of 320 wide 240 high 50 hz 2 bit monochrome stream.
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] Here is a minimal PIO program that packs the four GPIO lines (CSYNC, G0, G1, G2) into one 2-bit
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] pixel every 8 µs (≈ 12.5 MHz) and streams the result to the CPU.
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] It is written for RP2040 SDK 2.x and assumes the four signals are on consecutive GPIOs starting at
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] BASE_PIN (change the define to suit your wiring).
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] pico_luma.pio
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] ; 2-bit LUMA capture – 320 px / line, 240 lines / 50 Hz
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] ; one state machine samples 4 pins every 8 µs and packs two pixels per 32-bit word
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] ; word format:  [pixel1:2][pixel0:2] … packed little-endian
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] .program luma_capture
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] .side_set 1 opt
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] public start:
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     set x, 15            side 0      ; 16 pixels = 8 words per loop
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] pixel_loop:
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     in pins, 4           side 0      ; sample CSYNC,G2,G1,G0 into ISR
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     in null, 28                      ; pad to 32 bits (we only care about low 4)
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp x--, pixel_loop side 0
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     push                 side 0      ; 32-bit word now in RX FIFO
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     set x, 15            side 0
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp start            side 0
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] % c-sdk {
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] static inline void luma_capture_program_init(PIO pio, uint sm, uint offset, uint base_pin) {
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     pio_sm_config c = luma_capture_program_get_default_config(offset);
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     sm_config_set_in_pins(&c, base_pin);       // 4 consecutive pins
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     sm_config_set_in_shift(&c, false, true, 32); // shift left, autopush every 32 bits
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     sm_config_set_fifo_join(&c, PIO_FIFO_JOIN_RX); // one big RX FIFO
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset, &c);
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]     pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] %}
