2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] Notes
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] - Sampling rate is set by the PIO clock divider (default = 1 → 125 MHz).
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]   To hit exactly 12.5 MHz pixel clock (8 µs per pixel) set divider to 10:
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]   `smconfigset_clkdiv(&c, 10);`
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] - Each 32-bit word contains two 2-bit pixels:
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905]   `pixel0 = word & 3`, `pixel1 = (word >> 2) & 3`.
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] - CSYNC bit is captured but not used by the PIO; the ARM core can inspect it to detect line/field
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] sync if required.
2025-11-28 12:20:32 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:21:29 [nitro@ryzen5] no thanks, the first step is to establish sync, then sampling data is captured
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] Got it—sync first, data later.
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] Below is a minimal PIO program whose only job is to watch the CSYNC pin and tell the CPU
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] exactly when the 50 Hz frame starts (VSYNC) and when each of the 240 active lines starts (HSYNC).
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] No pixel data is touched until these time-stamps are rock-solid.
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] piolumasync.pio
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] ; CSYNC sync detector – 50 Hz 625-line PAL C64 style
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] ; GPIN0 = CSYNC (active-low sync pulses)
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] ; GPIN1 = optional /BLANK (high during active video), tie low if unused
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] ; side-set pin flashes an LED so you can see it lock with a scope
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] .program luma_sync
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] .side_set 1
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] public start:
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     wait 0 pin 0           side 0     ; sit on back porch
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     wait 1 pin 0           side 0     ; end of sync = rising edge
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp check_long                      ; was it VSYNC?
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] check_long:                            ; measure low time to spot VSYNC
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     set x, 31              side 0
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     mov y, x               side 0
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] measure:
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp pin, got_high      side 0     ; high yet?
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp x--, measure       side 0
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp lost_sync          side 0     ; line too long – noise
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] got_high:
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp !x, is_vsync       side 0     ; x rolled → long low = VSYNC
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] is_hsync:                              ; short sync = normal line
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     irq set 0              side 1     ; fire HSYNC irq
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp start              side 0
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] is_vsync:                              ; long sync = VSYNC
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     irq set 1              side 1     ; fire VSYNC irq
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] lost_sync:
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     jmp start              side 0
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] % c-sdk {
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] static inline void luma_sync_program_init(PIO pio, uint sm, uint offset,
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]                                           uint csync_pin, uint blank_pin) {
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     pio_sm_config c = luma_sync_program_get_default_config(offset);
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     sm_config_set_in_pins(&c, csync_pin);        // GPIN0 = CSYNC
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     sm_config_set_jmp_pin(&c, csync_pin);        // jmp pin reads CSYNC
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     sm_config_set_in_shift(&c, false, false, 0); // no shifting
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     pio_sm_init(pio, sm, offset, &c);
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905]     pio_sm_set_enabled(pio, sm, true);
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] }
2025-11-28 12:22:38 [kimi-k2-0905] %}
