2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] Trimmer Selection
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] The search results you listed are for Trimmer Capacitors (measured in pF), which are used
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] for radio frequency tuning. You require Trimmer Potentiometers (Variable Resistors).
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] For a cost-effective solution, search for "RM065 10k" or "PT10 10k". These are
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] standard carbon film horizontal preset potentiometers and are significantly cheaper than the
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] precision multi-turn cermet types (like the 3386P) while being sufficient for video thresholds.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] Wiring Description
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the connection plan based on your BOM. Note that the LM319 is powered by 5V, but the
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] outputs must be pulled up to 3.3V to protect the Pico.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • 1. Analog Input Stage*
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • RCA Jack (Signal): Connect to Line_In.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • RCA Jack (GND): Connect to Common Ground.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Termination: Connect 75 $\Omega$ Resistor between Line_In and Ground.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Coupling: Connect Line_In to Comparator Inputs (Direct DC coupling assumed per
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] your note).
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • 2. Comparator Setup (2x LM319)*
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Power: Connect LM319 VCC pins to 5V. Connect GND pins to Ground.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Decoupling: Place 0.1 $\mu$F capacitors between VCC and GND near each chip.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • 3. Reference Voltage Generation*
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • CSYNC (Fixed): Create a voltage divider (e.g., 1k $\Omega$ and 15k $\Omega$) from 5V to
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] Ground. Connect the junction (~0.3V) to LM319 Input 1 Reference.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Luma Levels (G0, G1, G2): Connect the outer legs of the 3x 10k Trimmers to 5V and Ground.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] Connect the Wiper (center pin) of each to the respective LM319 Input References.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • 4. Signal Comparison & Output*
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Signal Distribution: Connect the buffered/coupled Line_In to the other
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] input pin of all 4 comparators.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Outputs (Open Collector):
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Connect LM319 Output pins to Pico GPIO pins (e.g., GP0, GP1, GP2, GP3).
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro]        Connect a 2.2k $\Omega$ - 4.7k $\Omega$ resistor from each* Output pin to Pico
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 3.3V (3V3_OUT).
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro]        Warning:* Do not pull up to 5V, or you will damage the Pico.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • 5. Logic Table*
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • CSYNC: Trigger when Signal < Fixed Threshold.
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] • Luma: Trigger when Signal > Adjustable Thresholds (G0, G1, G2).
2025-11-28 13:24:03 [gemini-3-pro] 
