2025-11-28 13:47:28 [nitro@ryzen5] > shopping listJaycar10K ohm Piher Horizontal Trimpot $1.65LM319 High Speed Dual Comparator Linear IC $4.50
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding the LM319 replacement:
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] The LM319 comes in a 14-pin package because it isolates the input and output
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] grounds/supplies to achieve its high speed (80ns response time).
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] Finding a Dual High-Speed comparator in DIP-8 with equivalent performance is
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] difficult, especially at hobbyist retailers like Jaycar.
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] • LM393 (DIP-8): This is the standard dual comparator, but it is too slow (~1300ns) for C64
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] video signals.
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] • LM311 (DIP-8): This offers comparable speed (~165ns), but it is a single
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] comparator. You would need four chips instead of two LM319s.
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] • TLC372 (DIP-8): Faster than the LM393 (~200ns) but likely still too slow for crisp video
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] edges compared to the LM319.
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] • Recommendation:*
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] Stick with the LM319. The extra PCB footprint is necessary for the bandwidth required to
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] capture the C64 pixel clock cleanly.
2025-11-28 13:47:54 [gemini-3-pro] 
