2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the reorganized development documentation for the LUMA 2 project.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] LUMA 2 Project Specification
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Purpose:* Capture 2-bit monochrome video (specifically Commodore 64 Luma signal) using a
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] Raspberry Pi Pico.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] System Overview
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Hardware: Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040) + 2x LM319 Dual High-Speed Comparators.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Input Logic: 4 GPIO inputs representing CSYNC, G0 (Gray 1), G1 (Gray 2), and G2 (White).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Software Goal: PIO state machine to format inputs into a 320x240 @ 50Hz 2-bit monochrome
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] stream.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Bandwidth: ~0.96 MB/s (Compatible with USB 1.1 streaming).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Voltage Domain: 5V Analog / 3.3V Digital Logic.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] Bill of Materials (BOM)
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Semiconductors*
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 1x Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 2x LM319 High-Speed Dual Comparators (e.g., Linear IC).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Passive Components*
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 1x Resistor 75 $\Omega$ (Video Termination).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 4x Resistors 2.2k $\Omega$ – 4.7k $\Omega$ (Logic Pull-ups).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 2x Resistors (Fixed value for CSYNC voltage divider).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 3x Trimmer Potentiometers 10k $\Omega$ (Recommended: Piher Horizontal for G0, G1, G2).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 2x Capacitors 0.1 $\mu$F (Decoupling).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 1x Capacitor 100nF – 10$\mu$F (Optional: AC Coupling if DC clamp is implemented).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Connectors*
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 1x RCA Jack (PCB Mount).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] Wiring & Netlist
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 1. Power Distribution*
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • LM319 VCC: Connect to 5V (VBUS).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • LM319 GND/VEE: Connect to Common Ground (Single supply).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Pico: Powered via USB or VSYS; Logic operates at 3.3V.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Decoupling: Place 0.1 $\mu$F capacitors across LM319 VCC/GND pins close to the ICs.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 2. Video Input Stage*
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Signal: RCA Center Pin connected to the Non-Inverting Input (+) of all 4
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] comparator gates.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Ground: RCA Shield connected to Common Ground.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Termination: 75 $\Omega$ resistor between RCA Center Pin and Ground.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 3. Reference Thresholds (Inverting Inputs)*
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • CSYNC Comparator (- Input): Connect to fixed voltage divider (Target: ~0.3V for sub-black
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] sync pulses).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • G0, G1, G2 Comparators (- Inputs): Connect to the wiper of individual 10k Trimmers.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro]        Trimmer Legs:* Connect Leg 1 to 5V and Leg 2 to Ground.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • 4. Output Stage (Level Shifting)*
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Configuration: Open-Collector outputs.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Signal Path: Connect LM319 Outputs directly to 4 separate Pico GPIO pins.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] • Pull-ups (Critical): Connect a 2.2k $\Omega$ – 4.7k $\Omega$ resistor from each LM319
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] Output pin to Pico 3.3V (3V3_OUT).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro]        Warning:* Do not pull up to 5V. Pulling to 3.3V safely translates the 5V comparator
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] logic to RP2040 voltage tolerance.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] Design Notes
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Sync Separation: The fixed threshold comparator must detect sub-black sync pulses (0.0V
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] to ~0.3V).
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Hysteresis: Feedback resistors may be required on comparators to prevent oscillation at
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] video transition points.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  DC Coupling: The current design assumes a standard DC offset from the C64. If AC
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] coupling is added later, a DC clamp/restore circuit is required.
2025-11-28 15:15:05 [gemini-3-pro] 
