2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] The current implementation works for simple cases but has two specific issues:
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Artifacts: `\sqrt{x}` renders as `√{x}` because the braces aren't stripped.
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Greedy Regex: The `replaceLatex` regex `[^]+` will fail if the LaTeX string contains an
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] escaped dollar sign (`\`).
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the validated and improved code with brace handling and basic superscripts.
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] function texToUnicode(tex: string): string {
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	return tex
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		// Greek
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\alpha/g,'α').replace(/\\beta/g,'β').replace(/\\gamma/g,'γ')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\delta/g,'δ').replace(/\\theta/g,'θ').replace(/\\mu/g,'μ')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\pi/g,'π').replace(/\\sigma/g,'σ').replace(/\\omega/g,'ω')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		// Math
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\frac\{([^}]+)\}\{([^}]+)\}/g, '$1⁄$2')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\sqrt\{([^}]+)\}/g, '√$1')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\sqrt/g,'√')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\cdot/g,'·').replace(/\\times/g,'×')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\\leq/g,'≤').replace(/\\geq/g,'≥')
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		// Superscripts (simple single digit)
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\^([0-9])/g, (m, d) => "⁰¹²³⁴⁵⁶⁷⁸⁹"[d])
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		// Cleanup braces
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 		.replace(/\{|\}/g, '');
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] function replaceLatex(line: string): string {
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	// Logic updated to handle $$block$$ vs $inline$ slightly better
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	// and avoid capturing escaped \$
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 	return line.replace(/(\$\$?)((\\.|[^$])+?)\1/g, (_, delim, tex) => texToUnicode(tex));
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] }
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-28 15:44:38 [gemini-3-pro] 
