2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] The `BadResource: Bad resource ID` error in Deno typically means you're trying to use a resource
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] (file handle, network connection, stream) that's already been closed.
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] Looking at your stack trace, the crash originates from `console.log` calls, which suggests stdout
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] itself got closed - likely from a subprocess or stream issue.
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] Common causes:
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. Subprocess stdout/stderr closed prematurely - if you're piping from a child process that
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] died
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. Double-close on a resource - calling `.close()` twice on the same handle
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 3. Using a stream after it's been consumed/closed
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] Check around line 667 in `slopprompt.ts` and line 422 in `slopfountain.ts` - likely one of these
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] patterns:
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 08:59:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
