2025-11-29 10:56:21 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 10:56:21 [claude-opus-4-5] - Input 245s at 3.3V - address, control, clocks
2025-11-29 10:56:21 [claude-opus-4-5] - Output 245 at 5V - driving /NMI, /IRQ, /GAME, /EXROM
2025-11-29 10:56:21 [claude-opus-4-5] - Data 245 - tricky, needs to go both ways
2025-11-29 10:56:21 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 10:56:21 [claude-opus-4-5] For data you might need two 245s back to back, or accept 3.3V outputs to C64 (marginal but often
2025-11-29 10:56:21 [claude-opus-4-5] works with HC inputs on the C64 side).
