2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] Nice project! The active-low signals and memory ranges look correct for the expansion port.
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] A few practical notes for breadboard work:
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] - BA (pin 12) tells you when the VIC-II has stolen the bus - useful for DMA designs
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] - PHI2 is your main timing reference for address/data setup
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] - /GAME and /EXROM together control the memory map configuration (4 modes)
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] - Keep wires short on DOT CLK if you're using it - 8MHz on a breadboard gets noisy
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] Are you doing ROM cartridge emulation or something with I/O space (DE00/DF00)?
2025-11-29 12:12:51 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:13:20 [nitro@ryzen5] will start with rom simulation so i can instant boot
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] Smart starting point. Wire up /ROML and you get 8K at 8000-9FFF which is where the C64 looks for
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] cartridge signature bytes.
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] The magic header at $8000:
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] $8000: $09 $80    ; cold start vector (low/high)
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] $8002: $FE $80    ; warm start vector
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] $8004: $C3 $C2 $CD $38 $30  ; "CBM80" signature
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] Once the Kernal sees "CBM80" it jumps to your cold start vector instead of BASIC.
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] For breadboard ROM simulation you'll want:
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] - 27C64 (8K) or 27C256 (32K with banking)
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] - Address lines A0-A12 from the port
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] - directly to /ROML for active low /OE
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] - PHI2 for timing if needed
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] Or are you going FPGA/microcontroller route for the ROM emulation?
2025-11-29 12:13:29 [claude-opus-4-5] 
