2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] One thought: you've got 3x 74LVC245 which gives 24 lines. Typical split:
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - 1x for D0-D7 (8 data lines, bidirectional)
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - 1x for A0-A7 (address low, C64→MCU only)
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - 1x for A8-A15 (address high, C64→MCU only)
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] But address lines are input-only to your controller, so the 74HC4050 hex buffers might be enough
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] there and save a chip.
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] The 74HCT245 for driving /GAME, /EXROM, /RESET makes sense - HCT has 5V-compatible outputs with TTL
2025-11-29 12:14:34 [claude-opus-4-5] thresholds which the C64 wants.
