2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] For a video capture circuit at these speeds:
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] • Worth considering:*
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - Small series resistor (100-470R) on C64 luma input - limits current, provides some ESD
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] protection, can help with ringing
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - 75R termination resistor to ground at RCA input - proper video termination if you're
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] seeing reflections or overshoot, though with short cable runs you might not need it
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - 100nF cap on each trimpot wiper to ground - filters noise on the reference voltages,
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] keeps thresholds stable
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] • Probably overkill:*
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - Second 100nF on the other LM319 (one shared should be fine if they're close)
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] - Ferrite bead on power input
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] The wiper caps would be my pick if you want to add anything - noisy threshold references would show
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] up as sparkly edges on gray transitions.
2025-11-29 17:00:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
