2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] Shift registers 1-3 look good. Shared SH/LD on GP17, shared CLK on GP16, parallel Q7 outputs on
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] GP18/19/20/21. That's your four simultaneous reads sorted.
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] But register #4 has a copy-paste issue - you've got D0-D7 listed again instead of the control
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] signals. Should be something like:
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D0: /IRQ
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D1: /NMI
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D2: /RESET
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D3: /ROML
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D4: /ROMH
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D5: /EXROM
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D6: /GAME
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] - D7: DMA
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] Or whatever ordering makes your decode logic cleanest.
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] Also worth confirming - R/W and PHI2, where are they? PHI2 you'll want direct to a Pico GPIO for
2025-11-29 21:07:42 [claude-opus-4-5] triggering the PIO, not through a shift register. R/W could go either way but having it direct
