2025-11-29 21:23:33 [nitro@ryzen5] just to be clear the pio can write a byte of data to GP2..GP9?
2025-11-29 21:23:40 [claude-opus-4-5] Yes, PIO can write to any consecutive GPIO pins. GP2-GP9 is 8 consecutive pins, so a single `out
2025-11-29 21:23:40 [claude-opus-4-5] pins, 8` instruction with the pin base set to GP2 will do it.
2025-11-29 21:23:40 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:23:40 [claude-opus-4-5] Same for reading - `in pins, 8` with base GP2 pulls all 8 bits in one cycle.
2025-11-29 21:23:40 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:23:40 [claude-opus-4-5] The PIO pin mapping is flexible as long as they're consecutive for multi-bit operations.
