2025-11-29 21:28:29 [nitro@ryzen5] for pal what are clock freq?
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] PAL C64 clocks:
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] DOT, 7.88MHz
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] PHI2, 0.985MHz
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] DOT is the master, PHI2 is DOT divided by 8.
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] So PHI2 cycle is about 1.015µs, giving you roughly 500ns per half-cycle to work with. At 125MHz PIO
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] clock that's ~63 instructions per half-cycle.
2025-11-29 21:28:34 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:46 [nitro@ryzen5] a row of jumpers and headers could allow gpio flexibility
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] Good idea. Rather than hardwiring, a jumper block lets you reassign GPIOs if the PIO state machine
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] layout needs tweaking or you want to experiment with different pin groupings.
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] Something like a 2x20 header strip with jumper wires or shunts between Pico GPIOs and the
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] destination signals. Adds flexibility during development, can always commit to a fixed layout once
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] proven.
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] Also useful if you want to bring out test points - scope probes on PHI2, R/W, DOT, the shift clock,
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] etc.
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] Downside is trace length and potential noise pickup, but at these speeds probably fine. Would add
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] to BOM though - maybe:
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 1x 2x20 male header
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 20x jumper wires or shunts
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] Or just break out the flexible signals and hardwire the obvious ones like power and ground?
2025-11-29 21:29:56 [claude-opus-4-5] 
