2025-11-29 21:41:02 [nitro@ryzen5] which are the internal gpio again?
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] On the Pico board:
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] GP23, SMPS power save
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] GP24, VBUS sense
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] GP25, onboard LED
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] GP29 is also used internally for VSYS/3 voltage sensing via ADC.
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] So your current allocation has PHI2 on GP23 and R/W on GP24 which conflicts with those internal
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] functions. Might cause issues - the SMPS and VBUS sense are active on the Pico board even if you
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] don't use them in code.
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] Safer to move PHI2, R/W, DOT all below GP22 or onto GP26-28. You've got GP26/27 on control outputs
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] currently - could shuffle things around or accept the conflicts if you're not using USB power
2025-11-29 21:41:14 [claude-opus-4-5] sensing or power save modes.
