2025-11-29 21:58:29 [nitro@ryzen5] other alternative uses for 6.18
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 6.18 is B0 on transceiver 6, driven by GP10 via A0.
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] Options:
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. /RESET out - active control of C64 reset line
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. DOT passthrough - route DOT in to GP10, echo it out to B0 for debugging/scope
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 3. USER - general purpose active-low output for expansion
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 4. NC - leave unconnected, use GP10 purely as DOT input
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] If you want DOT as input on GP10, then B0 just follows whatever GP10 sees - probably not useful.
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] Better to leave 6.18 NC and accept GP10 is input-only for DOT.
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] GP10, DOT in
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 6.18, B0, NC
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] Then you lose /RESET output capability. Acceptable? Most cartridges don't drive /RESET anyway.
2025-11-29 21:58:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] Looks consistent now. One remaining issue:
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] GP10 is DOT input but also connected to transceiver 6.2 (A0). With DIR tied high, the 245 drives
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] from A to B - so whatever is on GP10 gets pushed out to B0 (NC). That's fine electrically since B0
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] is unconnected, but GP10 is being driven by the Pico side while you want it as an input from DOT.
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] Need to either:
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. Don't route GP10 through transceiver 6 - cut the connection, wire DOT directly to GP10
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] bypassing the 245
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. Flip DIR for just that channel - not possible, DIR is shared across all 8 channels
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] Option 1 means GP10 connects directly to DOT on the cartridge, with a 10K series resistor for
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] protection. Transceiver 6.2/6.18 left floating or tied off.
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 6.2, A0, NC
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 6.18, B0, NC
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] GP10, DOT (direct, 10K series)
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] That frees the 245 channel and keeps DOT as a clean input.
2025-11-29 21:59:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
