2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] Summary of signal flow:
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] • Inputs to Pico (active during PHI2):*
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - A0-A15 via shift registers 1+2 → GP18, GP19
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - D0-D7 via shift register 3 → GP20
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - /IRQ, /NMI, R/W, /ROML, /ROMH, /EXROM, /GAME, DMA via shift register 4 → GP21
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - DOT direct → GP10
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - PHI2 direct → GP28
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] • Outputs from Pico:*
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - D0-D7 via transceiver 5 → cartridge data bus (active when GP22 low)
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - /IRQ, /NMI, /ROML, /ROMH, /EXROM, /GAME, DMA via transceiver 6 → cartridge control (always
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] enabled)
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] • Shift register control:*
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - GP16 clocks all four 165s together
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - GP17 latches all four 165s together
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - GP18-21 read four serial streams in parallel
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] One minor note - you're reading and writing /IRQ, /NMI, /ROML, /ROMH, /EXROM, /GAME, DMA. That's
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] intentional for bidirectional control? The 10K series resistors on the output side will help avoid
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] contention if C64 is also driving those lines.
2025-11-29 22:01:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
