2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] A few issues I spot:
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] • 74HC165 powered at 5V but outputting to 3.3V RP2040* - Q7 outputs will be 5V logic
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] levels. Need level shifting or run the 165s at 3.3V instead (they'll still read 5V inputs fine with
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] HC family).
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] • Shift register 4 reading signals you're also driving via 245* - /ROMH, /EXROM, /GAME,
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] DMA, /IRQ, /NMI are on both the input shift register and output transceiver. Bus contention risk.
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] • 74LVC245 direction* - DIR tied to 5V means A→B always. That's RP2040→C64 which looks
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] correct for outputs, but verify that's the intent.
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] • Control signals active low* - Most C64 cart signals are active low with open-drain
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] expected. The 245 will drive them hard high/low rather than open-drain. May need to keep /OE high
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] and only enable when asserting low.
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] What's the intended operation - ROM emulation, REU style DMA, or something else? That'll clarify
2025-11-29 22:10:06 [claude-opus-4-5] whether reading back your own outputs makes sense.
