2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ## Simplified GPIO Connections (Read-Only Cartridge)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Removed Features
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - R/W drive capability (GP22 freed or repurposed)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - DMA write support (GP27 can be input-only or removed)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Address bus output (no additional transceivers needed)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### GP22 Repurposing Options
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] **Option 1: Keep as /OE for 74LVC245**
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Controls data bus output enable
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Logic: /OE LOW when (address in ROM range) AND (R/W HIGH from shift register)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] **Option 2: Additional Control Input**
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Monitor BA line (bus available) via 10K series
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Monitor RESET line
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Monitor COLOR CLOCK (3.58MHz NTSC / 4.43MHz PAL)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] **Option 3: Second Data Transceiver /OE**
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Add second 74LVC245 for banking or extended ROM space
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - GP21 and GP22 control separate 8K ROM windows
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Simplified DMA (Optional)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] GP27 (DMA out): Can still request DMA for read-only operations
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Useful for: Sprite data streaming, character set updates, screen DMA
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - C64 grants bus, cartridge only drives data during reads
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - No R/W control needed (BA LOW implies read cycles only for cart)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Updated Control Flow
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 1. Shift registers capture: Address (16-bit), Data (8-bit), Control (8-bit)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 2. RP2040 decodes address and R/W state from shift register data
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 3. If (address in range) AND (R/W = READ): lookup ROM data, drive to GP2-9, assert /OE
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 4. Otherwise: keep /OE HIGH (data bus tri-stated)
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Timing Simplified
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] Without write monitoring, the critical path is purely:
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] PHI2 edge → Shift register read → Address decode → ROM lookup → Data output
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] Target: <400ns for reliable operation at 1MHz
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] This removes the bidirectional complexity entirely. Would you like to update the netlist to reflect
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] this simplified approach?
2025-11-30 06:45:30 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:25 [nitro@ryzen5] would a cart ever need to read DMA pin?
2025-11-30 06:50:43 [claude-sonnet-4-5] Good question. Let me think through the DMA handshaking protocol.
2025-11-30 06:50:43 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:43 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:43 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ## DMA Pin Direction Analysis
2025-11-30 06:50:43 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:43 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### C64 DMA Protocol
2025-11-30 06:50:43 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 1. Cartridge asserts DMA LOW (requests bus)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 2. C64 responds by asserting BA LOW (bus available)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 3. Cartridge monitors BA to know when bus is granted
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 4. Cartridge drives bus while BA is LOW
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 5. Cartridge releases DMA HIGH when done
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 6. C64 releases BA HIGH and resumes control
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Does Cart Need to Read DMA?
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] **No.** The cartridge controls the DMA pin - it only needs to drive it.
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] **Monitoring bus grant:** Cart reads **BA** line (not DMA) to detect when C64 has granted the bus.
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - BA is currently on shift register 4.6 (P7) - but this appears to be labeled "DMA" in your netlist
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - **Clarification needed:** Is pin 4.6 connected to C64's BA line or DMA line?
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Correct Monitoring
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - **DMA (pin 13):** Cart output only (GP27 open drain)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - **BA (pin 7):** Cart input only (via shift register for monitoring)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### Updated Control Pins (Shift Register 4)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 4.3, P4, /ROMH    (input)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 4.4, P5, /EXROM   (input)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 4.5, P6, /GAME    (input)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 4.6, P7, BA       (input - monitors bus available)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### GP27 Usage
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] **Output only:** Open drain to DMA line
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Drive LOW to request bus
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Float HIGH (High-Z) when not requesting
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Never needs to read this pin
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] ### BA Monitoring
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] Read BA state from shift register bit (4.6)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - BA HIGH: C64 owns bus
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - BA LOW: Bus granted to cartridge (can drive address/data if implemented)
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] So DMA is output-only, and you monitor BA (not DMA) to detect the grant. Does your netlist pin 4.6
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] actually connect to BA or DMA on the C64 edge connector?
2025-11-30 06:50:44 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
