2025-11-30 06:59:18 [nitro@ryzen5] is dma pull low for assert, can i call it /DMA?
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] Yes, absolutely. DMA is active low on the C64 cartridge port, so `/DMA` is the correct notation.
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] • C64 DMA Protocol:*
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - `/DMA` pulled LOW by cartridge = Request bus mastership
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - C64 responds by pulling `BA` LOW = Bus granted
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - `/DMA` released HIGH (High-Z) = Release bus
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] • Updated Netlist Notation:*
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] GP27, /DMA out
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] And in the Open Drain signals section:
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] GP27, /DMA out
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] This is consistent with your other active-low signals like `/IRQ`, `/NMI`, `/ROML`, `/ROMH`,
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] `/EXROM`, and `/GAME`.
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] • Implementation remains the same:*
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Toggle between Output LOW (assert) and Input/High-Z (release)
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - 10K series resistor for protection
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] - Never drive Output HIGH
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] Good catch on the notation consistency.
2025-11-30 06:59:28 [claude-sonnet-4-5] 
