2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the Commodore 1540 was the disk drive released specifically for the VIC-20.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] It is electrically compatible with the C64, but the timing is different. The VIC-20's 6502 runs
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] uninterrupted, so the 1540 sends data slightly faster. The C64's VIC-II video chip halts the CPU
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] every 8th raster line ("badlines"), which causes the C64 to miss bits from a standard 1540.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] The 1541 was released to replace it; it runs slightly slower to accommodate the C64's video
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] interrupts.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] Project Fifteen Feedback
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding your BOM for the IEC bus:
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  2N7000 FETs: This is the correct approach for the IEC bus. The bus is Open
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] Collector.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Lines are pulled up to 5V by the computer/drive.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Devices pull the line Low to signal.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Your RP2040 GPIO (3.3V) driving the Gate will switch the FET, pulling the Drain (IEC line)
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] to Source (GND).
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  74HC165: Using a shift register to read the IEC bus is unusual and likely too
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] slow for the handshake timing.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   The IEC bus (ATN, CLK, DATA) is already serial.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   The RP2040 needs to react to state changes (High/Low) instantly for the handshake.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Recommendation: Use voltage dividers (e.g., 2.2k/3.3k) or a non-inverting buffer
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] (like 74LVC245 or 74LVC125) to read the 5V IEC lines directly into RP2040 GPIOs. This allows you to
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] use the RP2040 PIO (Programmable I/O) state machines to handle the protocol with precise timing.
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] IEC DIN-6 Pinout Reference
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] ╭────────┬──────────┬─────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╮
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  Pin   │  Name    │  Direction  │  Note                                                   │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] ├────────┼──────────┼─────────────┼─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  :---  │  :---    │  :---       │  :---                                                   │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  1     │  /SRQ    │  In/Out     │  Service Request (Fast Serial clock on C128/1571/1581)  │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  2     │  GND     │  -          │  Ground                                                 │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  3     │  /ATN    │  In         │  Attention (Host asserts low to start command)          │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  4     │  /CLK    │  In/Out     │  Clock (Handshake)                                      │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  5     │  /DATA   │  In/Out     │  Data (Handshake)                                       │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] │  6     │  /RESET  │  In         │  System Reset                                           │
2025-11-30 08:07:57 [gemini-3-pro] ╰────────┴──────────┴─────────────┴─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────╯
