2025-11-30 08:16:27 [nitro@ryzen5] which signals do i need to drive low as a node on the bus?
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the Commodore 1540 was the disk drive released specifically for the VIC-20. It
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] is mechanically identical to the 1541 but the ROM timing is slightly faster. The C64's VIC-II video
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] chip steals bus cycles, making the C64 too slow to talk to a stock 1540, forcing Commodore to slow
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] down the protocol for the 1541.
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding the PIO: It runs at system clock speed (125MHz+). It can shift registers
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] continuously at tens of megahertz. It is vastly faster than the IEC bus (which runs at ~1-2kHz
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] standard, or ~10-20kHz fast serial).
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] Since the IEC bus is slow and only has a few lines, dropping the shift register is the right design
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] choice.
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] Signals to Drive Low (Open Collector/Drain)
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] The IEC bus is Open Collector. The lines are pulled up to 5V by the computer/drive and
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] devices pull them to Ground to signal `0` or `Active`.
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] If acting as a Device (Disk Drive):
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  DATA: Must be able to pull Low (to send data and acknowledge attention).
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  CLK: Must be able to pull Low (to send data).
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  SRQ: (Optional) Used for C128 "Fast Serial" mode.
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  ATN: Read-only (The computer drives this low to command devices).
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  RESET: Read-only (Usually).
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] If acting as a Controller (The Computer):
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  ATN: Must be able to pull Low.
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  CLK: Must be able to pull Low.
2025-11-30 08:17:09 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  DATA: Must be able to pull Low.
