2025-11-30 08:18:23 [nitro@ryzen5] add ATN so 4 fet?
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the Commodore 1540 was the disk drive produced for the VIC-20. It uses a slightly
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] faster serial timing than the 1541. The C64 actually has to slow down its bus timing to talk to a
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 1541; the 1540 is generally incompatible with a stock C64 because the C64 CPU halts during video
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] line blanking, missing bits at 1540 speeds.
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] • PIO Speed:*
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] The RP2040 PIO runs at system clock (default 125MHz). It can shift data in/out at tens of megabytes
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] per second. The Commodore IEC bus runs at roughly 1.2kHz to 2.4kHz (Standard) or ~10-20kHz (Fast
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] Serial). The PIO is orders of magnitude faster than necessary; it can bit-bang IEC while sleeping.
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] • Signals to Drive:*
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] The IEC bus is Open Collector (Open Drain).
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  DATA: Drive Low (Acknowledge/Data).
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  CLK: Drive Low (Handshake/Clock).
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  ATN: Drive Low (Only if acting as Master/Host). A Drive usually only reads ATN.
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  SRQ: Drive Low (Fast Serial / Burst Mode). Used by 1571/1581/C128.
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] • 4 FETs?*
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] Yes. To be fully compliant (Fast Serial capable + Host capable), you need 4.
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] If simulating a standard 1541 only: 2 FETs (Data, Clk).
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] If simulating a 1581 or Host: 4 FETs (Data, Clk, Atn, Srq).
2025-11-30 08:19:10 [gemini-3-pro] 
