2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] Project Fifteen
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Commodore Serial Bus (IEC) Emulator*
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] To answer your questions:
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  1540 Model: Yes, the VIC-1540 was the companion drive for the VIC-20. It runs slightly
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] faster than the 1541 because the VIC-20 didn't require the "slow down" code added for the C64's
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] video chip timing.
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  PIO Speed: The RP2040 PIO runs at system clock speed (default 125MHz). It can sample or
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] toggle pins every cycle (8ns). This is orders of magnitude faster than the IEC bus (standard
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] ~1-2kHz, Fast Serial ~20-80kHz).
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Signals to Drive: As a device (Drive), you must be able to pull DATA and
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] CLK low. For Fast Serial (C128/1571/1581), you also drive SRQ. Driving ATN
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] allows the RP2040 to act as a Host (Computer) or signal requests, so 4 FETs is the correct choice
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] for full flexibility.
2025-11-30 08:26:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
