2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the Commodore 1540 was the disk drive designed for the VIC-20. It runs slightly faster
2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] than the 1541 because the VIC-20 Video Interface Chip did not slow down the CPU, allowing tighter
2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] timing loops. The 1541 added code to slow it down for the C64.
2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding the RP2040 PIO: It can run at system clock speed (125MHz+). It is significantly faster
2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] than the IEC bus (Standard ~20kHz, Fast Serial ~400kHz) and can easily handle sampling and driving
2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] these lines directly without shift registers.
2025-11-30 08:27:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
