2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] These are well-structured hardware interface designs for RP2040-based C64 peripherals. A few
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] observations:
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] • Fifteen (IEC Bus)* - Clean approach. The 2.2k/3.3k divider gives ~3.0V from 5V which is
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] safe for RP2040 inputs. 2N7000 open-drain is standard for IEC.
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] • LUMA2* - Interesting video capture concept. Note: 320×200×2bit×50Hz = 640KB/s raw
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] throughput. PIO should handle the sampling, but buffering/USB transfer will need attention. The
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] LM319 is a good choice for the ~8MHz dot clock timing.
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] • Toast (Cartridge)* - Most complex design. A few points:
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] - GP26 is listed for both ADC0 and DOT clock - potential conflict
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] - The 74HC165 cascade for reading address/data/control is sensible for GPIO conservation
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] - PHI2 at ~1MHz with voltage divider should work, though timing margins will be tight for
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] cycle-accurate emulation
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] - You're reading control signals via shift register (slower) but also have direct GPIO assignments
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] for the same signals as outputs - this asymmetry is intentional for the active-low assertion use
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] case
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] The 10K series resistors for static 5V inputs are conservative - should be fine for DC reads but
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] may slow edge transitions if timing matters.
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] Want me to review any specific aspect in more detail, or help with PIO/firmware code for any of
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] these?
2025-11-30 08:50:00 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:50:57 [nitro@ryzen5] what is pinout for the other user port on the c64?
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] The C64 user port is a 24-pin edge connector (12 pins per side):
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] ╭───────┬──────────┬──────────┬───────╮
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Pin  │  Top     │  Bottom  │  Pin  │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] ├───────┼──────────┼──────────┼───────┤
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  1    │  GND     │  GND     │  A    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  2    │  +5V     │  /FLAG2  │  B    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  3    │  /RESET  │  PB0     │  C    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  4    │  CNT1    │  PB1     │  D    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  5    │  SP1     │  PB2     │  E    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  6    │  CNT2    │  PB3     │  F    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  7    │  SP2     │  PB4     │  H    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  8    │  /PC2    │  PB5     │  J    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  9    │  ATN     │  PB6     │  K    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  10   │  9VAC    │  PB7     │  L    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  11   │  9VAC    │  PA2     │  M    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] │  12   │  GND     │  GND     │  N    │
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] ╰───────┴──────────┴──────────┴───────╯
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] • Key signals:*
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] - PB0-PB7: CIA2 Port B (directly accent, accent accent)
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] - PA2: CIA2 Port A bit 2
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] - SP1/SP2, CNT1/CNT2: CIA serial ports
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] - FLAG2: CIA2 handshake input
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] - PC2: CIA2 handshake output
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] - ATN: directly accent to IEC bus ATN line
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] The accent accent PB0-PB7 lines are accent popular for accent accent accent accent accent accent
2025-11-30 08:51:26 [claude-opus-4-5] accent accent accent accent accent accent accent accent accent accent accent accent accent accent
