2025-11-30 09:15:07 [nitro@ryzen5] what is SP2?
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] SP2 is CIA2's second serial port data line.
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] CIA2 has two independent serial shift registers:
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] - SP1/CNT1 - Serial Port 1 data/clock
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] - SP2/CNT2 - Serial Port 2 data/clock
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] Each can shift 8 bits in or out, clocked by its CNT line. Used for fast serial protocols - much
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] quicker than the software-bitbanged IEC bus.
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] Common uses:
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] - Fast disk loaders (e.g. SpeedDOS, JiffyDOS parallel cable)
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] - Linking two C64s
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] - High-speed peripherals
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] If you only need one serial channel, SP1 alone is fine. If you want both directions on SP2, add Q11
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] for SP2 out on a spare GPIO.
2025-11-30 09:15:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
