2025-11-30 09:21:57 [nitro@ryzen5] what is PA2?
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] PA2 is bit 2 of CIA2 Port A.
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] Port A is mostly used for IEC bus and VIC bank switching, but PA2 is directly exposed on the user
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] port as a general purpose I/O line.
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] Common uses:
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] - Directly tied to IEC /CLK line internally
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] - RS-232 carrier detect on some adapters
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] - General handshaking signal
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] - Extra control line for user port peripherals
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] It's just a single GPIO from CIA2 - useful as a 9th data bit or control flag alongside PB0-7.
2025-11-30 09:22:04 [claude-opus-4-5] 
