2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] Yes. Two 74HC165 daisy-chained:
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP15,shift CLK,Output
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP16,shift SH/LD,Output
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP17,shift Q7,Input
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 3 GPIOs reads 16 bits:
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] - PB0-7 (8 bits)
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] - SP1, SP2, PA2, FLAG2, PC2 (5 bits)
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] - CNT1, CNT2 (2 bits) - but these are clocks, shift register too slow
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] - Spare (1 bit)
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] Problem: CNT1/CNT2 are clock signals, need real-time sampling not shift register.
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] So shift register for static signals:
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 165 #1: PB0-7
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 165 #2: SP1, SP2, PA2, FLAG2, PC2, spare, spare, spare
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] Keep CNT1/CNT2 on direct GPIO with dividers if needed.
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP15,shift CLK
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP16,shift SH/LD
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP17,shift Q7
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP26,CNT1,Input,divider
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] GP28,CNT2,Input,divider
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:36:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
