2025-11-30 09:48:46 [nitro@ryzen5] how about flag2 and pc2?
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] • FLAG2* - CIA2 input only. External device pulls low to signal "data ready". Directly
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] triggers CIA interrupt. C64 cannot drive it.
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] • PC2* - CIA2 output only. Directly controlled by C64 to signal "byte taken". Directly
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] triggers CIA interrupt. C64 pulses it automatically on Port B read/write.
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] So:
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] - FLAG2 - input to C64, output from Pico → needs 2N7000
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] - PC2 - output from C64, input to Pico → shift register only
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] GP19,FLAG2 out,Output,2N7000,B
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] Updates BOM to:
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 14x 2N7000 (PB0-7, PA2, SP1, SP2, CNT1, CNT2, FLAG2)
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 09:48:58 [claude-opus-4-5] PC2 stays input via 165.
