2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] Acknowledged. Four RP2040 interface projects for C64/CBM hardware:
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] - Fifteen: IEC serial bus interface with voltage dividers and 2N7000 open-drain drivers
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] - LUMA2: Video capture using LM319 comparators for 2-bit monochrome + optional chroma
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] - Toast: Cartridge port interface with shift registers and level translation
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] - Node: User port interface for CIA2 parallel/serial communication
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] All use similar patterns: voltage dividers for 5V→3.3V input, 2N7000 FETs for open-drain outputs,
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] 74HC165 for parallel-to-serial reads, 74LVC245 for buffered writes.
2025-11-30 12:15:09 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 12:16:03 [nitro@ryzen5] rate the main design issues
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] • Fifteen* - Solid. Simple and proven approach. No issues.
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] • LUMA2* - Timing is tight. 280ns chroma window at 125MHz gives ~35 cycles. PIO edge
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] counting feasible but needs careful tuning. Bias resistor through GPIO (220K) is unconventional -
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] works but adds coupling between threshold adjustment and Pico state.
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] • Toast* - PHI2 at ~1MHz through voltage divider is marginal. 3.3K to ground with cable
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] capacitance may round edges. Consider lower divider impedance (1K/1.5K). Also reading control
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] signals through shift register adds 8+ clock latencies - fine for slow signals, problematic if
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] timing ROM responses to PHI2.
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] • Node* - 74HC165 running at 5V with Q7 through 10K to 3.3V GPIO is borderline. HC outputs
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] swing to VCC, so you're relying on the 10K plus GPIO clamp diodes. Works but not ideal. Consider
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] 74LVC165 at 3.3V or proper level shifter. CNT1/CNT2 dividers are correct for clock inputs.
2025-11-30 12:16:16 [claude-opus-4-5] 
