2025-11-30 12:25:16 [claude-opus-4-5] No. The 100K bias resistor is specific to LUMA2's AC-coupled chroma comparator - it provides DC
2025-11-30 12:25:16 [claude-opus-4-5] bias to the comparator input after the coupling capacitor.
2025-11-30 12:25:16 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 12:25:16 [claude-opus-4-5] Node uses DC-coupled signals throughout. The 1K series resistors limit current, the voltage
2025-11-30 12:25:16 [claude-opus-4-5] dividers on CNT1/CNT2 handle level shifting. No bias resistors needed.
