2025-11-30 17:22:25 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding the update to Project Crumpet:
2025-11-30 17:22:25 [gemini-3-pro] The revision to the output logic is significant. By splitting the 16-bit data bus into two parallel
2025-11-30 17:22:25 [gemini-3-pro] 8-bit streams (GP13 for Low Byte, GP14 for High Byte), you reduce the PIO burden to 8 clock cycles
2025-11-30 17:22:25 [gemini-3-pro] per write. This is crucial for meeting the timing constraints of the Megadrive's ~7.67MHz bus, as a
2025-11-30 17:22:25 [gemini-3-pro] linear 16-bit shift might be too slow during tight read/write windows.
