2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] I have noted the update to Project Crumpet regarding the parallel shift architecture for
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] the Sega Megadrive interface.
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] • Updated Project Crumpet Output GPIO Allocation:*
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] • GP10: Shift Out CLK
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] • GP11: Shift Out Latch (SH/LD / RCLK)
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] • GP12: Shift Out /OE
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] • GP13: Data Out (D0–D7 chain)
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] • GP14: Data Out (D8–D15 chain)
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] This configuration allows reading the 48 input bits (Address, Data, Control) in 8 clock cycles via
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] GP4–GP9, and writing the 16 output bits (Data Bus) in 8 clock cycles via GP13–GP14.
2025-11-30 17:23:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] Project Crumpet looks like a robust solution for the high pin count of the 16-bit era. The update
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] to the GPIO allocation for parallel shifting is a significant optimization; reducing the read
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] operation to 8 clock cycles (reading 6 bits wide) and the write operation to 8 clock cycles
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] (writing 2 bits wide) will drastically improve timing margins against the ~7.6MHz bus.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] Here are a few observations on the updated Netlist and BOM:
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • BOM vs. Summary Discrepancy*
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • Summary: Mentions `2x74LVC245` transceivers.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • BOM/Netlist: Lists `2x 74HC595` shift registers for the output stage.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • Note: If the plan is to drive the 5V data bus via shift registers, ensure you use
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] 74HCT595 (TTL inputs) if powering them at 5V. Standard HC chips at 5V may not reliably
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] detect the RP2040's 3.3V logic high. Alternatively, the LVC245s mentioned in the summary would
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] handle level translation perfectly if placed between the 3.3V logic and the bus.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • Logic Logic*
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • Input Coverage: 6 × 74HC165 provides 48 bits of input.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Address (23) + Data (16) = 39 bits.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro]     *   This leaves 9 bits for control signals (/AS, /DTACK, etc.), which fits perfectly.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • Output Coverage: 2 × 74HC595 provides 16 bits of output.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro]     *   This covers D0–D15 exactly.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • Updated GPIO Allocation*
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] The updated pinout for the output stage looks correct for the parallel write strategy:
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • GP10 (CLK) / GP11 (SH/LD) / GP12 (OE): Shared control lines.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • GP13 / GP14: Data lines feeding two shift registers simultaneously (High Byte / Low
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] Byte).
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] • GP15: Reserved for the incoming system clock.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] The documentation has been updated.
2025-11-30 17:24:26 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:26:22 [nitro@ryzen5] to emulate a cartridge please detail steps in series of csv
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the step-by-step procedure to emulate a Megadrive cartridge read cycle using the Project
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] Crumpet hardware, formatted as a CSV.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] Step,Phase,GPIO Action,Description
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 1,Idle,Monitor GP9 (Control Stream),Wait for /CE (Cartridge Enable) bit to go LOW indicating bus access start.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 2,Snapshot,Pulse GP3 (In_SH/LD) LOW then HIGH,Latch current state of Address Bus, Data Bus, and Control signals into 74HC165s.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 3,Ingest,Loop 8 times: Read GP4-GP9; Pulse GP2 (In_CLK),Parallel shift-in of 6 bytes (48 bits) covering A1-A23, D0-D15, and Controls in 8 clock cycles.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 4,Decode,Internal CPU Logic,Reconstruct 23-bit Address and Control flags. Verify Read cycle (/OE is Active).
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 5,Fetch,Internal CPU Logic,Retrieve 16-bit data word from RP2040 RAM/Flash array based on decoded Address.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 6,Serialize,Loop 8 times: Set GP13 (Data L) & GP14 (Data H); Pulse GP10 (Out_CLK),Shift retrieved 16-bit word into the two 74HC595 registers (8 bits per line simultaneously).
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 7,Stage,Pulse GP11 (Out_SH/LD),Transfer shifted data from 595 shift register to storage register (Outputs remain High-Z).
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 8,Drive,Set GP12 (Out_OE) LOW,Enable 74HC595 output buffers to drive D0-D15 lines on the Megadrive bus.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 9,Ack,Set Open Drain GPIO LOW,Assert /DTACK (Data Acknowledge) to signal Megadrive 68000 that valid data is on the bus.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 10,Hold,Monitor GP9 (via periodic re-snapshot) or GP15 (CLK),Wait for /CE or /AS to go HIGH indicating cycle completion.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 11,Release,Set GP12 (Out_OE) HIGH,Disable 74HC595 output buffers (High-Z) to free the Data Bus.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 12,Reset Ack,Set Open Drain GPIO HIGH-Z,De-assert /DTACK.
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:26:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:27:56 [nitro@ryzen5] which pins need to be driven low with fets?
2025-11-30 17:28:00 [nitro@ryzen5] for control
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the CSV netlists for the shift registers and FET assignments.
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] FET Control Logic
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] The two signals that require Open Drain driving (Active Low) on a Megadrive cartridge are:
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  /DTACK (Pin B31): Data Acknowledge. The console waits for this to go LOW before
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] finishing a bus cycle. Driving this allows the RP2040 to pause the 68k if it needs more time to
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] fetch data.
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  /CART (Pin B32): Cartridge Detect. Usually tied to GND. Driving this allows the RP2040
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] to simulate cartridge insertion/removal electronically.
2025-11-30 17:28:45 [gemini-3-pro] 
