2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the details for the Open Drain FET drivers and the logical steps for cartridge emulation
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] based on your updated GPIO allocation.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] FET Drivers
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] The Megadrive control lines are active low and often pulled up by the console. The cartridge must
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] pull them to Ground to assert them, or leave them floating (High-Z) to de-assert.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] • Pins to be driven low with 2N7000 FETs:*
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  /DTACK (Data Transfer Acknowledge):
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Function: Tells the 68000 that the cartridge has placed valid data on the bus
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] during a read cycle, or accepted data during a write cycle.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Logic:
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]         *   GPIO HIGH: FET On → /DTACK Low (Active/Asserted).
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]         *   GPIO LOW: FET Off → /DTACK Floating (Passive/High).
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  /CART (Cartridge Detect):
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Function: Tells the I/O controller that a cartridge is inserted.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Logic:
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]         *   GPIO HIGH: FET On → /CART Low (Cartridge Present).
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro]         *   GPIO LOW: FET Off → /CART Floating.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] Cartridge Emulation Logic (Read Cycle)
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] The following CSV details the sequence to emulate a ROM read. The RP2040 must monitor the input
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] registers for a Chip Enable (/CE) on the cartridge slot.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] Step,Phase,Action,GPIO Logic
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 1,Idle,Monitor Inputs,Pulse GP3 (SH/LD) Low then High to latch inputs.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 2,Idle,Read Controls,Clock GP2 (CLK) 8 times reading GP9 (Controls). Check if /CE is Low.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 3,Address,Read Address,Read GP4-GP6 (Address Lines) simultaneous with Step 2 shifting.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 4,Lookup,Fetch Data,Use Address A1-A23 to find 16-bit word in RP2040 RAM/Flash.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 5,Data Setup,Shift Out,Write High byte to GP14 and Low byte to GP13. Clock GP10 8 times.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 6,Data Setup,Latch Data,Pulse GP11 (SH/LD) to move data to 595 storage register.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 7,Bus Drive,Enable Output,Set GP12 (/OE) LOW to drive D0-D15 onto Megadrive bus.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 8,Handshake,Assert DTACK,Set GP16 HIGH (FET On) to pull /DTACK Low.
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 9,Hold,Wait Cycle,Wait for Megadrive to release /AS or /CE (monitor via Shift In).
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 10,Release,Release Bus,Set GP16 LOW (Release /DTACK) and GP12 HIGH (Disable D0-D15).
2025-11-30 17:33:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
