2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] FET Driver Requirements
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] To answer your question regarding which pins need Open Drain (FET) drivers:
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  /DTACK (Data Acknowledge): Required. The cartridge must pull this low to tell
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] the 68000 that valid data is on the bus. Since the RP2040 is using shift registers (which introduce
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] latency), you must hold this high (floating) until the shift-out is complete, then pull Low.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  /CART (Cartridge Detect): Required. This is a static signal usually tied to
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] ground on real carts. The RP2040 can pull this low to simulate "insertion."
