2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] Emulation Cycle Steps (CSV)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the logical flow for a Read Cycle using shift registers, relying on /DTACK to pause the
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] CPU.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] Step,Action,Signals,Description
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 1,Idle,GP16=LOW(Float); GP12=HIGH,Wait for start of cycle (monitor CLK/CS)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 2,Capture,GP3=LOW; GP3=HIGH,Pulse SH/LD to parallel load 74HC165 inputs
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 3,Shift In,GP2 cycles 8 times,Read 6 bits simultaneously (Addresses + Control)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 4,Decode,Internal Logic,Reconstruct 24-bit Address and check Control bits (/CE /AS)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 5,Lookup,Internal Logic,Fetch 16-bit word from ROM array based on Address
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 6,Shift Out,GP10 cycles 8 times,Push 16-bit Data to 74HC595 (GP13/GP14)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 7,Latch Out,GP11=HIGH; GP11=LOW,Move shifted data to storage register
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 8,Bus Drive,GP12=LOW,Enable 74HC595 Output (Put Data on Bus)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 9,Ack,GP16=HIGH(Active Low),Turn on FET to pull /DTACK Low (CPU resumes)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 10,Hold,Wait for Control High,Wait for /AS or /CE to go High (Cycle End)
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 11,Release,GP12=HIGH; GP16=LOW(Float),Disable 74HC595 Output; Release /DTACK
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] Timing Feasibility Analysis
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Is Crumpet timing ok?*
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Yes, but only because of /DTACK.*
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  The Challenge: The 68000 bus cycle is roughly 500ns-600ns. Using shift registers
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] creates significant latency.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Shift In (8 clocks) + Processing + Shift Out (8 clocks) will likely exceed the standard ROM
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] access window of a real cartridge (~200ns).
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  The Solution: The Sega Genesis/Megadrive respects the /DTACK line.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   The CPU will enter "Wait States" automatically if /DTACK is not asserted immediately.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   By leaving /DTACK floating (High) until the RP2040 has finished shifting bits in and out,
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] you effectively pause the console.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Constraint: You must ensure the RP2040 PIO is clocked high enough (e.g., >125MHz) to
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] minimize the wait states, otherwise audio glitching (which relies on CPU timing) or raster effects
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] might desync.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Signal Integrity: Ensure the 74HC595 Output Enable (GP12) is strictly managed. You must
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] not drive the data bus until you are sure it is a Read cycle, otherwise, you risk bus contention
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] (short circuit) if the CPU tries to write at the same time.
2025-11-30 17:35:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
