2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the breakdown for the FET drivers, the emulation sequence, and the timing analysis for
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] Project Crumpet.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] FET Drivers
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] The Megadrive bus relies on Open Drain signals for handshaking and presence detection.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  /DTACK (Data Acknowledge): Essential. The cartridge must pull this low to tell
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] the 68000 that data is valid on the bus. If this is not driven low, the console will hang (wait
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] state).
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  /CART (Cartridge Detect): Required. This must be pulled low for the I/O
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] controller to enable the cartridge slot power/logic.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Netlist update for FETs:*
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Q1 (/DTACK): Gate: GP16, Source: GND, Drain: B32 (/DTACK)
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Q2 (/CART): Gate: GP17, Source: GND, Drain: B32 (/CART) - Note: often pin B32, verify
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] specific edge connector pinout.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] Emulation Sequence (Read Cycle)
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] The following CSV details the steps the RP2040 must perform to emulate a ROM read cycle.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] Step,Action,Direction,Signal,Description
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 1,Wait,Input,/AS,Wait for 68k to pull Address Strobe LOW
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 2,Latch,Output,SH/LD,Pulse 74HC165 SH/LD to capture bus state
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 3,Shift In,Input,Q7 Lanes,PIO clocks 8 times to read Address (A1-A23) and Control
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 4,Process,Internal,RP2040,Decode Address and fetch 16-bit Data word
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 5,Shift Out,Output,SER/CLK,PIO shifts 16-bit Data into 74HC595s
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 6,Output Enable,Output,/OE,Enable 74HC595 outputs to drive D0-D15
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 7,Handshake,Output,/DTACK,Drive GP16 HIGH (FET pulls /DTACK LOW)
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 8,Hold,Input,/AS,Wait for 68k to release Address Strobe HIGH
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 9,Release,Output,/DTACK,Drive GP16 LOW (FET releases /DTACK to High-Z)
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 10,Disable,Output,/OE,Disable 74HC595 outputs (High-Z)
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] Timing Analysis
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Is Crumpet timing ok?*
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Yes, but it is tight.*
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Bus Speed: The 68000 runs at ~7.67 MHz. One clock cycle is ~130ns.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Access Window: A standard bus cycle is 4 clocks (~520ns). The time from `/AS` going low
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] to data setup required is roughly 250ns.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Propagation Delay:
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro]     *   74HC165 Latch/Shift: ~25ns
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Level Shifting (Resistors/Input capacitance): ~10ns
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro]     *   74HC595 Output Enable: ~25ns
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Budget: You have approximately 150ns - 190ns for the RP2040 to detect the
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] start of the cycle, shift in 8 bits, look up data, and shift out 8 bits (since 595s are likely
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] split into bytes or 16-bit deep depending on wiring).
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] • Recommendations:*
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Overclock: Run the RP2040 at 200MHz+ to ensure PIO instructions execute fast enough
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] (5ns per instruction).
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  PIO Optimization: The "8 shifts" approach is correct. Reading 6 lanes in parallel takes
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] only 8 PIO cycles.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Wait States: If the logic is too slow, you can delay asserting `/DTACK`. The 68000 will
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] wait indefinitely, though this may affect audio/video synchronization in time-critical games.
2025-11-30 17:37:32 [gemini-3-pro] 
