2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] The updated GPIO allocation looks valid and covers all necessary signal paths for the parallel
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] shift architecture.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] FET Open Drain Drivers
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] You correctly identified the two critical signals requiring open-drain logic (Active Low, Passive
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] High/Floating).
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  /DTACK (Data Transfer Acknowledge): The 68000 asserts /AS (Address Strobe). The
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] cartridge must assert /DTACK low when data is on the bus. If the RP2040 takes time to fetch data,
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] delaying /DTACK effectively pauses the CPU (wait states).
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  /CART (Cartridge Detect): Must be pulled low for the Megadrive to recognize a cartridge
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] is inserted.
