2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] Emulation Logic Flow
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the step-by-step logic for a read cycle in CSV format.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] step, trigger, action, notes
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 1, /CE falls, PIO_IN set SH/LD LOW, Latch logic levels into 74HC165s
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 2, immediate, PIO_IN set SH/LD HIGH, Switch to shift mode
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 3, PIO loop, PIO_IN clock & read 8 bits, Parallel read 6 pins (A1-A23 + Ctrl)
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 4, ARM core, Decode Address, Map A1-A23 to ROM array index
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 5, ARM core, Fetch Data, Get 16-bit word
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 6, ARM core, Push to TX FIFO, Send to PIO_OUT
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 7, PIO_OUT, Shift out 8 bits, Parallel write 2 pins (D0-D7 + D8-D15) to 74HC595s
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 8, PIO_OUT, Pulse Latch, Transfer shift register to storage register
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 9, PIO_OUT, Enable /OE, Drive 74HC595 outputs onto Data Bus
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 10, GPIO, Assert /DTACK LOW, Signal CPU that data is valid
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 11, /CE rises, Release /DTACK, Set to High-Z (Input)
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 12, immediate, Disable /OE, Tri-state 74HC595 outputs
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] Timing and PIO Strategy
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] The timing is tight but feasible. The 68000 bus cycle is approximately 500ns.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Shift In (8 cycles):*
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] Using PIO with `sideset`, you can toggle the clock pin during the input instruction. You do
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] not need NOPs; the 74HC series can handle ~20MHz+, and the RP2040 at 125MHz+ is fast enough to
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] drive it.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] • PIO Input: ~16 system cycles (approx 128ns at 125MHz) to read all addresses.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Processing: C processing time to lookup array.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] • PIO Output: ~16 system cycles to push data to 595s.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Optimization:*
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] Using `sideset` is strictly better than interleaving NOPs. It ensures the clock transitions happen
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] exactly at the defined instruction boundary.
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Example Logic (Conceptual):*
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] ; Shift In Loop
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] set pins, 1   side 0 ; CLK low
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] in pins, 6    side 1 ; Read 6 bits, CLK high
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] jmp x-- loop  side 0 ; Loop 8 times
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 17:39:52 [gemini-3-pro] • GPIO Allocation Final Check*
