2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] Timing Analysis
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] The parallel shifting strategy is sound. The Megadrive 68k clock is ~7.67 MHz (approx 130ns cycle).
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] • Read Cycle: You need to capture inputs, decide on data, and output data.
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] • PIO Speed: At 125MHz+, the RP2040 can easily perform 8 shift cycles (plus overhead)
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] within a reasonable window.
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] • DTACK: The crucial element is driving `/DTACK` low. This tells the Megadrive to wait,
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] allowing the RP2040 extra cycles to finish the shift-in/lookup/shift-out process without crashing
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] the bus.
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] • Interleaving: You may not need NOPs if the traces are short, but PIO `side_set` allows
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] you to toggle the clock while simultaneously reading/writing data bits, making the 8-cycle burst
2025-11-30 17:46:10 [gemini-3-pro] highly efficient.
