2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Pins 3,4,7,8,13,14,17,18 (D0-D7 Inputs): Connect to GP10-GP17
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Pins 2,5,6,9,12,15,16,19 (Q0-Q7 Outputs): Connect to Megadrive D8-D15
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] Write Logic Sequence
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] To present 16-bit data (e.g., `0xABCD`) to the Megadrive:
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Idle: GP26 (/OE) is HIGH (High-Z state, not interfering with bus).
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Setup Low: Put `0xCD` (Low Byte) on GP10-GP17.
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Latch Low: Pulse GP21 (CLK_LO) High then Low. (U7 now holds `0xCD`).
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Setup High: Put `0xAB` (High Byte) on GP10-GP17.
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  Latch High: Pulse GP22 (CLK_HI) High then Low. (U8 now holds `0xAB`).
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 6.  Drive Bus: Set GP26 (/OE) LOW. (Megadrive now sees `0xABCD`).
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 7.  Handshake: Assert /DTACK (GP19 High -> FET Pulls Low).
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 8.  Finish: When Read Cycle ends, release /DTACK and set GP26 (/OE) HIGH.
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] Important Notes
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Bus Contention: Ensure your code logic never pulls GP26 (/OE) LOW unless you are
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 100% sure the Megadrive is performing a Read cycle. If the Megadrive tries to write while the 374s
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] are active, you will have a short circuit.
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] • Speed: This parallel method is significantly faster than the 74HC595 serial method (2 bus
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] writes vs 16 serial shifts), leaving more PIO cycles for address decoding.
2025-11-30 18:29:55 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, using 74LS374 Octal D-Type Flip-Flops is the correct approach to drive a 16-bit bus
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] using only 8 data GPIOs. Unlike the '245 transceiver, the '374 has memory (latches), allowing you
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] to write the low byte, store it, write the high byte, store it, and then enable both onto the bus
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] simultaneously.
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] Since 74LS inputs are TTL compatible, the 3.3V logic high from the RP2040 is sufficient to drive
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] them while they are powered at 5V.
2025-11-30 18:31:49 [gemini-3-pro] 
