2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] Commodore and Sega hardware.
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] Per your request to comment on new or different content, I have identified a specific conflict in
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] the Project Crumpet (Megadrive) specification regarding the output logic:
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Inconsistency in Project Crumpet Output Stage:*
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  BOM & GPIO Allocation: Lists 74LS374 (Octal D-type Flip-Flops/Latches). The
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] GPIO allocation defines `GP10-GP17` as a parallel data bus ("latch d0-d7") with separate clock pins
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] (`GP18`, `GP19`) for low/high bytes. This suggests a multiplexed parallel write strategy.
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Emulation Logic Steps: Steps 5, 6, and 7 describe driving 74HC595 (Serial Shift
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] Registers). Specifically, Step 5 mentions "Clock GP10 8 times... Shift 16-bit data," and Step 7
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] explicitly names "Enable 74HC595 output drivers."
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] • Recommendation:*
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] • If using 74LS374 (Parallel): The Logic Steps need to be updated to reflect writing an
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 8-bit byte to `GP10-17`, pulsing `GP18` (Low Byte), writing the next byte, and pulsing `GP19` (High
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] Byte).
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] • If using 74HC595 (Serial): The BOM and GPIO allocation need to be changed to remove the
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] parallel bus pins and assign Serial Data (DS), Shift Clock (SHCP), and Store Clock (STCP) pins
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] instead.
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] The remaining projects (Fifteen, Luma2, Toast, Cbm Node) appear internally consistent regarding
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] their BOMs and Netlists.
2025-11-30 18:34:22 [gemini-3-pro] 
