2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] There are significant conflicts in Project Crumpet between the GPIO Allocation
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] list, the Component Netlist, and the Logic Steps.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] The BOM specifies 74LS374 (Parallel Latches), but the Logic Steps and Component details
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] describe 74HC595 (Serial Shift Registers) behavior. Additionally, GP16/GP17 are
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] double-booked.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the reconciliation assuming the BOM (74LS374) and GPIO List are the
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] intended architecture (Parallel Output is faster/better for this application).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] Conflicts Found
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Output Architecture:
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro]        List:* GP10–GP17 assigned to `Latch D0-D7` (Parallel).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro]        Logic/Netlist:* GP10 assigned as `SRCLK`, GP13/14 as `SER` data lines (Serial).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Double Booking (GP16/GP17):
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro]        List:* GP16/17 are `Latch D6/D7`.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro]        FET Section:* GP16/17 are `/DTACK` and `/CART`.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro]        Resolution:* Move FETs to GP21/GP22 as per the GPIO List.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Component Type:
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro]        Netlist:* Refers to U7/U8 inputs as `SER` (Serial Pin 14 on a 595).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro]        BOM:* Refers to U7/U8 as 74LS374 (Parallel D-Flip Flops).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 
