2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] Updated Logic Steps (Parallel Write)
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Idle: Listen to U6 (Control) stream.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Decode: Determine 16-bit word to write.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Write Low: Put Low Byte on `GP10-GP17`, Pulse `GP18` (CP_LO).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Write High: Put High Byte on `GP10-GP17`, Pulse `GP19` (CP_HI).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 5.  Drive: Pull `GP20` (/OE) LOW.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 6.  Ack: Pull `GP21` (/DTACK) HIGH (FET ON -> Bus Low).
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 7.  Hold: Wait for cycle end.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 8.  Release: Release `GP21`, Release `GP20`.
2025-11-30 18:37:20 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:42:00 [nitro@ryzen5] 74LS374 pinout
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] There are a few critical conflicts in the netlist text versus the GPIO allocation table,
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] specifically regarding the Output Latches (74LS374) and the FET control pins.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the 74LS374 pinout and the corrections required to make the logic work.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] 74LS374 Pinout (20-Pin DIP)
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] This is an 8-bit D-Type Flip-Flop (Parallel In / Parallel Out), not a serial shift
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] register.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
