2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] Corrections & Conflicts
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] • 1. Output Logic (Parallel vs Serial)*
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] Your BOM lists 74LS374, but your netlist text references `595` (shift registers) and `SER`
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] pins.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] • The Issue: You cannot feed a 374 serially. It requires a parallel bus.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] • The Fix: Your GPIO Allocation (GP10-GP17) is set up correctly for a multiplexed
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] parallel bus. You must wire GP10-GP17 to D0-D7 on BOTH U7 and U8. You then toggle the
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] specific Clock pin (GP18 or GP19) to latch the data into the specific chip.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] • 2. FET GPIO Conflict*
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] • The Issue: Your "Open Drain FETs" text lists GP16 and GP17 for /DTACK and
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] /CART.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] • The Conflict: GP16 and GP17 are already used by your Data Bus (Latch D6, D7).
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] • The Fix: Use GP21 and GP22 as listed in your GPIO Allocation table.
2025-11-30 18:42:33 [gemini-3-pro] 
