2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] Here is a review of Project Crumpet regarding pin accounting, specifically looking for signals
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] present on the standard Sega Megadrive/Genesis 64-pin cartridge port that are not explicitly
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] defined in your netlist or JS object.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 1. GPIO / Documentation Conflict
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] There is a discrepancy regarding the Master Clock input between your Netlist and the JS
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] module:
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Netlist: `GP28, CLK, in, 2.2K+3.3K` (GP26/27 listed as spare).
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • JS Module: `26: { name: "MD_CLK"... }`.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Resolution: Ensure the physical PCB routing matches the code. GP26-29 are ADC pins on the
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] Pico; GP26 is valid for digital input, but GP28 is often preferred for PIO clock synchronization if
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] available.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 2. The "U6" Control Line Shift Register
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] Your netlist defines U6 generically as `Control Lines, /CE /OE /LWR /UWR /AS /VRES etc`. To fully
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] emulate a cartridge, you need to map the specific 8 parallel inputs of U6.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Essential Signals (5): `/CE`, `/OE`, `/LWR` (Write Lower), `/UWR` (Write Upper), `/AS`
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] (Address Strobe).
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Reset (1): `/VRES` (B27) - Essential for detecting system reset.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Mapper/Compat (1): `/TIME` (B31) - Used for Master System compatibility mode and some
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] mappers.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Spare (1): You have 1 slot left on U6.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Unaccounted Edge Connector Pins
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] The following pins exist on the physical 64-pin cartridge slot but are not connected in your
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] Netlist. This is likely intentional for a standard ROM cart, but worth noting:
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • B1 (Audio Left) & B3 (Audio Right): Analog inputs. The cartridge can mix audio into the
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] console's output (e.g., Virtua Racing PWM). Your BOM has no DAC or PWM filtering to drive these.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • B2 (/MRES): Master Reset. distinct from `/VRES` (B27). Most carts tie these together or
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] ignore `/MRES`, relying on `/VRES`.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • B30 (/YS): Yamaha Select / Overlay. Used by the 32X or Genlocks to overlay video. Usually
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] left floating or grounded on standard carts.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] • A26 (/ASEL): Input. Used to distinguish between cartridge and card slot (Master System
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] converter). Usually ignored for Mega Drive native carts.
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] 4. Updated JS Module Snippet
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] To resolve the ambiguity in `U6` and the Clock pin, here is the corrected `gpio` section for the JS
2025-11-30 18:53:09 [gemini-3-pro] file:
