2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] The specific logic for Project Crumpet relies on shifting in control signals (like /AS,
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] /CE, /LWR) via U6. This introduces a serialization latency (approx 8 PIO cycles) which may be too
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] slow for the Megadrive's strict timing (approx 250ns access window).
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the pins not directly accounted for or potential bottlenecks:
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  /AS (Address Strobe) & /CE (Chip Enable): Currently routed only to U6 (Shift
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] Register).
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro]        Recommendation:* Connect /AS directly to GP26 (Spare) to allow the PIO to
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] "wait for pin" rather than polling the shift stream. This ensures synchronization with the 68K bus
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] cycle.
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  /MRES (Pin B2): Master Reset (Output from Cart to Console).
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro]        Status:* Not connected. Useful if the RP2040 needs to reboot the console.
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  /TIME (Pin B30):
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro]        Status:* Not connected. Used for specific M-Network bank switching or lockout,
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] though rarely needed for standard emulation.
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Audio Lines (B1, B3):
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro]        Status:* Not connected. (Likely intentional).
2025-11-30 18:56:37 [gemini-3-pro] 
