2025-11-30 18:59:16 [gemini-3-pro] Missing Pins Analysis
2025-11-30 18:59:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:59:16 [gemini-3-pro] You have accounted for the vast majority of the digital logic required for a standard cartridge.
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  U6 Control Register Capacity: U6 has 8 parallel inputs. Your listed control signals are
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] `/CE`, `/OE`, `/LWR`, `/UWR`, `/AS`, `/VRES`. This uses 6 inputs.
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Slot 7 (/TIME): Pin B30. Required for accurate emulation of hardware
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] registers/mappers.
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Slot 8 (/MRES): Pin B2. Distinct from `/VRES` (B27). `/MRES` is the master reset
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] line; while often tied to VRES, monitoring it separately fills the last slot on U6.
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Ignored Pins:
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Audio L/R (B1, B3): Analog pass-throughs, safely ignored for digital emulation.
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Power/Ground: Accounted for.
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 18:59:17 [gemini-3-pro] With `/TIME` and `/MRES` added to U6, the digital interface is complete.
