2025-11-30 19:04:03 [nitro@ryzen5] oh so audio is in not out
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the Sega Megadrive cartridge slot has two analog audio pins (B1 and B3) which allow the
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] cartridge to mix audio into the console's main output (used by games like Virtua Racing).
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] Missing Pins / Audio Logic
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Missing: Pin B1 (Audio Mono/Left) and B3 (Audio Right).
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] • Direction: These are Inputs to the Console, meaning the Cartridge (RP2040) must
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] Output to them if you want to generate sound.
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] • RP2040 Implementation: Since the RP2040 outputs digital, you would typically use
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] PWM on a spare GPIO with an RC filter (Resistor+Capacitor) to create the analog signal sent
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] to B1/B3.
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] Analog Inputs (ADC) on RP2040
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] If you intend to sample signals (e.g. if this is a sniffer rather than a cart emulator),
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] the RP2040 has specific pins for Analog to Digital Conversion (ADC):
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  GP26 (ADC0): Available (Currently `SPARE_0`).
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  GP27 (ADC1): Available (Currently `SPARE_1`).
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  GP28 (ADC2): Occupied. Currently assigned to `MD_CLK`.
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] To use 3 analog inputs, you would need to move `MD_CLK` to a different digital pin (e.g., GP0 or
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] GP1 if UART isn't needed).
2025-11-30 19:04:44 [gemini-3-pro] 
