2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the updated documentation and clean JavaScript file for Project Crumpet, including the PWM
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] audio output pins.
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] Regarding your question about missing pins:
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] • Audio Inputs (B1/B3): The standard Megadrive cartridge port (Pin B1) is a Mono
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] "Audio In" line that mixes with the console's audio. Stereo injection via the cartridge slot is not
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] standard on the edge connector. To get stereo, you might need to mix Left/Right passively into B1
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] or route audio externally.
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] • Shift Register Capacity: You have 48 bits of input capacity (6x8).
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Address (23 bits) + Data (16 bits) = 39 bits.
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Remaining capacity: 9 bits.
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Control signals listed: `/CE`, `/OE`, `/LWR`, `/UWR`, `/AS`, `/VRES`, `/TIME`, `/MRES` (8
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro] bits).
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Total Used: 47 bits.
2025-11-30 19:10:04 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Spare: 1 bit (U3 input H is currently grounded/unused).
