2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] A 16bit Sega Megadrive RP2040 hookup on plated 64 finger edge connector.
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] [USB] ─ RP2040 ─ 10kΩ series resistors ─ 6×74HC165 and 2x74LVC245 ─ cartridge port ─ [Megadrive]
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] description
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] Gangs of shift registers transport data between millenium.
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] basic rom cartridge logic
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] The RP2040 PIO empties shift registers in parallel = 8 cycles.
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] With address decoded and confirmation write cycle required, 16 bit data is prepared for bus.
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] The PIO writes 8 bits, latches the Low byte, writes 8 bits, latches the High byte, then enables
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] Output (/OE).
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-11-30 19:34:25 [gemini-3-pro] bom
