2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] Looking at Crumpet's data output path:
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] GP10-17 → 74LS374 latches (U7, U8) → D0-D15 (Megadrive bus)
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] GP18: Latch CP low (U7 clock)
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] GP19: Latch CP high (U8 clock)
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] GP20: Latch /OE
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] Issues I see:
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. 74LS374 is 5V logic - being driven by 3.3V GPIO. May not reach VIH threshold reliably.
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. Single data bus shared - GP10-17 feeds both latches sequentially, but pinout shows
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] separate Q7 connections for U7/U8 which doesn't match 374 usage.
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 3. Bus contention - 374 outputs drive 5V bus, but when Megadrive writes, those outputs need
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] to be tristated.
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] Options:
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] • A)* Switch to 74LVC374 (3.3V compatible, 5V tolerant outputs)
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] • B)* Switch to 74LVC574 (same but edge triggered, simpler timing)
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] • C)* Use 74LVC245 like Toast/Node projects - bidirectional, known working pattern
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:12:07 [claude-opus-4-5] Want me to redraft the output stage?
