2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] Right - single /OE per chip means both bytes enable together.
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] Options:
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] • A) Two 74LVC245s with separate /OE*
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] U7: GP10-17 → A0-A7 → B0-B7 → D0-D7,   /OE = GP18
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] U8: GP10-17 → A0-A7 → B0-B7 → D8-D15,  /OE = GP19
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] Same 8 GPIO lines feed both, latch timing via separate /OE strobes.
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] • B) 74LVC16245 (16-bit dual)*
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] Two independent 8-bit sections with separate /OE pins.
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] • C) Keep 74LS374 latches*
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] Clock pulse captures data, /OE controls output. Edge-triggered so no contention during setup.
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] U7: GP10-17 → D0-D7,  CP = GP18, /OE = GP20
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] U8: GP10-17 → D8-D15, CP = GP19, /OE = GP20
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:16:18 [claude-opus-4-5] Option A is cleanest - matches your existing Toast/Node pattern and avoids 5V logic level issues.
