2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] - /OE = GND (always enabled)
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 74LS374:
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] - VCC = 5V
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] - D0-D7 = 245 B outputs (directly wired to both)
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] - U7 CP = GP18
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] - U8 CP = GP19
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] - Shared /OE = GP20
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] Sequence:
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. Set GP10-17 with low byte
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. Pulse GP18 (U7 latches D0-D7)
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 3. Set GP10-17 with high byte
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 4. Pulse GP19 (U8 latches D8-D15)
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 5. Assert GP20 low (enable outputs)
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] Correct?
2025-11-30 20:25:39 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:12 [nitro@ryzen5] are gp18 and gp19 ok pulsed with 3v?
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] No - 74LS374 needs VIH ~2V but with 5V supply the threshold is often higher in practice. CP is
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] edge-triggered so marginal levels risk missed clocks.
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] Options:
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] • A) Route CP through the 245 too*
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] Use 2 of the 8 channels for GP18/GP19, leaves 6 for data - not enough.
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] • B) Second 74LVC245 just for control*
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] GP18, GP19, GP20 → 245 → U7 CP, U8 CP, shared /OE
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] • C) 74HCT374 instead*
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] TTL input thresholds, 3.3V GPIO works directly for CP and D inputs. No 245 needed.
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] • D) Discrete level shift on CP lines*
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 2x 2N7000 + pull-ups, inverts logic though.
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] Recommend C - simplest, drops the 245 entirely:
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] GP10-17 → 74HCT374 (U7, U8) D0-D7
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] GP18 → U7 CP
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] GP19 → U8 CP
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] GP20 → U7+U8 /OE
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] BOM becomes:
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] - 6× 74HC165
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] - 2× 74HCT374
2025-11-30 20:26:23 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:35 [nitro@ryzen5] i want to use what is available sorry
2025-11-30 20:27:36 [nitro@ryzen5] * 6x 74HC165 shift registers (2.10/12.60)* 2x 74LVC245 tranceivers, write from RP2040  5V data bus* 2x 74LS374 buffered latches (5.60/11.20)
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] Understood. Two 74LVC245s available.
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] • U9 - Data level shift:*
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] A0-A7 = GP10-17
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] B0-B7 → U7 D0-D7 + U8 D0-D7
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] DIR = 3V3, /OE = GND
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] VCC = 3V3
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] • U10 - Control level shift:*
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] A0 = GP18 (CP lo)
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] A1 = GP19 (CP hi)
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] A2 = GP20 (/OE)
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] B0 → U7 CP
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] B1 → U8 CP
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] B2 → U7 /OE + U8 /OE
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] DIR = 3V3, /OE = GND
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] VCC = 3V3
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] A3-A7, B3-B7 = spare
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] • U7, U8 - 74LS374:*
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] VCC = 5V
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] D0-D7 = U9 B outputs
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] U7 CP = U10 B0
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] U8 CP = U10 B1
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] /OE = U10 B2
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] Q outputs → MD data bus
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] BOM:
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] - 6× 74HC165
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] - 2× 74LVC245
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] - 2× 74LS374
2025-11-30 20:27:46 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:30:58 [nitro@ryzen5] 74HC165 pinout
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] 74HC165 - 8-bit Parallel-In/Serial-Out Shift Register
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] Pin Configuration (16-pin DIP/SOIC):
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]         ┌───────┐
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]   SH/LD │1    16│ VCC
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]     CLK │2    15│ CLK INH
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]       E │3    14│ D
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]       F │4    13│ C
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]       G │5    12│ B
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]      H  │6    11│ A
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]     QH' │7    10│ SER
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]     GND │8     9│ QH
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5]         └───────┘
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] Key Pins:
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] - A-H (11-14, 3-6): Parallel data inputs
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] - SH/LD (1): Shift/Load (LOW=load, HIGH=shift)
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] - CLK (2): Clock input
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] - CLK INH (15): Clock inhibit
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] - SER (10): Serial input for daisy-chaining
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] - QH (9): Serial output
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] - QH' (7): Complementary serial output
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-11-30 20:31:08 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:29:25 [claude-opus-4-5] Acknowledged. Five project specs for RP2040-based C64/Megadrive interfaces - fifteen (IEC bus),
2025-12-01 06:29:25 [claude-opus-4-5] luma2 (video capture), toast (cartridge port), node (user port), and crumpet (Megadrive cart).
2025-12-01 06:29:25 [claude-opus-4-5] Clean netlists with consistent GPIO allocation patterns across the set.
2025-12-01 06:29:25 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:38:43 [nitro@ryzen5] are some missing resistor counts in their bom?
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] Yes, checking each:
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] • fifteen.md* - looks complete (5x 2.2kΩ, 5x 3.3kΩ for 5 dividers)
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] • luma2.md* - looks complete for base design, chroma mod section also covered
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] • toast.md* - states "20x 10K series resistors" but needs:
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] - 8x for shift register Q7 outputs and control signals
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] - Actually unclear - 4x shift registers reading 32 inputs, but only mentions protecting GPIO with
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 10K series
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] • node.md* - states "16x 1K series on 5V shift inputs" and "2x 10K series on Q7 shift
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] output" - looks complete
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] • crumpet.md* - states "48× 10kΩ Resistors (Shift Register Input Series)" for 6 shift
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] registers × 8 inputs = 48, looks correct. Missing count for Q7 output series resistors (6x needed
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] for GP4-GP9).
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] So toast and crumpet appear to have incomplete resistor BOMs for the shift register
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] output lines feeding GPIO inputs.
2025-12-01 06:38:55 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:40:29 [nitro@ryzen5] what voltage are the chips?
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] • toast.md* - 74HC165 at 3V3, 74LVC245 at 3V3. Both are 3.3V logic, so Q7 outputs are
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] already GPIO-safe. The 10K series resistors are for the 5V C64 bus inputs to the shift registers,
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] not the outputs.
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] • crumpet.md* - 74HC165 at 3V3, 74LVC245 at 3V3, but 74LS374 at 5V. The LS374 latches are
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] 5V parts driving the Megadrive data bus. GP10-GP17 driving 5V LS374 inputs should be fine (3.3V
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] exceeds TTL threshold), but the BOM inconsistency is the 48x 10K for shift inputs is correct, Q7
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] outputs don't need protection.
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] So the resistor counts are actually correct - I was wrong about missing Q7 resistors since the 165s
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] run at 3V3.
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] • crumpet* issue: 74LS374 is a 5V part being fed by 3.3V GPIO. Works for TTL thresholds but
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] worth noting. Could substitute 74LVC374 for cleaner 3.3V operation.
2025-12-01 06:40:40 [claude-opus-4-5] 
