2025-12-01 07:13:21 [nitro@ryzen5] the fifteen could do gba network similar with commodore serial bus properties?
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] Yes, very similar topology:
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] ╭─────────────┬─────────────────┬─────────────────╮
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Property   │  C64 IEC        │  GBA Link       │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] ├─────────────┼─────────────────┼─────────────────┤
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Voltage    │  5V             │  3.3V           │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Pins       │  6              │  6              │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Topology   │  Bus (daisy)    │  Bus (daisy)    │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Clock      │  Open drain     │  Push-pull      │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Data       │  Open drain     │  Push-pull      │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Protocol   │  Async bit-bang │  SPI-like       │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Multi-drop │  Yes (30 devs)  │  Yes (4 devs)   │
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] ╰─────────────┴─────────────────┴─────────────────╯
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] Key difference: IEC is open-drain (any device can hold line low), GBA link is push-pull
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] master/slave.
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] A "fifteen-gba" variant would be simpler:
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] - No level shifting (3.3V native)
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] - No FETs needed
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] - Just direct GPIO + two 6-pin sockets
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] Could even be dual-purpose board with both DIN-6 (IEC) and GBA link sockets, active circuit
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] selected by jumper or detection.
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] Want a spec drafted?
2025-12-01 07:13:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
