2025-12-01 07:18:54 [nitro@ryzen5] from grok online
2025-12-01 07:18:55 [nitro@ryzen5] The "EXT connector" on the original Sega Mega Drive (also known as Genesis Model 1) refers to the 9-pin DE-9 (DB9) female port on the rear of early Model 1 consoles, all Japanese Mega Drive Model 1 units, TeraDrive, and Wondermega.consolemods.orgIt's electrically identical to the front controller ports (which are male DE-9), but female and gender-flipped to prevent incorrect connections. It supports parallel I/O (like a third controller port) or serial mode for 5V TTL communication (not RS-232), used primarily by the Japan-only Mega Modem for online play.consolemods.orgStandard pinout (female connector at console, pins numbered looking into the port):Pin	Function (Parallel/Controller Mode)	Function (Serial Mode)1	Up	-2	Down	-3	Left / Ground	-4	Right / Ground	-5	+5V	-6	Button B (3-btn) / A (6-btn) / TX	TX7	Select (thumbler/mode)	-8	Ground	Ground9	Button C/Start / RX	RX
