2025-12-01 07:41:27 [nitro@ryzen5] no breadboard, wire to wire, whats that called?
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Point-to-point wiring, or "dead bug" style if ICs are flipped legs-up.
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] For luma2 with LM319 DIP packages, you could also use:
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - Perfboard/stripboard (no etching)
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - IC socket with flying leads
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - Manhattan style (pads glued to copper ground plane)
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 07:41:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Point-to-point keeps it simple for a one-off prototype with few components.
