2025-12-01 08:41:04 [nitro@ryzen5] a tidy summary of the designs for inclusion in the vintagekids doc
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] # products
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] ## luma2
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] C64 composite video capture via LM319 comparators.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 2-bit greyscale, 320x200 @ 50Hz. Optional chroma/audio mods.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] ## fifteen
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] Triple network bridge: C64 IEC serial, GBA link, Megadrive EXT.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] Point-to-point wiring, no PCB required.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] ## waffle
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] GBA cartridge interface. 32-pin, 3.3V native.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] Direct GPIO connection, simplest PCB.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] ## node
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] C64 user port interface. 24-pin edge connector.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 8-bit parallel + serial via shift registers.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] ## toast
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] C64 expansion port interface. 44-pin edge connector.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] Full bus access via shift registers and FETs.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] ## crumpet
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] Megadrive cartridge interface. 64-pin edge connector.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 16-bit bus via shift registers and latches.
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:41:15 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:34 [nitro@ryzen5] a nine product, simple joystick cable to 10 pin header, automation for all joy
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] ## autojoy
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] Atari/C64 joystick adapter. DE-9 to 10-pin header.
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] Direct GPIO for Up, Down, Left, Right, Fire. No level shifting (active low to GND).
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] pin,de9,function,gpio
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 1,1,Up,GP2
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 2,2,Down,GP3
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 3,3,Left,GP4
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 4,4,Right,GP5
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 5,5,POT Y,GP26 (ADC)
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 6,6,Fire,GP6
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 7,7,+5V,VBUS
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 8,8,GND,GND
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 9,9,POT X,GP27 (ADC)
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 10,-,Fire 2,GP7
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] Simple passive cable - directly connects to Pico GPIO with internal pull-ups enabled. Active low
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] signals, no resistors needed (joystick switches to GND).
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] POT lines optional for paddle/analog support via ADC.
2025-12-01 08:53:45 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:10 [nitro@ryzen5] how difficult to add a passthrough for cartridges in crumpetac
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] Passthrough adds complexity:
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] aspect,difficulty,notes
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] mechanical,high,64-pin edge connector socket on top of PCB
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] routing,medium,all 64 signals need traces to both Pico interface and passthrough
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] timing,high,must not add significant delay to bus signals
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] buffering,optional,could sniff passively or actively intercept
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] Options:
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. Passive sniff - just parallel all lines to passthrough, shift registers read-only.
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] Simplest but can't inject data.
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. Active intercept - bus switches (74LVC4245 or similar) to isolate/insert. Complex,
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] timing critical.
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 3. Pass-through socket only - no Pico interaction with cart signals, just mechanical.
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] Easiest but limited use.
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] Main challenge is the 64-pin card edge socket sourcing - less common than the finger plating.
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] JLCPCB do stock some.
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] Worth it? Depends on use case - ROM dumping, save state capture, or full cart emulation with
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] original cart as fallback?
2025-12-01 09:30:27 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:41 [nitro@ryzen5] developer tool
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] For developer tool (debugging, ROM patching, save hacking):
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] feature,passthrough benefit
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] ROM intercept,patch reads on-the-fly
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] RAM snoop,watch game state
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] save capture,dump SRAM to USB
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] breakpoints,halt on address match
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] trace logging,record bus activity
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] hybrid boot,load from Pico then handoff to cart
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] Passive sniff gets you trace logging and save capture. Active intercept needed for ROM patching and
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] breakpoints.
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] Suggest two-stage approach:
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. crumpet v1 - current design, no passthrough, full cart emulation
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. crumpet v2 - add passthrough socket, active bus switching
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] v1 proves the timing and PIO code. v2 adds passthrough once basics work.
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] Passthrough socket BOM addition:
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 1x 64-pin card edge connector socket (female, 2.54mm pitch)
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 2x 74LVC4245 (quad bus switch) - if active intercept needed
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] Start with v1?
2025-12-01 09:33:57 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:37:57 [nitro@ryzen5] not too many gpio available to enable and disable user cart
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] Right. GPIO budget already tight on crumpet:
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] function,gpio count
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] shift CLK + SH/LD,2
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] shift Q7 x6,6
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] latch D0-D7,8
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] latch CP lo/hi + /OE,3
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] /DTACK + /CART FETs,2
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] CLK input,1
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] audio PWM,2
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] UART,2
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] total,26
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] Passthrough bus switching needs control lines per bus segment:
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] bus,width,switch IC,enable pins
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] A0-A23,24,3x 74LVC4245,3
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] D0-D15,16,2x 74LVC4245,2
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] control,8,1x 74LVC4245,1
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] total,,6,6
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] No spare GPIO for 6 more enables.
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] Options:
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. I2C GPIO expander - adds latency
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. Shift register for enables - reuse existing shift CLK, add one more 74HC595
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 3. Fixed passthrough - directly parallel, no switching (passive sniff only)
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] Option 3 simplest - passthrough always connected, Pico just listens. Can't intercept but can log
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] and dump. Good enough for dev tool?
2025-12-01 09:38:11 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:39:20 [nitro@ryzen5] no it needs to be able to enable passive and then disable to drive
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] Need one GPIO to switch between modes:
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] mode,user cart,pico drives
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] passive,enabled,disabled
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] active,disabled,enabled
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] Single control line to all bus switches - directly or via inverter.
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] GP_SWITCH (1 GPIO)
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5]   │
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5]   ├─► 74LVC4245 /OE_A (user cart side)
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5]   │
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5]   └─► inverted ─► 74LVC4245 /OE_B (pico side)
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] One GPIO high = cart enabled, pico tristated.
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] One GPIO low = cart tristated, pico drives.
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] Could steal GP25 (LED) or repurpose one audio PWM if stereo not needed.
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] Or add 74HC595 shift register for enables - uses existing shift CLK/SH_LD, just one more Q7 daisy
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] chain. Adds latency but no new GPIO.
2025-12-01 09:40:01 [claude-opus-4-5] 
