2025-12-01 12:07:14 [nitro@ryzen5] what is basic input count for buttons etc
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Counting digital inputs across all ports:
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] ╭─────────────────────┬─────────┬──────────────────────────────╮
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] │  Port               │  Count  │  Buttons                     │
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] ├─────────────────────┼─────────┼──────────────────────────────┤
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] │  DB9 Atari/C64      │  4×     │  5 each (U/D/L/R/Fire) = 20  │
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] │  PSX DualShock      │  2×     │  14 each (via SPI) = 28      │
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] │  DA15 Neo Geo       │  1×     │  10 (D-pad + 6 buttons)      │
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] │  DB19 Soundblaster  │  1×     │  4 buttons                   │
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] │  DE9 Apple IIe      │  1×     │  5 (U/D/L/R/Fire)            │
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] ╰─────────────────────┴─────────┴──────────────────────────────╯
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] • Digital total: ~67 buttons*
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Plus analog:
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - 2× PSX sticks (4 axes each) = 8 axes via SPI
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - Soundblaster = 4 axes (555 timing)
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - Apple paddles = 2 axes (ADC or 558 timing)
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] • Analog: ~14 axes*
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] PSX is efficient - 28 buttons + 8 axes on 4 GPIOs (SPI protocol).
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] The 4× DB9 inputs are the GPIO hogs at 20 lines. Shift registers would collapse that to 3 GPIOs.
2025-12-01 12:07:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:18 [nitro@ryzen5] so 10 shift registers to keep it tidy?
