2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] • GPIO usage:*
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] GP2, shift CLK
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] GP3, shift SH/LD
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] GP4, shift Q7 (daisy chain all 10)
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Or parallel Q7 for speed:
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] GP4-GP13, shift Q7 × 10
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 3 GPIOs chained vs 12 parallel. Chained is 80 clocks per read, parallel is 8.
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] PSX stays on dedicated SPI (GP22-24, GP28).
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] ADC for paddles (GP26-27).
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Leaves plenty free for output driving.
2025-12-01 12:08:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 12:09:31 [nitro@ryzen5] for safely driving the output ports
