2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] Hi. I have reviewed the Project Joy documentation. There are significant conflicts between
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] the GPIO Allocation section and the Wiring section that need resolution before
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] layout.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] Critical Issues
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  GPIO Conflict (GP5 - GP9):
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Allocation Section: Lists GP5 as `FET SEL`, and GP6–8 as `MUX S0–S2`.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Wiring Section: Lists GP5, GP6, GP7, and GP8 as distinct Data Inputs (Q7)
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] for Shift Registers U2, U3, U4, and U5.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Impact: You cannot drive the Multiplexers/FETs and read separate shift registers on
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] the same pins.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Shift Register Topology:
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   The wiring currently describes a Parallel configuration (consuming 5 GPIOs for
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] data).
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Recommendation: Use a Daisy Chain configuration. Connect `Q7` of U1 to `DS`
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] (Serial Input) of U2, and so on. This requires only 1 GPIO (GP4) for all 5 shift registers,
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] freeing up GP5–GP8 for the MUX and Select lines.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Missing Netlist Details:
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   CD4051 Analog Mux: The BOM includes them, and GP26/27 are assigned to ADCs, but the
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] netlist does not define the connections for the Mux Select lines (S0-S2) or the Joystick
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] Potentiometer inputs.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Sega Select: The "Multiple select cycles" feature requires a dedicated output line
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] to toggle Pin 7 on the Sega ports. This is alluded to as `fet SEL out` on GP5 but needs to be
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] explicit in the netlist.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Voltage Levels:
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro]     *   74HC165 powered at 3.3V reading 5V logic: Ensure the 10kΩ series resistors mentioned in the
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] summary are strictly applied to limit current into the input protection diodes.
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] Suggested Resolution
2025-12-01 13:39:29 [gemini-3-pro] 
