2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Hi, I have reviewed the WIP documentation for Project Joy.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Here is a summary of the issues found in the netlist and logic, specifically regarding the Shift
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Register chaining and Voltage compliance.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Shift Register Daisy Chain (Logic Direction)
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] The netlist for the 74HC165 cascade appears to be wired backwards for a standard "Shift In"
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] configuration where `U1` is closest to the RP2040.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Current (Incorrect) logic:*
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • `U1.9 (Q7)` → `U2.10 (DS)`
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • `U5.9 (Q7)` → `GND` (Shorting an output to ground)
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Correction:*
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Data must flow towards the Pico. `U1` feeds the Pico, `U2` feeds `U1`, etc. The last chip
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] (`U5`) should have its Serial Input (`DS`) grounded (or tied High), and its Output (`Q7`) feeds the
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] previous chip.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Corrected Chain:
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Pico GP4 (MISO) <── U1.9 (Q7)
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro]                     U1.10 (DS) <── U2.9 (Q7)
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro]                     U2.10 (DS) <── U3.9 (Q7)
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro]                     ...
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro]                     U5.10 (DS) <── GND
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Voltage Levels & Protection
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • 74HC165 Power: You have `VCC` tied to `3V3`.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Input Levels: Vintage joysticks/consoles operate at 5V.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Risk: Feeding 5V signals (from the joystick port) directly into a 74HC165 powered by 3.3V
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] exceeds the input voltage tolerance (V_CC + 0.5V).
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Fix: You need current limiting series resistors (e.g., 1kΩ - 10kΩ) on the joystick inputs
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] (P0-P7) to allow the 74HC165 internal clamping diodes to handle the 5V safely, similar to your
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Project Toast design.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Missing Connections
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Sega Select (Multiplexer): `GP5` is allocated as `fet SEL out (Sega)`, but it is not
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] listed in the DB9 header pinouts or the netlist. Sega controllers require this pin (usually DB9 Pin
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 7) to toggle High/Low to read the full 12-button state.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Analog Mux (CD4051): The BOM lists 2x CD4051, and GPIOs are allocated for `ADC0/1` and
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] `MUX S0-S2`, but the netlist does not define which DB9 pins (Pot X/Y) connect to the Mux inputs
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] (Y0-Y7).
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 4. Apple II Paddle Logic
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Apple II paddles are variable resistors (0-150kΩ), not voltage dividers.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • To read these via ADC, you need a pull-up resistor (e.g., 3.3kΩ to 3.3V) on the Mux Common line
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] or individual inputs to create a voltage divider the ADC can read. The current BOM/Netlist does not
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] show this bias resistor.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 5. BOM Discrepancies
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] • Resistors: BOM lists "10x 10kΩ resistor (pull-ups)".
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro]     *   With 5 chips x 8 inputs = 40 inputs.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Atari/C64 joysticks switch to Ground. You need pull-ups on all inputs unless relying on
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] internal MCU/Shift register weak pull-ups (HC165 usually requires external pull-ups or inputs will
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] float). 10 resistors is insufficient for 40 inputs.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] Summary
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] The project needs a logic reversal on the shift register chain and specific attention to 5V-to-3.3V
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] input protection to avoid damaging the RP2040 or the logic chips.
2025-12-01 13:58:36 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] Here is a review of the Project Joy work-in-progress document.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] Logic and Netlist Review
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • 1. Analog Multiplexers (Missing Wiring)*
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] The BOM lists 2x CD4051 and GPIOs are allocated for MUX S0-S2 and ADC0/1, but the Wiring
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] section completely omits the CD4051 connections.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • You need to map the Joystick Potentiometer pins (DB9 Pin 5 and 9) to the CD4051 inputs (Y0-Y7).
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Ensure the Common Output (Z) of the muxes connects to GP26/GP27.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • 2. Shift Register Chain*
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] The daisy-chain logic in the final revision is correct for data flowing towards the RP2040:
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] `GND -> U5(DS) -> U5(Q7) -> U4(DS)... -> U1(Q7) -> GP4`
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Observation: Ensure U5 Pin 10 is pulled to the logic state you want to shift in when the
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] chain runs out of data (usually logic 0/GND is fine, but strictly defining it prevents floating
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] bits).
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • 3. Voltage Levels (3.3V vs 5V)*
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] You are powering the 74HC165s with 3V3.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Passive Controllers: Works fine for Atari/C64 (switches to ground).
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Active Controllers: Sega Genesis/Megadrive controllers are active 5V devices. Feeding a
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] logic High (5V) into a 74HC165 powered at 3.3V violates Vin \le VCC. This can damage the
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] shift registers or the RP2040 via current injection.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Fix: Run the 74HC165s at 5V and place a voltage divider (or level shifter) on the
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] final `Q7 -> GP4` line.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • 4. Sega Select Line*
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • GPIO: GP5 is allocated as `fet SEL out (Sega)`.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Wiring: The netlist does not show the connection from GP5 to the DB9 connectors.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Requirement: Connect GP5 (likely via a level shifter or open drain FET if the controllers
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] are 5V) to Pin 7 of the Sega input ports to allow multiplexing between D-Pad and Buttons.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • 5. Latch Mapping (Remote Drive)*
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] The bit-packing across U9, U10, and U11 is efficient but complex:
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Joy 2 is split between U9 (Q5-Q7) and U10 (Q0-Q1).
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Joy 4 is split between U10 (Q7) and U11 (Q0-Q3).
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Ensure your software abstraction layer handles these split masks correctly when writing to the
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] latches.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] Minor Notes
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • U11 Wiring: The list for U11 stops at Q3. Q4-Q7 should be explicitly marked NC or
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] grounded if unused inputs (though these are outputs on a 374, so NC is fine).
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] • Apple II: U5 inputs P0-P2 are mapped to Apple buttons. Ensure the Apple II joystick
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] connector provides a ground reference compatible with the board.
2025-12-01 14:02:56 [gemini-3-pro] 
