2025-12-01 15:20:15 [nitro@ryzen5] how about the latch, it only needs to pull low or float
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] Correct - the latches only need to pull low or float:
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] • 74LS374 Output Behavior:*
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - Output LOW: Actively drives 0V to ground joystick line
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - Output HIGH: High impedance (floating) - joystick pull-up resistor provides +5V
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] • Why this works:*
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - Joystick inputs have internal/external pull-ups to +5V
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - Latch LOW = button "pressed" (active low)
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - Latch floating = button "released" (pull-up makes it HIGH)
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] • Perfect for:*
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - Driving active-low joystick inputs
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - No need for active HIGH drive capability
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] - Simple open-drain-like behavior
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] The design correctly uses latches that can only sink current, not source it, which matches the
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] active-low joystick requirements.
2025-12-01 15:20:25 [deepseek-chat] 
