2025-12-01 15:37:22 [nitro@ryzen5] gemini can you help?
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the details for the missing Apple II connections, the RP2040 button usage, and the
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] requested pinouts.
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 1. RP2040 SEL Button
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] The `BOOTSEL` button on the Pico is primarily for entering bootloader mode. While it can be
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] read by software during runtime (by toggling the flash CS pin), it interrupts flash execution and
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] can be tricky to use as a regular input.
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Recommendation: Use GP22* (which is currently free) for a dedicated tactile "Mode
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] Select" button. This allows you to cycle through mapping modes (e.g., 4-player independent vs.
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 2-player split) without resetting the board.
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Apple II "Resonators" (Annunciators)
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] You are likely referring to the Annunciators (AN0–AN3). These are digital outputs from the
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] Apple II used to control complex peripherals (like the Koala Pad or digital joysticks).
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Yes, we can use the spare outputs on Latch U8 (Q4–Q7)* to drive these pins. This
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] makes your hub capable of hosting advanced Apple II peripherals.
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 3. WS2812B Meaning
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] The "B" in WS2812B stands for the Improved Version (Generation B).
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Protection: It has reverse polarity protection (won't burn out immediately if wired
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] backwards).
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Pins: It uses a 4-pin structure (VDD, GND, DIN, DOUT) compared to the 6-pin structure of
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] the older WS2812.
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] • Brightness: It offers better brightness consistency.
2025-12-01 15:38:28 [gemini-3-pro] 
