2025-12-01 15:39:37 [nitro@ryzen5] The Apple 2 pinout, as csv plase
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the information on the addressable LEDs, the Apple II pinouts, and the utilization of the
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] remaining latch pins.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] WS2812B
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Protocol Name: Single-wire NRZ (Non-Return-to-Zero) asynchronous serial. Often referred
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] to generically as "NeoPixel" (Adafruit trade name) or "Addressable LED".
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] • What is B: The 'B' stands for the specific package revision.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro]     *   WS2812: Original 6-pin component.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro]     *   WS2812B: Improved 4-pin component (integrated protection, better brightness,
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] separate power/control layout not required).
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] RP2040 SEL Button
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] The BOOTSEL button on the Pico can be used as a user input, but it is not a standard GPIO.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] Reading it requires the code to briefly disable interrupts and talk to the flash memory chip (CS
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] pin), which can cause glitches in timing-critical applications (like bit-banging video or
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] high-speed serial).
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Verdict: Good for "Mode Select" or "Setup" at startup. Bad for "Fire Button" during
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] gameplay.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] U8 Latch & Apple II "Resonators"
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] You are likely thinking of Annunciators.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Annunciators (AN0-AN3): These are digital Outputs from the Apple II (used
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] to turn on stepper motors or switch banks). Since U8 is an output from the RP2040, you
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] cannot drive the Apple's outputs.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Buttons (SW0-SW2): These are digital Inputs to the Apple II.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Utilization: Yes, you can use U8 Q4 and U8 Q5 to drive Apple II
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] SW0 and SW1. This allows the RP2040 to "press the buttons" on the Apple II.
2025-12-01 15:40:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
