2025-12-01 15:46:22 [nitro@ryzen5] 4 more analog ins, any ideas?
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] The "Apple resonators" are the Annunciators (AN0-AN3). These are digital outputs from an
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] Apple II normally used to switch stepper motors (in disk drives) or handle special joystick
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] features. If we are the host, we can drive them to support complex controllers.
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] To get 4 more analog inputs, we can utilize the unused channels on the second CD4051 (U10).
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] It only uses 4 channels for the Apple paddles, leaving 4 spare.
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:47:40 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the updated configuration.
