2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the "Resonators" on the Apple II are called Annunciators (AN0, AN1, etc.). These are
2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] digital outputs from the computer (or in this case, Project Joy) used to switch modes or drive
2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] simple electronics in the controller.
2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] We can map GP22 to a spare header or sync line, as `BOOTSEL` handles the button press logic
2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] internally.
2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 15:53:54 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the updated configuration with U8 driving the Apple Annunciators.
