2025-12-01 16:06:38 [nitro@ryzen5] Shared OE means data always latched, latches pull low or float.
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] The 'B' in WS2812B indicates the updated silicon revision (Generation B). It improved on
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] the original WS2812 by reducing the pin count from 6 to 4 (integrating power/ground) and adding
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] reverse polarity protection and better brightness consistency.
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the finalized specification for Project Joy.
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Apple II Outputs: Mapped the "Resonators" (Annunciators) to the spare bits on the third
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] latch (U8).
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Spare Analog: The 4 remaining channels on the second multiplexer (U10) are broken out to
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] an auxiliary header.
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] • GP22: Assigned to Apple Strobe, a dedicated signal often used for latching data
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] on the Apple game port.
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Output Enable: Tied `GP21` to `/OE`. While 74LS374s are totem-pole (push-pull), driving a
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] Logic 1 (5V) into a pulled-up console input is standard practice. To "float" the bus completely,
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] toggle GP21 High.
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] Project Joy
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] An RP2040 multi-joystick hub. Reads standard DB9 controllers and drives vintage computer ports via
2025-12-01 16:07:59 [gemini-3-pro] DE9 cables.
