2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Acknowledged. I've reviewed the shared project files:
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - fifteen.md - IEC serial bus interface with GBA link and Megadrive EXT ports
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - luma2.md - Composite video capture using LM319 comparators
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - toast.md - C64 cartridge port interface (44-pin)
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - node.md - C64 user port interface (24-pin)
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - crumpet.md - Megadrive cartridge interface (64-pin)
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - designs.md - Project summary and parts overview
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - vintagekid.md - Product listing
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] - joy.md - Multi-joystick hub with analog support
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] Consistent design patterns across projects: shift registers for input, latches/transceivers for
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] output, 2N7000 FETs for open-drain signals, voltage dividers for clock inputs.
2025-12-01 16:09:36 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:09:55 [nitro@ryzen5] is Shared OE means data always latched, latches pull low or float. clear in joy?
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] No, it's unclear. The statement is ambiguous about:
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. Whether shared /OE means all three 74LS374 latches (U6, U7, U8) share GP21
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. How "pull low or float" works - 74LS374 outputs are totem-pole, not open-drain
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] If you want active-low-or-float behaviour on joystick outputs, you'd need either:
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] - 74LS374 driving 2N7000 gates (adds 24 FETs)
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] - Replace with open-drain latches like 74HC05 or similar
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] Should I clarify the intent in the document?
2025-12-01 16:10:03 [claude-opus-4-5] 
