2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] No, none of those are open-drain latches.
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] The 74HC374 and 74HC573 are both totem-pole output latches - they actively drive high or low.
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] For true open-drain you'd need:
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] - ULN2803 - 8-channel Darlington (sinks only, needs external pull-up)
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] - 74HC05 - Hex inverter, open-drain
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] - 74HC03 - Quad NAND, open-drain
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] Alternatively, keep 74HC374 ($1.59) and add 8× 2N7000 per latch for open-drain conversion. That's
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] the pattern used in your other designs.
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] Or reconsider the requirement - if driving active-low joystick lines that expect passive-high, the
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] 74HC374 with active-low logic might suffice if the target has internal pull-ups.
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] What's the actual target device expecting?
2025-12-01 16:12:38 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:00 [nitro@ryzen5] 74HC04 Hex Inverter IC would work no?
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] No, 74HC04 is totem-pole output, not open-drain.
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] You're thinking of 74HC05 - the open-drain variant of the hex inverter.
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 74HC04: pushes high, pulls low
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 74HC05: floats high, pulls low
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] The 05 isn't in that stock list. You'd need to source it elsewhere or use the 2N7000 approach.
2025-12-01 16:14:07 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:19 [nitro@ryzen5] not available at jaycar
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] Options then:
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 1. 2N7000 per output - already in your BOM, proven pattern from other designs
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 2. ULN2803 - 8-channel Darlington array, commonly available, check Jaycar for "ULN2803" or
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] similar driver array
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 3. Diode + resistor per line - 74HC374 output through diode to bus, external pull-up on bus
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] side (hacky but works)
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] The 2N7000 route is cleanest and consistent with fifteen/toast/node designs. 24 FETs for 3 latches
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] adds ~$4 to BOM.
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] Want me to update joy.md with explicit 2N7000 drivers on latch outputs?
2025-12-01 16:14:32 [claude-opus-4-5] 
