2025-12-01 16:22:43 [nitro@ryzen5] good, what is practical count for 2812 lights on this circuit powered from rp2040
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] Practical limit from Pico USB power: 8-12 LEDs at full brightness.
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] Math:
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] - Pico USB budget: ~500mA total, Pico takes ~50-100mA
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] - WS2812B: 60mA max per LED (20mA × 3 colours)
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] - 400mA ÷ 60mA = ~6 LEDs at full white
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] - At 50% brightness or coloured indicators: 12-16 LEDs safe
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] For 24 status lights you'd need external 5V supply to LED chain.
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] Suggest: 8× WS2812B - one per joystick port (4 in, 4 out), powered from Pico.
2025-12-01 16:22:53 [claude-opus-4-5] 
