2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] # Digital Input Protection
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] ## Shift Register Inputs (5V → 3.3V)
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 74HC165 parallel inputs (40 pins total): 10kΩ series resistors protect against 5V joystick signals.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] Series resistance limits current if GPIO clamping diodes activate.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] * U1-U4: 8 inputs each (32 total) from DB9 joystick ports
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] * U5: 3 inputs from Apple II buttons, 5 NC
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] ## Shift Chain Output (3.3V)
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] GPIO shift data input (GP4): 10kΩ series resistor on U1 Q7 output.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] Chain runs at 3.3V logic - resistor provides ESD protection only.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] ## Analog Inputs
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] CD4051 powered from 3.3V - analog signals clamped to rail.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] Joystick pots typically 0-5V; exceeding 3.3V clips at Pico ADC input.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] Consider voltage divider on pot inputs if full range needed.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] ## Latch Outputs (5V)
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] 74LS374 outputs are 5V TTL driving 2N7000 gates.
2025-12-01 16:24:47 [claude-opus-4-5] No protection needed - FET gates are high impedance.
