2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] Most of these are specific mechanical connectors or ICs that might not be standard stock at general
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] electronics stores.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] ICs & Actives
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • LM319 Dual High-Speed Comparator: (For Luma2)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]        Note:* Jaycar typically stocks the LM339 (Quad), but the LM319 is significantly
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] faster (80ns response vs 1.3µs). You likely need to source the specific LM319 from a distributor
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] like Mouser, DigiKey, or element14 to ensure the video capture works at 50Hz.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • CD4051 Analog Multiplexer: (For Joy)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Jaycar often stocks this (Cat ZC4051), but verify stock levels as you need 2 per board.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] Edge Connectors (Critical)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] These are physically large and pitch-specific.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • 64-pin Card Edge (2x32): (For Crumpet)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Pitch: 2.54mm (0.1").
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • 44-pin Card Edge (2x22): (For Toast)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Pitch: 2.54mm (0.1").
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • 24-pin Card Edge (2x12): (For Node)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Pitch: 3.96mm (0.156").
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]        Important:* The C64 User Port is 3.96mm pitch. Standard 2.54mm connectors will not
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] fit.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] Interface Connectors
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • DIN-6 Socket (DIN 45322): (For Fifteen)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Must be the "Commodore" style arrangement.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • DB9 / DE9 Connectors: (For Joy)
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   4x Male (for remote output) and 4x Female (for input).
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   IDC (Ribbon crimp) style is recommended to save wiring time given the high pin count.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • DIP16 Socket: (For Joy / Apple II port).
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] Passives & Misc
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Resistor Networks (SIP/SIL):
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   You have high counts of 10kΩ resistors (48x for Crumpet alone).
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Sourcing 9-pin isolated resistor networks (8 resistors + 1 common) will
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] significantly reduce board space and soldering time compared to individual axial resistors.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Ribbon Cable (10-way):
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Essential for the Joy project breakouts.
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro] • Raspberry Pi Pico (RP2040):
2025-12-01 18:11:52 [gemini-3-pro]     *   One unit required per project.
