2025-12-01 20:19:01 [nitro@ryzen5] Preview on 2" 320x240 IPS Display Module
2025-12-01 20:19:03 [nitro@ryzen5] new feature
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the assessment for adding the LCD and Stereo Audio to Luma2, along with an
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] explanation of IPS and the Chroma strategy.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 1. What is IPS?
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • IPS (In-Plane Switching)* is a screen technology used in modern LCDs.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Viewing Angles: You can look at the screen from the side, up, or down, and the colors do
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] not invert or wash out (unlike older TN screens).
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Color: It produces much more vibrant and accurate colors.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Relevance: For a retro project, IPS is highly recommended because it mimics the vibrancy
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] of a CRT better than cheap TN panels.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Chroma: Edge Counting vs. More Bits
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] For the C64, Edge Counting via PIO is likely the best approach for this specific hardware.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • How it works: The PIO measures the time distance between the Horizontal Sync and the
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] zero-crossing of the Chroma signal. This determines the phase, which determines the color.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Is it enough? Yes. The C64 only has 16 colors. The phase differences between them are
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] significant enough that a fast PIO counter (~125MHz or overclocked) can distinguish them.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • More Comparators? Adding more comparators (flash ADC style) adds significant component
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] cost and complexity for diminishing returns on an RP2040. The bottleneck is usually the timing
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] resolution of the capture, not the voltage levels, since Chroma is phase-modulated.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 3. GPIO Audit & LCD Selection
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Waveshare 1.14" vs 2.0":*
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • 1.14" (240x135): Too small. You would have to crop or scale down the C64's 320x200 image,
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] losing detail.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • 2.0" IPS (320x240): Perfect fit. You can display the full 320x200 C64 image with
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] a small border for status/UI.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • GPIO Availability:*
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Current Luma2: Uses ~7 pins.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Stereo Audio: Uses 2 pins (ADC).
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • SPI LCD: Uses ~5-6 pins.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Total: ~15 pins used.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Pico Capacity: 26 GPIO available. Status: PLENTY of room.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] Pinout Re-Shuffle
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Critical Note:* Most Pico LCD "Hats" hardwire the screen to specific pins (usually SPI0 on
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] GP16-GP20). Your current Luma2 design uses GP16-GP22 for video input.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] • Action: Move Luma2 video inputs to GP0-GP6* to leave the standard SPI pins free
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] for the LCD.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] Updated Project Luma2 Spec
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] Includes Stereo Audio, 2.0" IPS LCD support, and re-mapped GPIO to avoid SPI conflicts.
2025-12-01 20:20:30 [gemini-3-pro] 
