2025-12-02 07:17:44 [nitro@ryzen5] keep gp0 gp1 for host uart
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] Good point - preserving GP0/GP1 for UART is essential for debugging and communication. Here's the
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] revised GPIO allocation:
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GPIO Allocation (Waffle)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP0:  UART0_TX (Host communication)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP1:  UART0_RX (Host communication)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP2:  SHIFT_CLK (74HC165 chain clock)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP3:  SHIFT_SH_LD (74HC165 shift/load)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP4:  SHIFT_Q7 (Data from shift chain)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP5:  GBA_/CS (Chip Select - timing critical)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP6:  GBA_/RD (Read Strobe - timing critical)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP7:  GBA_/WR (Write Strobe - timing critical)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP8:  BANK_LATCH (Bank switching control)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP9:  SAVE_/CS (Save memory chip select)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP10: SAVE_SCK (Save memory serial clock)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP11: SAVE_SI (Save memory serial in)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP12: SAVE_SO (Save memory serial out)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP13-20: DATA_BUS D0-D7 (via 74LVC245)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP21: GBA_RESET (optional)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP22: GBA_IRQ (optional)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP23: SMPS_MODE (internal)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP24: VBUS_SENSE (internal)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP25: LED (internal)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] GP26-28: Spare/Address extension
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] Design Implications
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] Shift Register Chain (U1-U3)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - U1: Capture A0-A7 + control signals
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - U2: Capture A8-A15 + status signals
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - U3: Capture save memory lines + spare
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - All share GP2 (CLK), GP3 (SH/LD), output to GP4 via chain
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] Critical Timing Paths
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - GP5 (/CS): Direct GPIO for precise timing
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - GP6 (/RD): Direct GPIO for read timing
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - GP7 (/WR): Direct GPIO for write timing
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - These need PIO or tight software control
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] Save Memory Interface
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - GP9-12 provide flexible save memory support
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - Can bit-bang SPI for Flash/EEPROM
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - Direct control for SRAM
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] Bank Switching
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - GP8 latches high address bits (A16-A23)
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - Could use 74HC574 if more bits needed
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] - Alternative: Use spare GPIOs 26-28 for direct bank select
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] Trade-offs
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 1. Speed: Shift registers add latency for address capture
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 2. Flexibility: Direct GPIO on critical signals maintains timing
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 3. Complexity: More direct connections than pure shift register approach
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] This preserves UART while addressing GBA's timing requirements. The hybrid approach (shift
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] registers + direct GPIO) balances IC count with performance.
2025-12-02 07:18:04 [deepseek-chat] 
