2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] GP14: SAVE_SO
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] GP15-22: DATA_BUS D0-D7 (via 74LVC245)
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] GP23-28: Spare/Address extension
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] PIO Advantage
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] With parallel Q7 inputs:
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] - Single clock cycle to read all 3 bytes (24 bits)
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] - 8 cycles to shift in full 24-bit state (vs 24+ cycles daisy chain)
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] - Timing: ~104ns at 8MHz PIO clock (fits GBA timing)
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] PIO Program Concept
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] .program read_gba_bus
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     set pins, 0 [1]    ; SH/LD low (load parallel)
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     set pins, 1        ; SH/LD high (shift mode)
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     mov x, 7           ; 8 bits per register
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] loop:
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     in pins, 3         ; Read 3 bits (GP4,5,6)
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     set pins, 1 [1]    ; Clock high
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     set pins, 0        ; Clock low
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     jmp x-- loop
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat]     push               ; Send 24 bits to FIFO
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] Performance Estimate
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] - Address capture: ~1µs total
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] - Data bus write: Direct via 74LVC245
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] - /CS assertion: Direct GPIO for timing
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] This parallel approach is significantly faster and better suited to GBA timing constraints. Good
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] catch!
2025-12-02 07:19:50 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] The Waffle project appears to be a 3.3V GBA cartridge adapter using similar shift register and
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] transceiver logic as the Toast C64 project, but with key differences:
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] • Key similarities:*
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] - Both use 74HC165 shift registers for input capture
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] - Both use 74LVC245 transceivers for data bus output
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] - Both interface RP2040 with vintage gaming hardware
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] • Key differences:*
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 1. Voltage levels: Waffle is 3.3V native (GBA), while Toast needs 5V interfacing
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 2. Bus architecture: GBA uses multiplexed address/data bus (AD0-AD15), C64 has separate
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] address and data buses
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 3. Control signals: Different sets (GBA: /CS, /RD, /WR; C64: /ROML, /ROMH, /IRQ, etc.)
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 4. Clock speed: GBA PHI ~16.78MHz vs C64 PHI2 ~0.985MHz
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 5. No open-drain drivers: Waffle doesn't need FETs since it's 3.3V to 3.3V
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] • Notable Waffle features:*
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] - Save memory interface (GP11-14) for SRAM/EEPROM/Flash
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] - Bank latch control (GP10) for larger ROMs
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] - Direct control signal connections (GP7-9) without shift registers
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] The Waffle design seems cleaner due to matching voltage levels, though the multiplexed bus adds
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] complexity. Both projects demonstrate clever use of shift registers to expand GPIO capabilities.
2025-12-02 07:23:56 [deepseek-chat] 
