2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] • GBA Cartridge Pinout (input to cartridge):*
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 1. VCC (+3.3V) - Power
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 2. PHI (CPU Clock) - Input to cartridge (~16.78 MHz)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 3. /WR (Write Strobe) - Input to cartridge (active low)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 4. /RD (Read Strobe) - Input to cartridge (active low)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 5. /CS (ROM Chip Select) - Input to cartridge (active low)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 6-21. AD0-AD15 - Bidirectional (address during T1, data during T2)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 22-29. A16-A23 - Input to cartridge (address only, not multiplexed)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 30. /CS2 (Save Memory Chip Select) - Input to cartridge (active low)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 31. GND
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 32. VCC (+3.3V)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] • Summary:*
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] - Input only to cartridge: PHI, /WR, /RD, /CS, A16-A23, /CS2
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] - Bidirectional: AD0-AD15 (multiplexed address/data)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] - Output only from cartridge: None (all pins are either input or bidirectional from GBA
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] perspective)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] • For your Project Muffin:*
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] - GP5 (PHI), GP6 (/WR), GP26 (/RD), GP27 (/CS), GP28 (/CS2) should be inputs to RP2040
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] - GP7-22 (AD0-AD15) need to be bidirectional (input during reads, output during writes)
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] - A16-A23 would come from your shift register (GP2-4) as inputs to RP2040
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] The GBA drives all control signals and upper address lines to the cartridge.
2025-12-02 08:38:54 [deepseek-chat] 
