2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] Based on the provided files, here is an analysis of the pin mapping between the RP2040 and the GBA
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] Cartridge port.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] Hardware Architecture Analysis
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] The GPIO allocation suggests the RP2040 is acting as a GBA Cartridge Emulator (Flashcart)
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] rather than a dumper/writer.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Address/Data Bus (AD0-AD15): The multiplexed low address and data lines are mapped
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] contiguously to GP7–GP22. This is ideal for RP2040 PIO (Programmable I/O) state machines to
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] handle the bus timing efficiently.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Upper Address Lines (A16-A23): There are no direct GPIOs assigned to GBA pins 22–29
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] (A16–A23).
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro]     *   The presence of GP2 (SHIFTCLK), GP3 (SHIFTSHLD), and GP4
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] (SHIFTQ7) strongly implies a 74HC165 PISO (Parallel-In Serial-Out) shift register
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] is used.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro]     *   The GBA drives A16–A23 into the shift register, and the RP2040 reads the address serially
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] via GP4.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Control Signals: All critical control lines (/CS, /RD, /WR, PHI, /CS2) are mapped
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] directly.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] Combined Pin Mapping
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the correlation between the provided CSV pinout and the RP2040 GPIO list:
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] ╭──────────────────┬───────────┬──────────────────┬──────────────────────────────────────╮
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  Signal Name     │  GBA Pin  │  RP2040 GPIO     │  Function                            │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] ├──────────────────┼───────────┼──────────────────┼──────────────────────────────────────┤
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  :---            │  :---     │  :---            │  :---                                │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **VCC**         │  1, 32    │  N/A             │  3.3V Power                          │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **PHI**         │  2        │  **GP28**        │  System Clock (~16.78MHz)            │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **/WR**         │  3        │  **GP27**        │  Write Strobe                        │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **/RD**         │  4        │  **GP26**        │  Read Strobe                         │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **/CS**         │  5        │  **GP5**         │  ROM Chip Select                     │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **AD0 – AD15**  │  6 – 21   │  **GP7 – GP22**  │  Multiplexed Address/Data            │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **A16 – A23**   │  22 – 29  │  *Indirect*      │  Via Shift Register (GP2, GP3, GP4)  │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **/CS2**        │  30       │  **GP6**         │  SRAM/Save Chip Select               │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] │  **GND**         │  31       │  N/A             │  Ground                              │
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] ╰──────────────────┴───────────┴──────────────────┴──────────────────────────────────────╯
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] Implementation Notes
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Contiguous GPIOs: GP7 through GP22 form a perfect 16-bit block. In C/C++ SDK, this allows
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] a single `gpiogetall()` masked operation or a `in` instruction in PIO to capture the entire
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] bus instantly.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Shift Register Timing: Since the GBA access time is fast, the PIO code will likely need
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] to trigger the `SHIFTSHLD` immediately upon detecting a valid address setup to capture
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] A16-A23 before the GBA bus cycle completes.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] • UART: GP0/GP1 are reserved for debugging, which is standard practice.
2025-12-02 08:47:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:50:00 [nitro@ryzen5] the pcb is thinner for a gba cart?
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the PCB for a Game Boy Advance cartridge is thinner than the standard FR4 thickness found in
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] most electronics.
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] • GBA Cartridge PCB Thickness: Approximately 0.8mm.
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] • Standard PCB Thickness: 1.6mm.
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] If you are designing a board to insert directly into a GBA console slot, you must specify
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] 0.8mm thickness when ordering from your PCB fabricator. Attempting to force a standard
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] 1.6mm board into the slot will damage the console's contact pins.
2025-12-02 08:50:16 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:52:37 [nitro@ryzen5] muffin toast and crumpet should have pvb on their bom with correct dimensions
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, GBA cartridge PCBs are thinner than the standard 1.6mm used in most electronics.
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] For Project Waffle (and the associated boards "muffin", "toast", and "crumpet"), you should specify
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] a PCB thickness of 0.8mm in your fabrication notes or BOM.
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] Using a standard 1.6mm PCB will likely prevent the board from fitting into the plastic cartridge
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] shell and could permanently damage the pins inside the Game Boy Advance cartridge slot.
2025-12-02 08:52:47 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:53:47 [nitro@ryzen5] what is standard with and height for gba cart pcb?
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the PCB for a Game Boy Advance cartridge is significantly thinner than the standard 1.6mm used
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] in most electronics. Using a standard thickness board will damage the pins in the GBA cartridge
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] slot.
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the standard dimensions for a GBA cartridge PCB:
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Thickness*
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • 0.8 mm (Critical)
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Note: Standard FR4 is usually 1.6mm. You must specify 0.8mm to your fabrication house.
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Dimensions (Approximate)*
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Width: 54.5 mm (fits inside the standard shell)
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Height: 34.5 mm (standard ROM cart size)
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Notches: There are specific cutouts required on the sides to fit the plastic posts inside
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] the cartridge shell.
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] • Fabrication Recommendations*
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Edge Connector: Hard Gold plating (ENIG is acceptable for prototypes, but wears out
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] faster).
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Edge Beveling (Chamfer): Highly recommended (usually 30° or 45°) to ensure the 0.8mm
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] board slides into the connector smoothly without catching pins.
2025-12-02 08:54:09 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:55:49 [gemini-3-pro] Yes, the PCB for a Game Boy Advance cartridge is significantly thinner than standard PCBs to
2025-12-02 08:55:49 [gemini-3-pro] accommodate the shell form factor and the sprung pins in the console slot.
2025-12-02 08:55:49 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 08:55:49 [gemini-3-pro] A standard PCB is 1.6mm. A GBA PCB must be 0.8mm.
