2025-12-02 12:41:42 [gemini-3-pro] KiCad (and most modern CAD tools) typically uses STEP AP214 protocols for colors. It does
2025-12-02 12:41:42 [gemini-3-pro] not use a fixed palette like CGA; instead, it defines specific RGB values (usually 0.0 to 1.0
2025-12-02 12:41:42 [gemini-3-pro] floats) linked to geometry via a chain of entity references starting with `STYLED_ITEM`.
