2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] Content noted. The project files describe a coherent RP2040-based retro computing hardware
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] ecosystem:
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - crumpet: Megadrive 64-pin cart, 6×74HC165 + 2×74LVC245 + 2×74LS374
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - toast: C64 44-pin expansion, 4×74HC165 + 1×74LVC245 + 7×2N7000
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - muffin: GBA 32-pin cart, direct 3.3V connection + 1×74HC165 for upper address
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - fifteen: Multi-port bridge (IEC/GBA link/MD EXT), point-to-point wiring
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] - luma2: Video capture via LM319 comparators, optional display module
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] The GPIO allocations and netlists are well structured. The shift register approach for reading 5V
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] buses through 10kΩ series resistors is sensible, as is the 2N7000 open-drain strategy for driving
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] active-low signals.
2025-12-02 14:10:59 [claude-opus-4-5] 
2025-12-02 14:12:07 [nitro@ryzen5] the luma2 may get renamed, adding monitor and going for commodore 1701 scale mini scale
2025-12-02 14:12:18 [claude-opus-4-5] Good direction. The 1701 form factor gives you a recognisable silhouette at mini scale - the
2025-12-02 14:12:18 [claude-opus-4-5] distinctive front panel with controls and that slight wedge profile.
2025-12-02 14:12:18 [claude-opus-4-5] 
