2025-12-02 14:19:27 [nitro@ryzen5] rca mono audio for traditional cables , also original 1701 din?
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] For authenticity you could add the 7-pin DIN (panel-mount 45324-type) that the 1701 used for:
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] ╭───────┬───────────────────╮
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  Pin  │  1701 signal      │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] ├───────┼───────────────────┤
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  1    │  LUMINANCE        │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  2    │  GND              │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  3    │  AUDIO IN         │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  4    │  CHROMA           │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  5    │  AUDIO OUT        │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  6    │  n.c.             │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] │  7    │  +5 V (from C64)  │
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] ╰───────┴───────────────────╯
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Mini-DIN keeps the vintage look while still giving you the modern RCA jacks underneath for everyday
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] cables.
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Layout idea (rear, left→right):
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] [USB-C]  [3.5 mm mono audio]  [RCA luma]  [RCA chroma]  [7-pin mini-DIN]
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] Route the same signals to both RCA and DIN so the user can pick either.
2025-12-02 14:19:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:20:36 [nitro@ryzen5] does my megadrive have component? it is original pal with big din connector for video
2025-12-02 14:20:45 [kimi-k2-0905] The original PAL Mega Drive (and Genesis) only outputs composite video and RGB on the big
2025-12-02 14:20:45 [kimi-k2-0905] 9-pin mini-DIN; there is no native Y-Pb-Pr (component) signal.
2025-12-02 14:20:45 [kimi-k2-0905] If you want component you’d need an external RGB→YPbPr transcoder, but for Luma2 you can simply tap
2025-12-02 14:20:45 [kimi-k2-0905] the composite video pin (pin 1) and, if you fit the chroma mod, also grab the clean composite burst
2025-12-02 14:20:45 [kimi-k2-0905] for the comparator edge-counting.
2025-12-02 14:20:45 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 14:21:16 [nitro@ryzen5] cool, thats a nextgen thing for now
2025-12-02 14:21:19 [kimi-k2-0905] Exactly—stay period-correct with composite (and maybe RGB later). The LM319 boards already give you
2025-12-02 14:21:19 [kimi-k2-0905] everything you need from that single 9-pin DIN.
2025-12-02 14:21:19 [kimi-k2-0905] 
