2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Here is a review of the two Luma2 SKUs.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Verdict: The µ1701-2 (2-inch) is the winner.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] • Reasoning:*
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  GPIO Compatibility: The 2.8" Touch version is technically incompatible with your
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] current netlist without major rewiring. The Waveshare 2.8" shield hardwires the LCD control and
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Touch interface to GP16 through GP22. These are the exact pins you have allocated for the
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Luma2 capture logic (Chroma and Grey levels).
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Aesthetics: The 2" screen has a higher pixel density. For a "Mini Commodore 1701"
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] replica, the smaller screen looks more like a sharp CRT monitor relative to the bezel size. The 4
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] physical buttons on the 2" unit are also perfect for adjusting contrast/brightness without needing
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] a touch driver.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Technical Analysis
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Option A: µ1701-2 (2-inch) - RECOMMENDED
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] This "Hat" fits your GPIO allocation perfectly, provided you use the default Waveshare button
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] mappings (which differ slightly from your text list, but fit the holes in your logic).
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] • LCD SPI: GP8, GP9, GP10, GP11, GP12, GP13 (Matches your allocation).
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] • Physical Buttons: GP2, GP3, GP15, GP17 (Standard Waveshare 2" pinout).
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] • Conflict Check:
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro]     *   GP14 (CSYNC) is FREE.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro]     *   GP16 (Chroma) is FREE.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro]     *   GP18-22 (Grey Levels) are FREE.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] • Form Factor: 40mm width allows for a compact "Monitor" casing with the trimmers mounted
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] on the base PCB below the screen ("Chin" of the monitor).
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Option B: µ1701-2.8 (2.8-inch Touch) - NOT RECOMMENDED
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] • Conflict: Uses GP16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21, 22 for SPI and Touch.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] • Result: You would lose your Chroma input and all Grey level inputs. You would have to
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] bit-bang SPI on lower pins or cut traces on the LCD PCB.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Revised GPIO Map (Optimized for µ1701-2)
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] This map aligns the Luma2 capture logic with the fixed hardware pins of the Waveshare 2" LCD Hat.
