2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Design Note: The "Monitor" Look
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] To achieve the "Pots at front, connectors at back" layout with the 2" Hat:
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  PCB Layout: The main Luma2 PCB should be longer than the Pico.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Mounting:
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Rear: RCA and Power jacks.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Middle: Socket for the Pico.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Front: The 5 Piher trimpots arranged in a row (Brightness, Contrast, Saturation,
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] etc.).
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  The Stack: The Pico plugs into the Luma2 PCB. The LCD Hat plugs into the top of the
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] Pico.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 4.  Case: The 3D print can bezel the screen and the buttons, leaving the trimpots
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] accessible on the "shelf" below the screen, mimicking the control door of a 1701.
2025-12-02 15:31:01 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:33:24 [nitro@ryzen5] ribbon to 5 trimpot assembly header
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the review of the Luma2 display options and the trimpot assembly integration.
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] SKU Decision: Go with the 2-inch (µ1701-2)
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Critical Conflict Found: The 2.8" Touch version is incompatible* with your
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] current GPIO allocation.
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • The 2.8" Waveshare module hardwires LCDDC, LCDCS, and LCD_CLK to GP16, GP17,
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] GP18.
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Project Luma2 requires GP16, GP18, GP19, GP20 for high-speed parallel video
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] capture (Chroma/Luma).
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Verdict: Use the 2-inch version. It uses GP8-GP13, leaving the high-speed capture
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] pins (GP14-GP22) free for the LM319 comparators. Plus, the 4 physical buttons on the 2" unit are
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] perfect for a monitor OSD (Menu, Up, Down, Select).
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] Trimpot Daughterboard (Ribbon Cable)
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] To mount the controls on the front of the "Mini 1701" case while keeping the PCB fast and tidy,
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] move the 5 trimpots to a separate PCB connected via a ribbon cable.
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Ribbon Specification:*
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Wires Required: 7 (1x 5V, 1x GND, 5x Wiper Returns).
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Connector: 8-pin IDC (2x4) or JST-XH 8-pin.
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] • Pot Function: These adjust the reference voltage for the LM319 comparators.
2025-12-02 15:33:59 [gemini-3-pro] 
