2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the conflict analysis based on the provided dimensions and component specifications.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Project Fifteen (1541 Scale Model)
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Conflict: Physical Connector vs. Case Dimensions*
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] You specified a target case size of 32mm (W) x 15mm (H) x 80mm (D) to house 2x DIN
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 45322 sockets.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Height Issue: A standard panel-mount DIN 45322 socket requires a mounting hole of roughly
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 16mm to 19mm diameter (depending on the specific manufacturer/locking ring). The flange is
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] usually 20mm+.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro]        Result:* The socket is taller than the entire case (15mm).
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Width Issue: Two DIN sockets side-by-side require approximately 40mm to 45mm
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] width (including minimal spacing between flanges).
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro]        Result:* Two sockets will not fit on the 32mm faceplate.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Depth Issue: A standard DIN socket extends ~25-30mm into the case. With a Pico (51mm
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] long) inside an 80mm deep case, you have length available, but the height/width is the blocker.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Recommendations:*
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Mini-DIN: Switch to Mini-DIN-6 connectors (PS/2 style). These are ~10mm diameter and
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] would fit the 15mm height constraint.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Pigtails: Do not mount sockets on the chassis. Pass a cable through a strain relief
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] gland.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Scale Adjustment: To fit full-size DINs, the case needs to be approx 45mm (W) x
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 22mm (H) minimum.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Project LUMA2 (1701 Scale Monitor)
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Conflict: PCB Width vs. Case Walls*
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] You specified a case width of 57.4mm for the 2:13 scale 1701.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Component: The Waveshare Pico LCD 2 (2-inch IPS) PCB dimensions are typically
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 56.0mm wide (screen active area is smaller, but the PCB overhangs).
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Calculation: 57.4mm (Case) - 56.0mm (PCB) = 1.4mm total clearance.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Result: This leaves 0.7mm for wall thickness on each side.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro]        Risk:* This is too thin for standard FDM 3D printing (usually requires 1.2mm -
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 1.6mm). It might work for Resin printing, but structure will be brittle.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] • Recommendations:*
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  Bezel Design: Design the front bezel to snap over the internal frame, allowing
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] the structural walls to be behind the screen edge.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  Scale Adjustment: Increase width to 60mm to allow for 2mm walls.
2025-12-02 17:35:02 [gemini-3-pro] 
