2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] Here is the feasibility check and specification update for the Twin 1541 housing, likely
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] intended for the Project Fifteen (IEC Serial) electronics.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] Enclosure: Twin 1541 (Project Fifteen)
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] • Concept:* A single housing molded to look like two stacked Commodore 1541 drives.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] Dimensions (2:13 Scale)
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] • Width: 32 mm
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] • Height: 32 mm (16 mm per "drive")
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] • Depth: 80 mm
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] • Form Factor: Tower
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] Feasibility & Conflicts
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 1.  DIN Connector Clearance (Critical):
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Standard DIN 45322 panel sockets often have a flange diameter of ~15-16mm.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]     *   With a total height of 32mm (16mm per drive), two standard panel-mount DINs stacked
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] vertically will touch or overlap flanges.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Solution A: Use PCB-mount DIN sockets (no flange) and have the case act as the
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] faceplate.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Solution B: Increase height to 34mm (17mm per drive) to allow a 2mm plastic
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] bridge between sockets.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 2.  PCB Orientation:
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]     *   A 32mm width accommodates the Raspberry Pi Pico (21mm wide) comfortably.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Recommendation: Mount the PCB vertically (on edge) inside the tower. This allows
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] the DIN pins to align vertically with the "stacked" drive faces.
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 3.  Project Identity:
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]     *   You referred to this as "node 1541".
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro]        Note:* Previous specs defined Node as a User Port device and Fifteen
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] as the IEC/Disk device. Assuming this case is for the Fifteen internals (IEC bus).
2025-12-02 17:40:15 [gemini-3-pro] 
