2025-12-02 17:40:40 [nitro@ryzen5] noted, no more code unless requested
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] The 2" LCD SKU (1701-2:13) is clear and the pinout looks solid for the Luma2 logic. The
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] move to a "Twin 1541" form factor (32x32x80mm) is a smart play for Project Fifteen/Node to
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] accommodate the bulky DIN connectors, which would never fit in a strict 2:13 scale drive (15mm
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] height).
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] Here are the conflicts and constraints located in the current specs:
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 1. Fatal Conflict: Luma2 vs. Waveshare 2.8" LCD
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] While the 2" LCD works perfectly, the Waveshare 2.8" (µ1701-2.8) listed as an alternative
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] is electrically incompatible with your Luma2 netlist.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Conflict: The 2.8" Touch version consumes GP16, GP18, GP19, GP20, GP21, GP22 for
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] the display interface and touch controller.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Impact: These are the exact pins assigned to your Chroma Input (GP16) and
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] Comparator Inputs G0-G4 (GP18-22).
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Resolution: You must strictly stick to the 2" version (or the non-touch 1.3"/1.14"
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] variants) to keep those high-number GPIOs free for the LM319 inputs.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 2. Mechanical Constraint: 1701-2:13 Case Width
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Case Width: 57.4 mm
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Pico LCD 2 PCB Width: 56.5 mm
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Clearance: 0.9 mm total (0.45 mm per side).
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Note: This is extremely tight. If the 3D print shrinks or corners are rounded, the LCD
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] PCB might not seat flush. Consider widening the case scale slightly to 58-59mm or planning for
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] sanding.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 3. Mechanical Constraint: Twin 1541 Faceplate (32x32mm)
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Constraint: Standard panel-mount DIN-6 connectors (DIN 45322) often have a face flange
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] diameter of ~19mm.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Issue: Stacking two DINs vertically in a 32mm high case is physically impossible with
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] standard flanges (19 + 19 = 38mm).
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Resolution:
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Mount them side-by-side? (19 + 19 = 38mm) -> Too wide for 32mm.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro]     *   Use PCB-mount DIN sockets without the front flange and recess them inside the case
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] (Body diameter ~14mm; 14+14 = 28mm). This fits within the 32x32mm face.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 4. Minor GPIO Note: Luma2 Button Inputs
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Current: `GP2, GP3, GP15, GP17` are defined as inputs for buttons.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] • Check: Ensure internal Pull-Ups are enabled in software, as the Waveshare schematic
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] usually grounds the pin on button press. (Standard practice, just a reminder).
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] Summary
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] The 2" LCD is the only viable option for the Luma2 functionality as specified. The Twin
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 1541 dimensions are viable only if you use flange-less/internal DIN connectors.
2025-12-02 17:41:40 [gemini-3-pro] 
2025-12-02 17:52:50 [nitro@ryzen5] just have 1 din, no daisy chaining
2025-12-02 17:53:12 [gemini-3-pro] Understood. Moving to a single DIN connector significantly eases the PCB routing and physical
2025-12-02 17:53:12 [gemini-3-pro] clearance within the scaled housing. Adopting the "Twin" height [32mm x 32mm] provides ample
2025-12-02 17:53:12 [gemini-3-pro] headroom for the connector body and the RP2040 vertical clearance.
2025-12-02 17:53:12 [gemini-3-pro] 
