2025-12-02 20:09:16 [nitro@ryzen5] the header24 expansion on the vic:6 what can we add to complete it?
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] Based on the VIC-20's 24-pin expansion port (standard pinout: A0-A13, D0-D7, /RESET, /IRQ, /NMI,
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] /BLK1-5, +5V, GND, etc.), to complete the header24 expansion for VIC:6, consider adding:
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] 
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] - Shift Registers: 3x 74HC165 for parallel bus reads (address/data/controls), similar to
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] Toast/Crumpet.
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] - Buffers: 1x 74LVC245 for 8-bit data writes to VIC-20.
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] - Open Drain Drivers: 4x 2N7000 FETs for active-low signals like /RESET, /IRQ, /NMI.
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] - Series Resistors: 10kΩ on all 5V inputs for protection.
2025-12-02 20:09:21 [grok-code-1] - Decoupling Caps: 100nF per IC.
