2025-12-02 20:50:38 [nitro@ryzen5] hi claude, can you give joy.md the once over please
2025-12-02 20:51:32 [nitro@ryzen5] hi kimi, your thoughts on the joy.md designs
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] Looking at joy.md - this is a solid multi-joystick design with clever use of 74LS374 latches
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] driving 2N7000 FETs for open-drain outputs. The 40-bit shift chain for inputs and 24-bit latch
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] array for outputs should handle Atari/Commodore/Sega protocols well.
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] A few observations:
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] - The Sega 6-button mapping looks correct (pins 1-4 + 6 for XYZ/ABC)
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] - Analog multiplexing with CD4051s is efficient for paddles
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] - The shared 8-bit data bus for latches reduces GPIO count nicely
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] - Consider adding 100nF caps on each 74LS374 for decoupling
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] - The Apple II DIP-16 connector is a nice touch for full compatibility
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] The PIO strategies look sound - parallel load then shift for inputs, and sequential latch pulses
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] for outputs. Should work well for real-time joystick polling.
2025-12-02 20:51:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:53:02 [nitro@ryzen5] space on pcb?
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] The PCB dimensions in joy.md show 60 × 30 mm (1:6 scale breadbin).
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] With two DB-9s edge-mounted on the 60 mm side you already consume ~30 mm width, leaving ~25 mm
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] clear between them.
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] Quick component tally:
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - 5 × 16-pin DIP (74HC165 + 74LS374) ≈ 5 × 8 mm = 40 mm if stacked end-to-end
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - 2 × 16-pin SOIC/CD4051 ≈ 6 mm
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - 24 × SOT-23 2N7000 ≈ 12 mm × 6 mm cluster
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] - passives 0603 negligible
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] All parts fit comfortably on a single 2-layer board if you:
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Place the shift/latch chips across the 30 mm depth, perpendicular to the DB-9s.
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. Put the 2N7000 array as a tight grid between the jacks.
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Route the shared 8-bit bus on the back side—no need for extra layers.
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] You still have room along the 30 mm edge for the 24-pin header24 expansion strip (2 × 12 pins on
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 0.1″ centres = 30.48 mm, exactly the board width).
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] No size changes required; everything packs in with a few mm to spare.
2025-12-02 20:53:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
