2025-12-02 20:56:52 [nitro@ryzen5] can we use 4051 for sampling microphne l and r
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Using the CD4051 analog multiplexer for stereo microphone sampling is possible, but
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] with caveats:
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] ⚠️ Limitations of CD4051 for Audio
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 1. Bandwidth: CD4051 is audio-capable but only ~40 kHz @ 5 V (less at 3.3
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] V).
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Acceptable for voice or low-fidelity sampling (8–16 kHz).
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Not hi-fi—roll-off above 5–7 kHz.
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 2. On-resistance: ~120 Ω typical (5 V).
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Forms a low-pass filter with ADC input capacitance (≈ 12 pF).
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Fc ≈ 110 kHz—fine for 48 kHz sampling, but SNR degrades.
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 3. Crosstalk: –50 dB @ 1 kHz between channels.
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]    - Audible L/R bleed if gain is high.
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] ✅ Minimal Circuit (if acceptable quality)
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Left MIC  → 2.2k bias → 100nF → CD4051 I/O 0
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Right MIC → 2.2k bias → 100nF → CD4051 I/O 1
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Select lines GP6–GP8 (shared with pots)
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] COM out → GP26 (ADC0) already wired
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] Sample rate: **16 kHz max** to avoid MUX switching artifacts
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 🔧 Better Option (still tiny)
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] - Dual SPDT analog switch (e.g., 74LVC2G53) instead of 4051:
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]   - 0.5 Ω on-resistance, >100 MHz bandwidth
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]   - Still fits SOT-363, same PCB space as one 4051
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905]   - Use one GPIO for L/R select, feed single ADC
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] ━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] ✅ Bottom Line
2025-12-02 20:57:23 [kimi-k2-0905] - CD4051 works for voice/intercom quality inside the existing footprint.
