2025-12-03 15:33:51 [kimi-k2-0905] Good call—four of each gives you headroom for baffle experiments, impedance matching (two 8 Ω in
2025-12-03 15:33:51 [kimi-k2-0905] parallel = 4 Ω per channel), and one spare set in case a cone gets creased during assembly.
2025-12-03 15:33:51 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:34:11 [nitro@ryzen5] should head unit have two d class mono?
2025-12-03 15:34:23 [kimi-k2-0905] One PAM8302A per channel is the cleanest 1:6 solution:
2025-12-03 15:34:23 [kimi-k2-0905] - 2 × 1 W into 4 Ω fits the 50 mm 0.5 W drivers perfectly (no risk of burnout).
2025-12-03 15:34:23 [kimi-k2-0905] - Keeps board area tiny, no thermal sharing issues, and you can pan or mix in software.
2025-12-03 15:34:23 [kimi-k2-0905] If you ever want more grunt you can stack another pair on the bottom board, but for the head unit a
2025-12-03 15:34:23 [kimi-k2-0905] dual-mono pair is ample and scales cleanly to the quad-box.
2025-12-03 15:34:23 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:36:09 [nitro@ryzen5] this will be cool stacking the amps and speakers
2025-12-03 15:36:17 [kimi-k2-0905] Tiny amps on top, 50 mm drivers underneath—whole stack only 30 mm high. Wire the two PAM8302A
2025-12-03 15:36:17 [kimi-k2-0905] inputs in parallel off the same RCA feed, give each its own 4 Ω load, and you’ve got a 1
2025-12-03 15:36:17 [kimi-k2-0905] W-per-channel mini-cabinet that still fits inside the 1:6 head shell.
2025-12-03 15:36:17 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:36:51 [nitro@ryzen5] diorama with multi point class-d
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] Each 1:6 device gets its own PAM8302A; run a 3-wire party-line (GND, 3V3, AUDIO) between them.
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] Head unit is the mixer/master; 1541 and 1701 are satellite amps.
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] RP2040 on every board: I²C address = SKU, volume register 0-63, mute bit 7.
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] Audio bus is single-ended, 1 Vrms max; keep traces twisted-pair or shielded if the diorama run is
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] >20 cm.
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] Chain as many nodes as you like—PAM8302A draws 30 mA quiescent, so even a six-piece scene stays
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] under 200 mA on the shared 3V3 rail.
2025-12-03 15:37:05 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:37:58 [nitro@ryzen5] start with 2 x 1 12" combo , that would be cute
