2025-12-03 15:40:02 [kimi-k2-0905] 1:6 scale → 17 × 11 × 2 mm (about the size of a postage stamp).
2025-12-03 15:40:02 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:41:01 [nitro@ryzen5] how big is micro sd
2025-12-03 15:41:07 [kimi-k2-0905] Micro-SD card: 15 × 11 × 1 mm.
2025-12-03 15:41:07 [kimi-k2-0905] That’s almost exactly the 1:6 cassette footprint—just 0.5 mm thinner—so you can hide a µSD inside
2025-12-03 15:41:07 [kimi-k2-0905] the shell and still have room for a tiny lid or label.
2025-12-03 15:41:07 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:43:19 [nitro@ryzen5] what was commodore cassette loader called?
2025-12-03 15:43:22 [kimi-k2-0905] Datassette — official model 1530/1531, but everyone just said “Datassette”.
2025-12-03 15:43:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:43:41 [nitro@ryzen5] 1530 1:8 size ?
2025-12-03 15:43:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 1530 Datassette real: 305 × 190 × 60 mm
2025-12-03 15:43:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 1:6 scale → 51 × 32 × 10 mm
2025-12-03 15:43:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 1:8 scale → 38 × 24 × 7.5 mm (matchbox-size).
2025-12-03 15:43:46 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 15:44:04 [nitro@ryzen5] sorry i mean 1:6, easy to typo
2025-12-03 15:44:08 [kimi-k2-0905] No worries—1:6 Datassette comes out 51 × 32 × 10 mm, same footprint as the 1541-1:6 drive
2025-12-03 15:44:08 [kimi-k2-0905] so they stack neatly on the diorama shelf.
2025-12-03 15:44:08 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 16:07:13 [nitro@ryzen5] so JST PH 3 for a neo light connector?
2025-12-03 16:07:22 [kimi-k2-0905] Yes—JST PH 3-pin (2 mm pitch) is perfect for a tiny NeoPixel chain:
2025-12-03 16:07:22 [kimi-k2-0905] pin-1 5 V, pin-2 Data, pin-3 GND.
2025-12-03 16:07:22 [kimi-k2-0905] Common on small WS2812B strips/grilles and the Pico can drive it straight off GP28 (or any spare)
2025-12-03 16:07:22 [kimi-k2-0905] with the usual 330 Ω series resistor at the header.
2025-12-03 16:07:22 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 16:12:05 [nitro@ryzen5] what standard header fits 5mm across
2025-12-03 16:12:13 [kimi-k2-0905] Pin-header on 0.1 inch (2.54 mm) pitch gives 5.08 mm between rows – close enough that a plain 2×3
2025-12-03 16:12:13 [kimi-k2-0905] (6-pin) shrouded 0.1" header is 5 mm across the outer edges and is the cheapest "standard" part
2025-12-03 16:12:13 [kimi-k2-0905] that fits.
2025-12-03 16:12:13 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 16:13:34 [nitro@ryzen5] which JST-PH would suit a microsd connector
2025-12-03 16:13:43 [kimi-k2-0905] JST PH series has no micro-SD slot; the only standard JST that mates with a micro-SD card is the
2025-12-03 16:13:43 [kimi-k2-0905] push-push socket itself (e.g. Hirose DM3 series).
2025-12-03 16:13:43 [kimi-k2-0905] If you just want a removable cable to the µSD board, solder a JST PH 4-pin to the adapter’s
2025-12-03 16:13:43 [kimi-k2-0905] VCC-D0-D1-GND and use a PH 4 plug on the harness—keeps the 2 mm pitch while giving you polarised, 2
2025-12-03 16:13:43 [kimi-k2-0905] A-rated connections.
2025-12-03 16:13:43 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 16:14:37 [nitro@ryzen5] SD card on a cable doesn't make much sense...
2025-12-03 16:14:41 [kimi-k2-0905] Exactly—µSD belongs on the PCB. Run the JST-PH 3 for the NeoPixels and put the micro-SD socket
2025-12-03 16:14:41 [kimi-k2-0905] directly on the board so there’s nothing to shake loose when the 1:6 stack gets bumped.
2025-12-03 16:14:41 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 16:15:24 [nitro@ryzen5] so 51 32 10 datasette is just another usb device with a microsd slot and some lights
2025-12-03 16:15:31 [kimi-k2-0905] Yep—51 × 32 × 10 mm shell, RP2040 USB-C, micro-SD on-board, JST-PH 3 for the grille LEDs, and a
2025-12-03 16:15:31 [kimi-k2-0905] single button that cycles tap-tempo rainbow or disk-activity flicker. Shows up as a tiny USB drive
2025-12-03 16:15:31 [kimi-k2-0905] and a HID light controller at the same time.
2025-12-03 16:15:31 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 16:16:29 [nitro@ryzen5] it could have tiny touch screen, will check waveshare
2025-12-03 16:16:37 [kimi-k2-0905] Smallest Waveshare Pico LCD is the 0.96" 160×80 IPS (ST7735, 4-wire SPI) – 25 × 14 mm active area,
2025-12-03 16:16:37 [kimi-k2-0905] overall PCB 32 × 20 mm.
2025-12-03 16:16:37 [kimi-k2-0905] That just fits the 51 × 32 mm Datassette lid; mount it behind a smoked-perspex window and you’ve
2025-12-03 16:16:37 [kimi-k2-0905] got a 1:6 tape deck that scrolls PETSCII "LOAD"* stripes while the LEDs chase.
2025-12-03 16:16:37 [kimi-k2-0905] 
2025-12-03 16:16:37 [kimi-k2-0905] • or whatever filename is on the µSD.
